    "topic": "Magnetic Fields and Lines",
    "prompt": "What is the direction of the magnetic force on a positive charge that moves as shown in each of the six cases?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>What is the direction of the magnetic force on a positive charge that moves as shown in each of the six cases?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>What is the direction of the magnetic force on a positive charge that moves as shown in each of the six cases?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Case a: B is out of the page, v is down. Case b: B is to the right, v is up. Case c: B is in, v is to the right. Case d: B is to the right, v is to the left. Case e: B is up, v is into the page. Case f: B is to the left, v is out of the page.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/de0dbdef3b90e41da9ee5e82.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171361495808",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-11#fs-id1171361495808-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. left; b. into the page; c. up the page; d. no force; e. right; f. down</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 15. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171361495808\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
