    "prompt": "Prove that using x ( t ) = A sin ( ω t + ϕ ) will produce the same results for the period for the oscillations of a mass and a spring. Why do you think the cosine function was chosen?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Prove that using <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mtext>sin</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> will produce the same results for the period for the oscillations of a mass and a spring. Why do you think the cosine function was chosen?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Prove that using <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mtext>sin</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> will produce the same results for the period for the oscillations of a mass and a spring. Why do you think the cosine function was chosen?</p>\n</div>",
