    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-3#fs-id1168326790679-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Graph shows velocity in meters per second plotted as a function of time at seconds. Velocity starts as 10 meters per second, decreases to -30 at 0.4 seconds; increases to -10 meters at 0.6 seconds, increases to 5 at 1 second, increases to 15 at 1.6 seconds.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/b24655bc9e935910ed8fb260.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
