    "number": 29,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Rotational Variables",
    "prompt": "A track star runs a 400-m race on a 400-m circular track in 45 s. What is his angular velocity assuming a constant speed?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A track star runs a 400-m race on a 400-m circular track in 45 s. What is his angular velocity assuming a constant speed?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A track star runs a 400-m race on a 400-m circular track in 45 s. What is his angular velocity assuming a constant speed?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-problems#fs-id1167134541813",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-10#fs-id1167134541813-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>ω</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mfrac>\n<mrow>\n<mn>2</mn>\n<mi>π</mi>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>rad</mtext>\n</mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mn>45.0</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>s</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mfrac>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0.14</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>rad/s</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 29. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-problems#fs-id1167134541813\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
