    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Moment of Inertia and Rotational Kinetic Energy",
    "prompt": "A diver goes into a somersault during a dive by tucking her limbs. If her rotational kinetic energy is 100 J and her moment of inertia in the tuck is 9.0 kg · m 2 , what is her…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A diver goes into a somersault during a dive by tucking her limbs. If her rotational kinetic energy is 100 J and her moment of inertia in the tuck is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>9.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, what is her rotational rate during the somersault?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A diver goes into a somersault during a dive by tucking her limbs. If her rotational kinetic energy is 100 J and her moment of inertia in the tuck is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>9.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, what is her rotational rate during the somersault?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-problems#fs-id1167132288041",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 58. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-problems#fs-id1167132288041\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
