    "number": 23,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Simple Harmonic Motion",
    "prompt": "If your heart rate is 150 beats per minute during strenuous exercise, what is the time per beat in units of seconds?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>If your heart rate is 150 beats per minute during strenuous exercise, what is the time per beat in units of seconds?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>If your heart rate is 150 beats per minute during strenuous exercise, what is the time per beat in units of seconds?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/15-problems#fs-id1167131333987",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-15#fs-id1167131333987-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>0.400 s/beat</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 15, Problem 23. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/15-problems#fs-id1167131333987\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
