    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Electric Potential Energy",
    "prompt": "To form a hydrogen atom, a proton is fixed at a point and an electron is brought from far away to a distance of 0.529 × 10 −10 m, the average distance between proton and electron in a…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>To form a hydrogen atom, a proton is fixed at a point and an electron is brought from far away to a distance of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.529</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−10</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> the average distance between proton and electron in a hydrogen atom. How much work is done?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>To form a hydrogen atom, a proton is fixed at a point and an electron is brought from far away to a distance of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.529</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−10</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> the average distance between proton and electron in a hydrogen atom. How much work is done?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167586036401",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-7#fs-id1167586036401-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>U</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>4.36</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mo>×</mo>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<msup>\n<mrow>\n<mn>10</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mn>−18</mn>\n</mrow>\n</msup>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>J</mtext>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 31. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167586036401\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
