    "volume": 2,
    "chapter": 9,
    "number": 24,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Electrical Current",
    "prompt": "A conductor carries a current that is decreasing exponentially with time. The current is modeled as I = I 0 e − t / τ , where I 0 = 3.00 A is the current at time t = 0.00 s and τ = 0.50…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A conductor carries a current that is decreasing exponentially with time. The current is modeled as <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mi>t</mi><mtext>/</mtext><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is the current at time <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is the time constant. How much charge flows through the conductor between <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A conductor carries a current that is decreasing exponentially with time. The current is modeled as <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mi>t</mi><mtext>/</mtext><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is the current at time <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is the time constant. How much charge flows through the conductor between <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170901650971",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 24. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170901650971\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
