    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Faraday’s Law",
    "prompt": "A long solenoid with n = 10 turns per centimeter has a cross-sectional area of 5.0 cm 2 and carries a current of 0.25 A. A coil with five turns encircles the solenoid. When the current…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A long solenoid with <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> turns per centimeter has a cross-sectional area of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and carries a current of 0.25 A. A coil with five turns encircles the solenoid. When the current through the solenoid is turned off, it decreases to zero in 0.050 s. What is the average emf induced in the coil?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A long solenoid with <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> turns per centimeter has a cross-sectional area of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and carries a current of 0.25 A. A coil with five turns encircles the solenoid. When the current through the solenoid is turned off, it decreases to zero in 0.050 s. What is the average emf induced in the coil?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-problems#fs-id1171241110023",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 30. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-problems#fs-id1171241110023\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
