    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Magnetic Fields and Lines",
    "prompt": "(a) A cosmic ray proton moving toward Earth at 5.00 × 10 7 m/s experiences a magnetic force of 1.70 × 10 −16 N . What is the strength of the magnetic field if there is a 45º angle…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>(a) A cosmic ray proton moving toward Earth at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> experiences a magnetic force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.70</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−16</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the strength of the magnetic field if there is a 45º angle between it and the proton’s velocity? (b) Is the value obtained in part a. consistent with the known strength of Earth’s magnetic field on its surface? Discuss.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>(a) A cosmic ray proton moving toward Earth at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> experiences a magnetic force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.70</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−16</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the strength of the magnetic field if there is a 45º angle between it and the proton’s velocity? (b) Is the value obtained in part a. consistent with the known strength of Earth’s magnetic field on its surface? Discuss.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171361255945",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 22. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171361255945\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
