    "category": "challenge-problems",
    "topic": "Work and energy",
    "prompt": "The force F ( x ) varies with position, as shown below. Find the work done by this force on a particle as it moves from x = 1.0 m to x = 5.0 m .",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The force <em>F</em>(<em>x</em>) varies with position, as shown below. Find the work done by this force on a particle as it moves from <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The force <em>F</em>(<em>x</em>) varies with position, as shown below. Find the work done by this force on a particle as it moves from <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"This graph shows the function F(x) in Newtons as a function of x in meters. F(x) is constant at 1.0 N from x = 0 to x=1.0 m. It rises linearly to 5.0 N at x = 2.0 m then decreases linearly to 1.0 N at x = 4.0 m where it then drops instantly to 0 Newtons. F(x) then decreases linearly from 0 N at 4.0 m to -4.0 N at x=6.0 m.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/e0c00d43e58c0808dcbdc50e.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-challenge-problems#fs-id1165038293237",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-7#fs-id1165038293237-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>8.0 J</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 101. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-challenge-problems#fs-id1165038293237\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
