    "topic": "Equipotential Surfaces and Conductors",
    "prompt": "A long cylinder of aluminum of radius R meters is charged so that it has a uniform charge per unit length on its surface of λ . (a) Find the electric field inside and outside the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A long cylinder of aluminum of radius <em>R</em> meters is charged so that it has a uniform charge per unit length on its surface of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A long cylinder of aluminum of radius <em>R</em> meters is charged so that it has a uniform charge per unit length on its surface of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>\n<p>(a) Find the electric field inside and outside the cylinder. (b) Find the electric potential inside and outside the cylinder. (c) Plot electric field and electric potential as a function of distance from the center of the rod.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167586176637",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 62. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167586176637\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
