    "category": "challenge-problems",
    "topic": "Current and resistance",
    "prompt": "The current through a 12-gauge wire is given as I ( t ) = ( 5.00 A ) sin ( 2 π 60 Hz t ) . What is the current density at time 15.00 ms?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The current through a 12-gauge wire is given as <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>5.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>sin</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mn>60</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Hz</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the current density at time 15.00 ms?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The current through a 12-gauge wire is given as <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>5.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>sin</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mn>60</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Hz</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the current density at time 15.00 ms?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-challenge-problems#fs-id1170902924994",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 82. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-challenge-problems#fs-id1170902924994\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
