    "imported": true,
    "source": "OpenStax",
    "volume": 2,
    "chapter": 11,
    "number": 103,
    "category": "challenge-problems",
    "topic": "Magnetic forces",
    "prompt": "A proton of speed v = 6 × 10 5 m/s enters a region of uniform magnetic field of B = 0.5 T at an angle of q = 30 ° to the magnetic field. In the region of magnetic field proton describes…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A proton of speed <em>v</em> = <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> enters a region of uniform magnetic field of <em>B</em> = 0.5 T at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> to the magnetic field. In the region of magnetic field proton describes a helical path with radius <em>R</em> and pitch <em>p</em> (distance between loops). Find <em>R</em> and <em>p</em>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A proton of speed <em>v</em> = <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> enters a region of uniform magnetic field of <em>B</em> = 0.5 T at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> to the magnetic field. In the region of magnetic field proton describes a helical path with radius <em>R</em> and pitch <em>p</em> (distance between loops). Find <em>R</em> and <em>p</em>.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-challenge-problems#fs-id1171361646329",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-11#fs-id1171361646329-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>R</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mi>m</mi>\n<mi>v</mi>\n<mspace width=\"0.1em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>sin</mtext>\n<mspace width=\"0.1em\"></mspace>\n<mi>θ</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n<mtext>/</mtext>\n<mi>q</mi>\n<mi>B</mi>\n<mo>;</mo>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>p</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>(</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mrow>\n<mn>2</mn>\n<mi>π</mi>\n<mi>m</mi>\n</mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>e</mi>\n<mi>B</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n<mo>)</mo>\n</mrow>\n<mi>v</mi>\n<mtext>cos</mtext>\n<mspace width=\"0.1em\"></mspace>\n<mi>θ</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 103. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-challenge-problems#fs-id1171361646329\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
