    "number": 27,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Position, Displacement, and Average Velocity",
    "prompt": "The position of a particle moving along the x -axis is given by x ( t ) = 4.0 − 2.0 t m. (a) At what time does the particle cross the origin? (b) What is the displacement of the particle…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The position of a particle moving along the <em>x</em>-axis is given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> m. (a) At what time does the particle cross the origin? (b) What is the displacement of the particle between <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>t</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>3.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>t</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The position of a particle moving along the <em>x</em>-axis is given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> m. (a) At what time does the particle cross the origin? (b) What is the displacement of the particle between <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>t</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>3.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>t</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168326940079",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-3#fs-id1168326940079-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> s; b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3.0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>−8.0</mn><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>−2.0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>−6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 3, Problem 27. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168326940079\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
