    "topic": "Forces",
    "prompt": "Two teenagers are pulling on ropes attached to a tree. The angle between the ropes is 30.0 ° . David pulls with a force of 400.0 N and Stephanie pulls with a force of 300.0 N. (a) Find…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Two teenagers are pulling on ropes attached to a tree. The angle between the ropes is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30.0</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. David pulls with a force of 400.0 N and Stephanie pulls with a force of 300.0 N. (a) Find the component form of the net force. (b) Find the magnitude of the resultant (net) force on the tree and the angle it makes with David’s rope.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Two teenagers are pulling on ropes attached to a tree. The angle between the ropes is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30.0</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. David pulls with a force of 400.0 N and Stephanie pulls with a force of 300.0 N. (a) Find the component form of the net force. (b) Find the magnitude of the resultant (net) force on the tree and the angle it makes with David’s rope.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-problems#fs-id1165039443644",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1165039443644-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mrow><mtext>net</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>660.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>150.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mtext>net</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>676.6</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12.8</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> from David’s rope</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 21. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-problems#fs-id1165039443644\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
