    "prompt": "A 2.5-g copper penny is given a charge of 4.0 × 10 −9 C . (a) How many electrons are removed from the penny? (b) If no more than one electron is removed from an atom, what percent of the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A 2.5-g copper penny is given a charge of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−9</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (a) How many electrons are removed from the penny? (b) If no more than one electron is removed from an atom, what percent of the atoms are ionized by this charging process?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A 2.5-g copper penny is given a charge of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−9</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (a) How many electrons are removed from the penny? (b) If no more than one electron is removed from an atom, what percent of the atoms are ionized by this charging process?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172102113431",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 42. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172102113431\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
