    "previewHTML": "<p>The current through a conductor is modeled as <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>sin</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>60</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Hz</mtext></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Write an equation for the charge as a function of time.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The current through a conductor is modeled as <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>sin</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>60</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Hz</mtext></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Write an equation for the charge as a function of time.</p>\n</div>",
