    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Magnetic Fields and Lines",
    "prompt": "(a) A physicist performing a sensitive measurement wants to limit the magnetic force on a moving charge in her equipment to less than 1.00 × 10 −12 N . What is the greatest the charge…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>(a) A physicist performing a sensitive measurement wants to limit the magnetic force on a moving charge in her equipment to less than <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−12</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the greatest the charge can be if it moves at a maximum speed of 30.0 m/s in Earth’s field? (b) Discuss whether it would be difficult to limit the charge to less than the value found in (a) by comparing it with typical static electricity and noting that static is often absent.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>(a) A physicist performing a sensitive measurement wants to limit the magnetic force on a moving charge in her equipment to less than <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−12</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the greatest the charge can be if it moves at a maximum speed of 30.0 m/s in Earth’s field? (b) Discuss whether it would be difficult to limit the charge to less than the value found in (a) by comparing it with typical static electricity and noting that static is often absent.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171361650166",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 24. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171361650166\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
