    "category": "challenge-problems",
    "topic": "Electric potential",
    "prompt": "Three Na + and three Cl − ions are placed alternately and equally spaced around a circle of radius 50 nm. Find the electrostatic energy stored.",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Three <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mtext>Na</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and three <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mtext>Cl</mtext></mrow><mtext>−</mtext></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> ions are placed alternately and equally spaced around a circle of radius 50 nm. Find the electrostatic energy stored.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Three <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mtext>Na</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and three <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mtext>Cl</mtext></mrow><mtext>−</mtext></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> ions are placed alternately and equally spaced around a circle of radius 50 nm. Find the electrostatic energy stored.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-challenge-problems#fs-id1167586277929",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 106. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-challenge-problems#fs-id1167586277929\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
