    "topic": "Electromagnetic induction",
    "prompt": "A copper wire of length L is fashioned into a circular coil with N turns. When the magnetic field through the coil changes with time, for what value of N is the induced emf a maximum?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A copper wire of length <em>L</em> is fashioned into a circular coil with <em>N</em> turns. When the magnetic field through the coil changes with time, for what value of <em>N</em> is the induced emf a maximum?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A copper wire of length <em>L</em> is fashioned into a circular coil with <em>N</em> turns. When the magnetic field through the coil changes with time, for what value of <em>N</em> is the induced emf a maximum?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-challenge-problems#fs-id1171242074016",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-13#fs-id1171242074016-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p><em>N</em> = 1</p>\n</div>",
