    "topic": "Newton's Second Law",
    "prompt": "In Figure 5.12 , the net external force on the 24-kg mower is given as 51 N. If the force of friction opposing the motion is 24 N, what force F (in newtons) is the person exerting on the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>In <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-3-newtons-second-law\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Figure 5.12</a>, the net external force on the 24-kg mower is given as 51 N. If the force of friction opposing the motion is 24 N, what force <em>F</em> (in newtons) is the person exerting on the mower? Suppose the mower is moving at 1.5 m/s when the force <em>F</em> is removed. How far will the mower go before stopping?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>In <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-3-newtons-second-law\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Figure 5.12</a>, the net external force on the 24-kg mower is given as 51 N. If the force of friction opposing the motion is 24 N, what force <em>F</em> (in newtons) is the person exerting on the mower? Suppose the mower is moving at 1.5 m/s when the force <em>F</em> is removed. How far will the mower go before stopping?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-problems#fs-id1165039125323",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 28. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-problems#fs-id1165039125323\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
