    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Magnetic Fields and Lines",
    "prompt": "An electron moving at 4.00 × 10 3 m/s in a 1.25-T magnetic field experiences a magnetic force of 1.40 × 10 −16 N . What angle does the velocity of the electron make with the magnetic…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>An electron moving at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in a 1.25-T magnetic field experiences a magnetic force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.40</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−16</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What angle does the velocity of the electron make with the magnetic field? There are two answers.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>An electron moving at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in a 1.25-T magnetic field experiences a magnetic force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.40</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−16</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What angle does the velocity of the electron make with the magnetic field? There are two answers.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171358224079",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-11#fs-id1171358224079-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mn>10.1</mn>\n<mtext>°</mtext>\n<mo>;</mo>\n<mn>169.9</mn>\n<mtext>°</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 23. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171358224079\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
