    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Energy Stored in a Capacitor",
    "prompt": "In open-heart surgery, a much smaller amount of energy will defibrillate the heart. (a) What voltage is applied to the 8.00 - μ F capacitor of a heart defibrillator that stores 40.0 J of…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>In open-heart surgery, a much smaller amount of energy will defibrillate the heart. (a) What voltage is applied to the <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>8.00</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> capacitor of a heart defibrillator that stores 40.0 J of energy? (b) Find the amount of the stored charge.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>In open-heart surgery, a much smaller amount of energy will defibrillate the heart. (a) What voltage is applied to the <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>8.00</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> capacitor of a heart defibrillator that stores 40.0 J of energy? (b) Find the amount of the stored charge.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/8-problems#fs-id1167133456316",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 8, Problem 44. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/8-problems#fs-id1167133456316\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
