    "topic": "Momentum and collisions",
    "prompt": "A ramp of mass M is at rest on a horizontal surface. A small cart of mass m is placed at the top of the ramp and released. What are the velocities of the ramp and the cart relative to…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A ramp of mass <em>M</em> is at rest on a horizontal surface. A small cart of mass <em>m</em> is placed at the top of the ramp and released.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A ramp of mass <em>M</em> is at rest on a horizontal surface. A small cart of mass <em>m</em> is placed at the top of the ramp and released.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Before release, the cart, mass m, is at the top of a structure that consists of a horizontal stretch a the bottom and a ramp that rises up and to the right to a height h. The ramp has mass M and is on wheels. After release, the cart mass m is on the horizontal part of the ramp and is moving to the left with velocity v cart. The ramp is moving to the right with velocity v ramp.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/4c3f9bc49f28cf64eff2c4d7.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n<p>What are the velocities of the ramp and the cart relative to the ground at the instant the cart leaves the ramp?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-challenge-problems#fs-id1167132426551",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 117. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-challenge-problems#fs-id1167132426551\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
