    "category": "challenge-problems",
    "topic": "Rotation",
    "prompt": "Zorch, an archenemy of Rotation Man, decides to slow Earth’s rotation to once per 28.0 h by exerting an opposing force at and parallel to the equator. Rotation Man is not immediately…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Zorch, an archenemy of Rotation Man, decides to slow Earth’s rotation to once per 28.0 h by exerting an opposing force at and parallel to the equator. Rotation Man is not immediately concerned, because he knows Zorch can only exert a force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mn>.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a little greater than a Saturn V rocket’s thrust). How long must Zorch push with this force to accomplish his goal? (This period gives Rotation Man time to devote to other villains.)</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Zorch, an archenemy of Rotation Man, decides to slow Earth’s rotation to once per 28.0 h by exerting an opposing force at and parallel to the equator. Rotation Man is not immediately concerned, because he knows Zorch can only exert a force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mn>.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a little greater than a Saturn V rocket’s thrust). How long must Zorch push with this force to accomplish his goal? (This period gives Rotation Man time to devote to other villains.)</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-challenge-problems#fs-id1167131103221",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 124. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-challenge-problems#fs-id1167131103221\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
