    "topic": "Angular momentum",
    "prompt": "A bug flying horizontally at 1.0 m/s collides and sticks to the end of a uniform stick hanging vertically. After the impact, the stick swings out to a maximum angle of 5.0 ° from the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A bug flying horizontally at 1.0 m/s collides and sticks to the end of a uniform stick hanging vertically. After the impact, the stick swings out to a maximum angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> from the vertical before rotating back. If the mass of the stick is 10 times that of the bug, calculate the length of the stick.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A bug flying horizontally at 1.0 m/s collides and sticks to the end of a uniform stick hanging vertically. After the impact, the stick swings out to a maximum angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> from the vertical before rotating back. If the mass of the stick is 10 times that of the bug, calculate the length of the stick.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-challenge-problems#fs-id1165036833826",
