    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Average and Instantaneous Acceleration",
    "prompt": "A cheetah can accelerate from rest to a speed of 30.0 m/s in 7.00 s. What is its acceleration?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A cheetah can accelerate from rest to a speed of 30.0 m/s in 7.00 s. What is its acceleration?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A cheetah can accelerate from rest to a speed of 30.0 m/s in 7.00 s. What is its acceleration?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168328303424",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-3#fs-id1168328303424-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>a</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>4.29</mn>\n<msup>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>m/s</mtext>\n</mrow>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
