    "source": "OpenStax",
    "volume": 1,
    "chapter": 5,
    "number": 29,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Newton's Second Law",
    "prompt": "The rocket sled shown below accelerates opposite to the motion at a rate of 196 m/s 2 . What force is necessary to produce this acceleration opposite to the motion? Assume that the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The rocket sled shown below accelerates opposite to the motion at a rate of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>196</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What force is necessary to produce this acceleration opposite to the motion? Assume that the rockets are off. The mass of the system is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> kg.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The rocket sled shown below accelerates opposite to the motion at a rate of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>196</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What force is necessary to produce this acceleration opposite to the motion? Assume that the rockets are off. The mass of the system is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> kg.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows a rocket sled pointing right. Frictional force f points left. Upward force N and downward force w are equal in magnitude.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/7ad2b4f5cfc8e0a4f6b3ec97.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-problems#fs-id1165039485302",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1165039485302-solution",
