    "topic": "Motion of a Charged Particle in a Magnetic Field",
    "prompt": "A cosmic-ray electron moves at 7.5 × 10 6 m/s perpendicular to Earth’s magnetic field at an altitude where the field strength is 1.0 × 10 −5 T . What is the radius of the circular path…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A cosmic-ray electron moves at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>7.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> perpendicular to Earth’s magnetic field at an altitude where the field strength is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−5</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>T</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the radius of the circular path the electron follows?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A cosmic-ray electron moves at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>7.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> perpendicular to Earth’s magnetic field at an altitude where the field strength is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−5</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>T</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the radius of the circular path the electron follows?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171360274445",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-11#fs-id1171360274445-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>4.27 m</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 25. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171360274445\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
