    "topic": "Motional Emf",
    "prompt": "An automobile with a radio antenna 1.0 m long travels at 100.0 km/h in a location where the Earth’s horizontal magnetic field is 5.5 × 10 − 5 T . What is the maximum possible emf induced…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>An automobile with a radio antenna 1.0 m long travels at 100.0 km/h in a location where the Earth’s horizontal magnetic field is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>T</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the maximum possible emf induced in the antenna due to this motion?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>An automobile with a radio antenna 1.0 m long travels at 100.0 km/h in a location where the Earth’s horizontal magnetic field is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>T</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the maximum possible emf induced in the antenna due to this motion?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-problems#fs-id1171242499034",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-13#fs-id1171242499034-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>0.0015 V</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 37. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-problems#fs-id1171242499034\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
