    "number": 31,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Impulse and Collisions",
    "prompt": "What is the momentum (as a function of time) of a 5.0-kg particle moving with a velocity v → ( t ) = ( 2.0 i ^ + 4.0 t j ^ ) m/s ? What is the net force acting on this particle?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>What is the momentum (as a function of time) of a 5.0-kg particle moving with a velocity <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mi>t</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>? What is the net force acting on this particle?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>What is the momentum (as a function of time) of a 5.0-kg particle moving with a velocity <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mi>t</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>? What is the net force acting on this particle?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-problems#fs-id1167131498070",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-9#fs-id1167131498070-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>t</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>20</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 31. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-problems#fs-id1167131498070\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
