    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Rotational Variables",
    "prompt": "The angular position of a rod varies as 20.0 t 2 radians from time t = 0 . The rod has two beads on it as shown in the following figure, one at 10 cm from the rotation axis and the other…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The angular position of a rod varies as <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20.0</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> radians from time <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. The rod has two beads on it as shown in the following figure, one at 10 cm from the rotation axis and the other at 20 cm from the rotation axis. (a) What is the instantaneous angular velocity of the rod at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (b) What is the angular acceleration of the rod? (c) What are the tangential speeds of the beads at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (d) What are the tangential accelerations of the beads at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (e) What are the centripetal accelerations of the beads at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The angular position of a rod varies as <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20.0</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> radians from time <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. The rod has two beads on it as shown in the following figure, one at 10 cm from the rotation axis and the other at 20 cm from the rotation axis. (a) What is the instantaneous angular velocity of the rod at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (b) What is the angular acceleration of the rod? (c) What are the tangential speeds of the beads at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (d) What are the tangential accelerations of the beads at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (e) What are the centripetal accelerations of the beads at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure is a drawing of a rod that rotates counterclockwise. Rod has two beads on it, one at 10 cm from the rotation axis and the other at 20 cm from the rotation axis.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/2f05901b427022b92f2e9868.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-problems#fs-id1167134539353",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 36. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-problems#fs-id1167134539353\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
