    "prompt": "Two parallel conducting plates are separated by 10.0 cm, and one of them is taken to be at zero volts. (a) What is the electric field strength between them, if the potential 8.00 cm from…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Two parallel conducting plates are separated by 10.0 cm, and one of them is taken to be at zero volts. (a) What is the electric field strength between them, if the potential 8.00 cm from the zero volt plate (and 2.00 cm from the other) is 450 V? (b) What is the voltage between the plates?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Two parallel conducting plates are separated by 10.0 cm, and one of them is taken to be at zero volts. (a) What is the electric field strength between them, if the potential 8.00 cm from the zero volt plate (and 2.00 cm from the other) is 450 V? (b) What is the voltage between the plates?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167583511101",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-7#fs-id1167583511101-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.63</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kV/m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nb. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>563</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 39. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167583511101\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
