    "topic": "Energy Stored in a Capacitor",
    "prompt": "Suppose you have a 9.00-V battery, a 2.00 - μ F capacitor, and a 7.40 - μ F capacitor. (a) Find the charge and energy stored if the capacitors are connected to the battery in series. (b)…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Suppose you have a 9.00-V battery, a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.00</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> capacitor, and a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>7.40</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> capacitor. (a) Find the charge and energy stored if the capacitors are connected to the battery in series. (b) Do the same for a parallel connection.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Suppose you have a 9.00-V battery, a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.00</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> capacitor, and a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>7.40</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> capacitor. (a) Find the charge and energy stored if the capacitors are connected to the battery in series. (b) Do the same for a parallel connection.</p>\n</div>",
