    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Simple Harmonic Motion",
    "prompt": "A type of cuckoo clock keeps time by having a mass bouncing on a spring, usually something cute like a cherub in a chair. What force constant is needed to produce a period of 0.500 s for…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A type of cuckoo clock keeps time by having a mass bouncing on a spring, usually something cute like a cherub in a chair. What force constant is needed to produce a period of 0.500 s for a 0.0150-kg mass?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A type of cuckoo clock keeps time by having a mass bouncing on a spring, usually something cute like a cherub in a chair. What force constant is needed to produce a period of 0.500 s for a 0.0150-kg mass?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/15-problems#fs-id1167131540637",
