    "topic": "Model of Conduction in Metals",
    "prompt": "A cylindrical wire has a current density from the center of the wire’s cross section as J ( r ) = C r 2 where r is in meters, J is in amps per square meter, and C = 10 3 A/m 4 . This…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A cylindrical wire has a current density from the center of the wire’s cross section as <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is in meters, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is in amps per square meter, and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mtext>A/m</mtext><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. This current density continues to the end of the wire at a radius of 1.0 mm. Calculate the current just outside of this wire.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A cylindrical wire has a current density from the center of the wire’s cross section as <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is in meters, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is in amps per square meter, and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mtext>A/m</mtext><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. This current density continues to the end of the wire at a radius of 1.0 mm. Calculate the current just outside of this wire.</p></div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170902619307",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 32. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170902619307\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
