    "topic": "Motional Emf",
    "prompt": "A coil of 1000 turns encloses an area of 25 cm 2 . It is rotated in 0.010 s from a position where its plane is perpendicular to Earth’s magnetic field to one where its plane is parallel…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A coil of 1000 turns encloses an area of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>25</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. It is rotated in 0.010 s from a position where its plane is perpendicular to Earth’s magnetic field to one where its plane is parallel to the field. If the strength of the field is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−5</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>T</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> what is the average emf induced in the coil?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A coil of 1000 turns encloses an area of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>25</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. It is rotated in 0.010 s from a position where its plane is perpendicular to Earth’s magnetic field to one where its plane is parallel to the field. If the strength of the field is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−5</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>T</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> what is the average emf induced in the coil?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-problems#fs-id1171242152341",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 40. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-problems#fs-id1171242152341\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
