    "prompt": "An electron in a TV CRT moves with a speed of 6.0 × 10 6 m/s , in a direction perpendicular to Earth’s field, which has a strength of 5.0 × 10 −5 T . (a) What strength electric field…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>An electron in a TV CRT moves with a speed of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in a direction perpendicular to Earth’s field, which has a strength of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−5</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>T</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) What strength electric field must be applied perpendicular to the Earth’s field to make the electron moves in a straight line? (b) If this is done between plates separated by 1.00 cm, what is the voltage applied? (Note that TVs are usually surrounded by a ferromagnetic material to shield against external magnetic fields and avoid the need for such a correction.)</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>An electron in a TV CRT moves with a speed of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in a direction perpendicular to Earth’s field, which has a strength of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−5</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>T</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) What strength electric field must be applied perpendicular to the Earth’s field to make the electron moves in a straight line? (b) If this is done between plates separated by 1.00 cm, what is the voltage applied? (Note that TVs are usually surrounded by a ferromagnetic material to shield against external magnetic fields and avoid the need for such a correction.)</p></div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171360211325",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 28. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171360211325\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
