    "topic": "Newton’s laws",
    "prompt": "A body of mass m has initial velocity v 0 in the positive x -direction. It is acted on by a constant force F for time t until the velocity becomes zero; the force continues to act on the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A body of mass <em>m</em> has initial velocity <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in the positive <em>x</em>-direction. It is acted on by a constant force <em>F</em> for time <em>t</em> until the velocity becomes zero; the force continues to act on the body until its velocity becomes <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in the same amount of time. Write an expression for the total distance the body travels in terms of the variables indicated.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A body of mass <em>m</em> has initial velocity <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in the positive <em>x</em>-direction. It is acted on by a constant force <em>F</em> for time <em>t</em> until the velocity becomes zero; the force continues to act on the body until its velocity becomes <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in the same amount of time. Write an expression for the total distance the body travels in terms of the variables indicated.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-challenge-problems#fs-id1165039472721",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1165039472721-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mi>F</mi>\n<mi>m</mi>\n</mfrac>\n<msup>\n<mi>t</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 97. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-challenge-problems#fs-id1165039472721\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
