    "prompt": "Calculate the electric field of a dipole throughout space from the potential.",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Calculate the electric field of a dipole throughout space from the potential.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Calculate the electric field of a dipole throughout space from the potential.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-challenge-problems#fs-id1167586284051",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-7#fs-id1167586284051-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>Apply <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mtext>E</mtext></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"true\">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mover accent=\"true\"><mo>∇</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mo>∇</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>r</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>φ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>r</mi><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>sin</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> to the potential calculated earlier, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mfrac><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>p</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>·</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>r</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>p</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>d</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and assume that the axis of the dipole is aligned with the <em>z</em>-axis of the coordinate system. Thus, the potential is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>d</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>·</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>r</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>d</mi><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cos</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mtext>E</mtext></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"true\">→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cos</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>r</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>sin</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 109. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-challenge-problems#fs-id1167586284051\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
