    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Motion of a Charged Particle in a Magnetic Field",
    "prompt": "(a) What voltage will accelerate electrons to a speed of 6.00 × 10 7 m/s ? (b) Find the radius of curvature of the path of a proton accelerated through this potential in a 0.500-T field…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>(a) What voltage will accelerate electrons to a speed of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (b) Find the radius of curvature of the path of a proton accelerated through this potential in a 0.500-T field and compare this with the radius of curvature of an electron accelerated through the same potential.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>(a) What voltage will accelerate electrons to a speed of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (b) Find the radius of curvature of the path of a proton accelerated through this potential in a 0.500-T field and compare this with the radius of curvature of an electron accelerated through the same potential.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171360288029",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 30. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171360288029\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
