    "prompt": "The velocities of a 3.0-kg object at t = 6.0 s and t = 8.0 s are ( 3.0 i ^ − 6.0 j ^ + 4.0 k ^ ) m/s and ( −2.0 i ^ + 4.0 k ^ ) m/s , respectively. If the object is moving at constant…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The velocities of a 3.0-kg object at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> are <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>−2.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, respectively. If the object is moving at constant acceleration, what is the force acting on it?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The velocities of a 3.0-kg object at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> are <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>−2.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, respectively. If the object is moving at constant acceleration, what is the force acting on it?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-challenge-problems#fs-id1165039445425",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 98. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-challenge-problems#fs-id1165039445425\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
