    "topic": "Coulomb's Law",
    "prompt": "In a salt crystal, the distance between adjacent sodium and chloride ions is 2.82 × 10 −10 m . What is the force of attraction between the two singly charged ions?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>In a salt crystal, the distance between adjacent sodium and chloride ions is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.82</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−10</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the force of attraction between the two singly charged ions?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>In a salt crystal, the distance between adjacent sodium and chloride ions is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.82</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−10</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the force of attraction between the two singly charged ions?</p>\n</div>",
