    "topic": "Calculations of Electric Potential",
    "prompt": "In nuclear fission, a nucleus splits roughly in half. (a) What is the potential 2.00 × 10 −14 m from a fragment that has 46 protons in it? (b) What is the potential energy in MeV of a…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>In nuclear fission, a nucleus splits roughly in half. (a) What is the potential <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−14</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> from a fragment that has 46 protons in it? (b) What is the potential energy in MeV of a similarly charged fragment at this distance?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>In nuclear fission, a nucleus splits roughly in half. (a) What is the potential <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−14</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> from a fragment that has 46 protons in it? (b) What is the potential energy in MeV of a similarly charged fragment at this distance?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167585179868",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 48. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167585179868\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
