    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Magnetic Force on a Current-Carrying Conductor",
    "prompt": "What is the direction of a current that experiences the magnetic force shown in each of the three cases, assuming the current runs perpendicular to B → ?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>What is the direction of a current that experiences the magnetic force shown in each of the three cases, assuming the current runs perpendicular to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></semantics></math></span>?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>What is the direction of a current that experiences the magnetic force shown in each of the three cases, assuming the current runs perpendicular to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></semantics></math></span>?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Case a: B is out of the page, F is up. Case b: B is to the right, F is up. Case c: B is into the page, F is to the left.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/874b5a468da1c71c3a17e953.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171360215665",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 34. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171360215665\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
