    "number": 43,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Work",
    "prompt": "A particle moves along a curved path y ( x ) = ( 10 m ) { 1 + cos [ ( 0.1 m −1 ) x ] } , from x = 0 to x = 10 π m, subject to a tangential force of variable magnitude F ( x ) = ( 10 N )…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A particle moves along a curved path <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mtext>cos</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.1</mn><msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>−1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> from <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>π</mi><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> subject to a tangential force of variable magnitude <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext>sin</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.1</mn><msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>−1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> How much work does the force do? (<em>Hint:</em> Consult a table of integrals or use a numerical integration program.)</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A particle moves along a curved path <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mtext>cos</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.1</mn><msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>−1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> from <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>π</mi><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> subject to a tangential force of variable magnitude <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext>sin</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.1</mn><msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>−1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> How much work does the force do? (<em>Hint:</em> Consult a table of integrals or use a numerical integration program.)</p>\n</div>",
