    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Resistivity and Resistance",
    "prompt": "(a) To what temperature must you raise a copper wire, originally at 20.0 ° C , to double its resistance, neglecting any changes in dimensions? (b) Does this happen in household wiring…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>(a) To what temperature must you raise a copper wire, originally at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°</mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, to double its resistance, neglecting any changes in dimensions? (b) Does this happen in household wiring under ordinary circumstances?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>(a) To what temperature must you raise a copper wire, originally at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°</mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, to double its resistance, neglecting any changes in dimensions? (b) Does this happen in household wiring under ordinary circumstances?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170904130540",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-9#fs-id1170904130540-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.8em\"></mspace><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.8em\"></mspace><mtext>Δ</mtext><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>256.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°C</mtext><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.8em\"></mspace><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>276.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°</mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nb. Under normal conditions, no it should not occur.</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 43. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170904130540\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
