    "prompt": "An alpha-particle ( m = 6.64 × 10 −27 kg, q = 3.2 × 10 −19 C ) travels in a circular path of radius 25 cm in a uniform magnetic field of magnitude 1.5 T. (a) What is the speed of the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>An alpha-particle <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6.64</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−27</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg,</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−19</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C</mtext><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> travels in a circular path of radius 25 cm in a uniform magnetic field of magnitude 1.5 T. (a) What is the speed of the particle? (b) What is the kinetic energy in electron-volts? (c) Through what potential difference must the particle be accelerated in order to give it this kinetic energy?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>An alpha-particle <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6.64</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−27</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg,</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−19</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C</mtext><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> travels in a circular path of radius 25 cm in a uniform magnetic field of magnitude 1.5 T. (a) What is the speed of the particle? (b) What is the kinetic energy in electron-volts? (c) Through what potential difference must the particle be accelerated in order to give it this kinetic energy?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171360369858",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-11#fs-id1171360369858-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.8</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></msup><mtext>m/s</mtext><mo>;</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.8</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup><mtext>eV</mtext><mo>;</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> c. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup><mtext>V</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 31. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171360369858\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
