    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Impulse and Collisions",
    "prompt": "The x -component of a force on a 46-g golf ball by a 7-iron versus time is plotted in the following figure: Find the x -component of the impulse during the intervals [0, 50 ms], and [50…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The <em>x</em>-component of a force on a 46-g golf ball by a 7-iron versus time is plotted in the following figure:</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The <em>x</em>-component of a force on a 46-g golf ball by a 7-iron versus time is plotted in the following figure:</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"A graph of F sub x in Newtons as a function of time in milliseconds. The horizontal axis ranges from 0 to 100 and the vertical axis rages from 0 to 30. The graph starts at 0 and rises to 30 N at time 50 millisecnds. It is then constant at 30 N until t = 100 when it drops to 0.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/f37035e96fa2597572ab7c6d.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n<ol>\n<li>Find the <em>x</em>-component of the impulse during the intervals\n<ol>\n<li>[0, 50 ms], and</li>\n<li>[50 ms, 100 ms]</li>\n</ol></li>\n<li>Find the change in the <em>x</em>-component of the momentum during the intervals\n<ol>\n<li>[0, 50 ms], and</li>\n<li>[50 ms, 100 ms]</li>\n</ol></li>\n</ol>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-problems#fs-id1167131455779",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 32. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-problems#fs-id1167131455779\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
