    "prompt": "A student stands on the edge of a merry-go-round which rotates five times a minute and has a radius of two meters one evening as the sun is setting. The student produces a shadow on the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A student stands on the edge of a merry-go-round which rotates five times a minute and has a radius of two meters one evening as the sun is setting. The student produces a shadow on the nearby building. (a) Write an equation for the position of the shadow. (b) Write an equation for the velocity of the shadow.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A student stands on the edge of a merry-go-round which rotates five times a minute and has a radius of two meters one evening as the sun is setting. The student produces a shadow on the nearby building. (a) Write an equation for the position of the shadow. (b) Write an equation for the velocity of the shadow.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/15-problems#fs-id1167133839992",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-15#fs-id1167133839992-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>cos</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>0.52</mn><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mrow><mn>−1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>−1.05</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext>sin</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>0.52</mn><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mrow><mn>−1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 15, Problem 41. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/15-problems#fs-id1167133839992\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
