    "topic": "Kinetic Energy",
    "prompt": "(a) How fast must a 3000-kg elephant move to have the same kinetic energy as a 65.0-kg sprinter running at 10.0 m/s? (b) Discuss how the larger energies needed for the movement of larger…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>(a) How fast must a 3000-kg elephant move to have the same kinetic energy as a 65.0-kg sprinter running at 10.0 m/s? (b) Discuss how the larger energies needed for the movement of larger animals would relate to metabolic rates.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>(a) How fast must a 3000-kg elephant move to have the same kinetic energy as a 65.0-kg sprinter running at 10.0 m/s? (b) Discuss how the larger energies needed for the movement of larger animals would relate to metabolic rates.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165036778364",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-7#fs-id1165036778364-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. 1.47 m/s; b. answers may vary</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 45. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165036778364\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
