    "topic": "Capacitance",
    "prompt": "A capacitor has parallel plates of area 12 cm 2 separated by 2.0 mm. The space between the plates is filled with polystyrene. (a) Find the maximum permissible voltage across the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A capacitor has parallel plates of area <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> separated by 2.0 mm. The space between the plates is filled with polystyrene. (a) Find the maximum permissible voltage across the capacitor to avoid dielectric breakdown. (b) When the voltage equals the value found in part (a), find the surface charge density on the surface of the dielectric.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A capacitor has parallel plates of area <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> separated by 2.0 mm. The space between the plates is filled with polystyrene. (a) Find the maximum permissible voltage across the capacitor to avoid dielectric breakdown. (b) When the voltage equals the value found in part (a), find the surface charge density on the surface of the dielectric.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/8-challenge-problems#fs-id1167131152618",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 8, Problem 84. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/8-challenge-problems#fs-id1167131152618\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
