    "imported": true,
    "source": "OpenStax",
    "volume": 2,
    "chapter": 11,
    "number": 110,
    "category": "challenge-problems",
    "topic": "Magnetic forces",
    "prompt": "A circular loop of wire of area 10 cm 2 carries a current of 25 A. At a particular instant, the loop lies in the xy -plane and is subjected to a magnetic field B → = ( 2.0 i ^ + 6.0 j ^…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A circular loop of wire of area 10 cm<sup>2</sup> carries a current of 25 A. At a particular instant, the loop lies in the <em>xy</em>-plane and is subjected to a magnetic field <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>8.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>T</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> As viewed from above the <em>xy</em>-plane, the current is circulating clockwise. (a) What is the magnetic dipole moment of the current loop? (b) At this instant, what is the magnetic torque on the loop?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A circular loop of wire of area 10 cm<sup>2</sup> carries a current of 25 A. At a particular instant, the loop lies in the <em>xy</em>-plane and is subjected to a magnetic field <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>8.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>T</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> As viewed from above the <em>xy</em>-plane, the current is circulating clockwise. (a) What is the magnetic dipole moment of the current loop? (b) At this instant, what is the magnetic torque on the loop?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-challenge-problems#fs-id1171361439092",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 110. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-challenge-problems#fs-id1171361439092\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
