    "number": 81,
    "category": "challenge-problems",
    "topic": "Electromagnetic induction",
    "prompt": "An eight-turn coil is tightly wrapped around the outside of the long solenoid as shown below. The radius of the solenoid is 2.0 cm and it has 10 turns per centimeter. The current through…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>An eight-turn coil is <em>tightly wrapped</em> around the outside of the long solenoid as shown below. The radius of the solenoid is 2.0 cm and it has 10 turns per centimeter. The current through the solenoid increases according to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the emf induced in the coil when (a) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, (b) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and (c) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>An eight-turn coil is <em>tightly wrapped</em> around the outside of the long solenoid as shown below. The radius of the solenoid is 2.0 cm and it has 10 turns per centimeter. The current through the solenoid increases according to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the emf induced in the coil when (a) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, (b) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and (c) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows a coil that is tightly wrapped around the outside of the long solenoid.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/cc1db894c07d4f6215c14769.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-challenge-problems#fs-id1171242610369",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-13#fs-id1171242610369-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.01</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−6</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>V</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.37</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−7</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; c. 0 V</p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 81. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-challenge-problems#fs-id1171242610369\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
