    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Motion with Constant Acceleration",
    "prompt": "A particle moves in a straight line with an initial velocity of 0 m/s and a constant acceleration of 30 m/s 2 . If x = 0 at t = 0 , what is the particle’s position at t = 5 s?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A particle moves in a straight line with an initial velocity of 0 m/s and a constant acceleration of 30 m/s<sup>2</sup>. If <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo> at </mo>\n<mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, what is the particle’s position at <em>t</em> = 5 s?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A particle moves in a straight line with an initial velocity of 0 m/s and a constant acceleration of 30 m/s<sup>2</sup>. If <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo> at </mo>\n<mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, what is the particle’s position at <em>t</em> = 5 s?</p></div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168326925511",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 3, Problem 44. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168326925511\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
