    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Kinetic Energy",
    "prompt": "Calculate the kinetic energies of (a) a 2000.0-kg automobile moving at 100.0 km/h; (b) an 80.-kg runner sprinting at 10. m/s; and (c) a 9.1 × 10 −31 -kg electron moving at 2.0 × 10 7 m/s .",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Calculate the kinetic energies of (a) a 2000.0-kg automobile moving at 100.0 km/h; (b) an 80.-kg runner sprinting at 10. m/s; and (c) a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>9.1</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−31</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>-kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> electron moving at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Calculate the kinetic energies of (a) a 2000.0-kg automobile moving at 100.0 km/h; (b) an 80.-kg runner sprinting at 10. m/s; and (c) a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>9.1</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−31</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>-kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> electron moving at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165038044494",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-7#fs-id1165038044494-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. 772 kJ; b. 4.0 kJ; c. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.8</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−16</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>J</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 47. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165038044494\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
