    "topic": "Rolling Motion",
    "prompt": "A yo-yo can be thought of a solid cylinder of mass m and radius r that has a light string wrapped around its circumference (see below). One end of the string is held fixed in space. If…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A yo-yo can be thought of a solid cylinder of mass <em>m</em> and radius <em>r</em> that has a light string wrapped around its circumference (see below). One end of the string is held fixed in space. If the cylinder falls as the string unwinds without slipping, what is the acceleration of the cylinder?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A yo-yo can be thought of a solid cylinder of mass <em>m</em> and radius <em>r</em> that has a light string wrapped around its circumference (see below). One end of the string is held fixed in space. If the cylinder falls as the string unwinds without slipping, what is the acceleration of the cylinder?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"An illustration of a cylinder, radius r, and the forces on it. The force m g acts on the center of the cylinder and points down. The force T acts on the right hand edge and points up.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/0f486b2c49a1abe499a485ea.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-problems#fs-id1165036972880",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 26. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-problems#fs-id1165036972880\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
