    "number": 56,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Coulomb's Law",
    "prompt": "Point charges Q 1 = 2.0 μ C and Q 2 = 4.0 μ C are located at r → 1 = ( 4.0 i ^ − 2.0 j ^ + 5.0 k ^ ) m and r → 2 = ( 8.0 i ^ + 5.0 j ^ − 9.0 k ^ ) m . What is the force of Q 2 on Q 1 ?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Point charges <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> are located at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>r</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>j</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>k</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>r</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>8.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>j</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>9.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>k</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> on <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Point charges <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> are located at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>r</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>j</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>k</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>r</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>8.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>j</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>9.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>k</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> on <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172102028786",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 56. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172102028786\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
