    "source": "OpenStax",
    "volume": 1,
    "chapter": 7,
    "number": 49,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Kinetic Energy",
    "prompt": "An 8.0-g bullet has a speed of 800 m/s. (a) What is its kinetic energy? (b) What is its kinetic energy if the speed is halved?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>An 8.0-g bullet has a speed of 800 m/s. (a) What is its kinetic energy? (b) What is its kinetic energy if the speed is halved?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>An 8.0-g bullet has a speed of 800 m/s. (a) What is its kinetic energy? (b) What is its kinetic energy if the speed is halved?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165038045322",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-7#fs-id1165038045322-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. 2.6 kJ; b. 640 J</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 49. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165038045322\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
