    "prompt": "What is the current through a cylindrical wire of radius R = 0.1 mm if the current density is J = J 0 R r , where J 0 = 32000 A m 2 ?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>What is the current through a cylindrical wire of radius <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>mm</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> if the current density is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>32000</mn><mfrac><mtext>A</mtext><mrow><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>What is the current through a cylindrical wire of radius <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>mm</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> if the current density is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>32000</mn><mfrac><mtext>A</mtext><mrow><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-challenge-problems#fs-id1170901509558",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 90. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-challenge-problems#fs-id1170901509558\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
