    "topic": "Electromagnetic induction",
    "prompt": "Shown below is a long rectangular loop of width w , length l , mass m , and resistance R . The loop starts from rest at the edge of a uniform magnetic field B → and is pushed into the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Shown below is a long rectangular loop of width <em>w</em>, length <em>l</em>, mass <em>m</em>, and resistance <em>R</em>. The loop starts from rest at the edge of a uniform magnetic field <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></semantics></math></span> and is pushed into the field by a constant force <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Calculate the speed of the loop as a function of time.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Shown below is a long rectangular loop of width <em>w</em>, length <em>l</em>, mass <em>m</em>, and resistance <em>R</em>. The loop starts from rest at the edge of a uniform magnetic field <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></semantics></math></span> and is pushed into the field by a constant force <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Calculate the speed of the loop as a function of time.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows a long rectangular loop of width w. The loop starts from rest at the edge of a uniform magnetic field and is pushed into the field by a constant force F.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/98c676528ac0c709b4f8dbd4.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-challenge-problems#fs-id1171242085284",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 82. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-challenge-problems#fs-id1171242085284\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
