    "topic": "Motion with Constant Acceleration",
    "prompt": "A well-thrown ball is caught in a well-padded mitt. If the acceleration of the ball is 2.10 × 10 4 m/s 2 , and 1.85 ms ( 1 ms = 10 −3 s ) elapses from the time the ball first touches the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A well-thrown ball is caught in a well-padded mitt. If the acceleration of the ball is<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and 1.85 ms <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>ms</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> elapses from the time the ball first touches the mitt until it stops, what is the initial velocity of the ball?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A well-thrown ball is caught in a well-padded mitt. If the acceleration of the ball is<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and 1.85 ms <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>ms</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> elapses from the time the ball first touches the mitt until it stops, what is the initial velocity of the ball?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168326959416",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 3, Problem 50. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168326959416\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
