    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Work",
    "prompt": "A particle moving in the xy -plane is subject to a force F → ( x , y ) = ( 50 N / m ) ( x i ^ + y 2 3 m j ^ ) where x and y are in meters. Calculate the work done on the particle by this…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A particle moving in the <em>xy</em>-plane is subject to a force<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mi>F</mi></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"true\">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext><mo>/</mo><mtext>m</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo>\n<mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow>\n<mn>3</mn><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><br/></span>\nwhere <em>x</em> and <em>y</em> are in meters. Calculate the work done on the particle by this force, as it moves in a straight line from the point (3 m, 4 m) to the point (6 m, 8 m).</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A particle moving in the <em>xy</em>-plane is subject to a force<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mi>F</mi></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"true\">→</mo></mover><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext><mo>/</mo><mtext>m</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo>\n<mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow>\n<mn>3</mn><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><br/></span>\nwhere <em>x</em> and <em>y</em> are in meters. Calculate the work done on the particle by this force, as it moves in a straight line from the point (3 m, 4 m) to the point (6 m, 8 m).</p></div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165039191870",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 42. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165039191870\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
