    "prompt": "Find the potential at points P 1 , P 2 , P 3 , and P 4 in the diagram due to the two given charges.",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Find the potential at points <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in the diagram due to the two given charges.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Find the potential at points <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in the diagram due to the two given charges.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"The figure shows two charges, 5mC (located 4cm left from the center) and -10mC (located 4cm right from the center). Four Point P subscript 1, P subscript 2, P subscript 3 and P subscript 4 are located 2cm left, 2cm right, 3cm below and 3cm above the center.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/028757cb1310a58236071fcc.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167585038295",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 52. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167585038295\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
