    "chapter": 3,
    "number": 45,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Motion with Constant Acceleration",
    "prompt": "A particle moves in a straight line with an initial velocity of 30 m/s and constant acceleration 30 m/s 2 . (a) What is its displacement at t = 5 s? (b) What is its velocity at this same…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A particle moves in a straight line with an initial velocity of 30 m/s and constant acceleration 30 m/s<sup>2</sup>. (a) What is its displacement at <em>t</em> = 5 s? (b) What is its velocity at this same time?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A particle moves in a straight line with an initial velocity of 30 m/s and constant acceleration 30 m/s<sup>2</sup>. (a) What is its displacement at <em>t</em> = 5 s? (b) What is its velocity at this same time?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168326901284",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-3#fs-id1168326901284-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. 525 m;<span><br/></span>\nb. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
