    "prompt": "Suppose the mass of a fully loaded module in which astronauts take off from the Moon is 1.00 × 10 4 kg. The thrust of its engines is 3.00 × 10 4 N. (a) Calculate the module’s magnitude…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Suppose the mass of a fully loaded module in which astronauts take off from the Moon is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> kg. The thrust of its engines is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> N. (a) Calculate the module’s magnitude of acceleration in a vertical takeoff from the Moon. (b) Could it lift off from Earth? If not, why not? If it could, calculate the magnitude of its acceleration.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Suppose the mass of a fully loaded module in which astronauts take off from the Moon is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> kg. The thrust of its engines is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> N. (a) Calculate the module’s magnitude of acceleration in a vertical takeoff from the Moon. (b) Could it lift off from Earth? If not, why not? If it could, calculate the magnitude of its acceleration.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-problems#fs-id1165038019168",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 42. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-problems#fs-id1165038019168\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
