    "prompt": "Two identical pucks collide elastically on an air hockey table. Puck 1 was originally at rest; puck 2 has an incoming speed of 6.00 m/s and scatters at an angle of 30 ° with respect to…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Two identical pucks collide elastically on an air hockey table. Puck 1 was originally at rest; puck 2 has an incoming speed of 6.00 m/s and scatters at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with respect to its incoming direction. What is the velocity (magnitude and direction) of puck 1 after the collision?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Two identical pucks collide elastically on an air hockey table. Puck 1 was originally at rest; puck 2 has an incoming speed of 6.00 m/s and scatters at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with respect to its incoming direction. What is the velocity (magnitude and direction) of puck 1 after the collision?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Two sets of red and blue hockey pucks are shown. The first row has a blue hockey puck with an arrow pointing left toward a red hockey puck. The second row shows a similar blue puck with a shorter arrow pointing left toward a red hockey puck at a 30-degree angle from the horizontal.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/02a152a353450ed5bb88710c.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
