    "volume": 1,
    "chapter": 9,
    "number": 59,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Collisions in Multiple Dimensions",
    "prompt": "Three 70-kg deer are standing on a flat 200-kg rock that is on an ice-covered pond. A gunshot goes off and the deer scatter, with deer A running at ( 15 m/s ) i ^ + ( 5.0 m/s ) j ^ ,…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Three 70-kg deer are standing on a flat 200-kg rock that is on an ice-covered pond. A gunshot goes off and the deer scatter, with deer A running at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>15</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, deer B running at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>−12</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>8.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and deer C running at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>18.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the velocity of the rock on which they were standing?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Three 70-kg deer are standing on a flat 200-kg rock that is on an ice-covered pond. A gunshot goes off and the deer scatter, with deer A running at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>15</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, deer B running at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>−12</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>8.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and deer C running at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>18.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the velocity of the rock on which they were standing?</p></div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-problems#fs-id1167132416254",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-9#fs-id1167132416254-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>−</mtext>\n<mrow>\n<mo>(</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>1.47</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>m/s</mtext>\n</mrow>\n<mo>)</mo>\n</mrow>\n<mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\">\n<mover accent=\"true\">\n<mi>i</mi>\n<mo>^</mo>\n</mover>\n</mstyle>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>(</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>1.75</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>m/s</mtext>\n</mrow>\n<mo>)</mo>\n</mrow>\n<mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\">\n<mover accent=\"true\">\n<mi>j</mi>\n<mo>^</mo>\n</mover>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 59. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-problems#fs-id1167132416254\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
