    "prompt": "A body with a mass of 10.0 kg is assumed to be in Earth’s gravitational field with g = 9.80 m/s 2 . What is the net force on the body if there are no other external forces acting on the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A body with a mass of 10.0 kg is assumed to be in Earth’s gravitational field with <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.80</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the net force on the body if there are no other external forces acting on the object?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A body with a mass of 10.0 kg is assumed to be in Earth’s gravitational field with <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9.80</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the net force on the body if there are no other external forces acting on the object?</p></div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-problems#fs-id1165038385956",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1165038385956-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>98 N</p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 47. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-problems#fs-id1165038385956\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
