    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Calculating Moments of Inertia",
    "prompt": "A uniform rod of mass 1.0 kg and length 2.0 m is free to rotate about one end (see the following figure). If the rod is released from rest at an angle of 60 ° with respect to the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A uniform rod of mass 1.0 kg and length 2.0 m is free to rotate about one end (see the following figure). If the rod is released from rest at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>60</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with respect to the horizontal, what is the speed of the tip of the rod as it passes the horizontal position?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A uniform rod of mass 1.0 kg and length 2.0 m is free to rotate about one end (see the following figure). If the rod is released from rest at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>60</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with respect to the horizontal, what is the speed of the tip of the rod as it passes the horizontal position?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows a rod that is released from rest at an angle of 60 degrees with respect to the horizontal.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/6319430e45707040482c9b3c.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-problems#fs-id1167133346254",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-10#fs-id1167133346254-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>v</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>7.14</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>m</mtext>\n<mtext>/</mtext>\n<mtext>s</mtext>\n</mrow>\n<mo>.</mo>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 67. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-problems#fs-id1167133346254\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
