    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Resistivity and Resistance",
    "prompt": "If the 0.100-mm-diameter tungsten filament in a light bulb is to have a resistance of 0.200 Ω at 20.0 ° C , how long should it be?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>If the 0.100-mm-diameter tungsten filament in a light bulb is to have a resistance of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.200</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°</mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, how long should it be?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>If the 0.100-mm-diameter tungsten filament in a light bulb is to have a resistance of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.200</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°</mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, how long should it be?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170902207017",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-9#fs-id1170902207017-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mtable>\n<mtr>\n<mtd columnalign=\"left\">\n<mi>R</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mi>ρ</mi>\n<mfrac>\n<mi>L</mi>\n<mi>A</mi>\n</mfrac>\n</mtd>\n</mtr>\n<mtr>\n<mtd columnalign=\"left\">\n<mi>L</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>3</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>cm</mtext>\n</mtd>\n</mtr>\n</mtable>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 39. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170902207017\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
