    "topic": "Electric Generators and Back Emf",
    "prompt": "Design a current loop that, when rotated in a uniform magnetic field of strength 0.10 T, will produce an emf ε = ε 0 sin ω t , where ε 0 = 110 V and ω = 120 π rad/s .",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Design a current loop that, when rotated in a uniform magnetic field of strength 0.10 T, will produce an emf <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>sin</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>110</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn><mi>π</mi><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>rad/s</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Design a current loop that, when rotated in a uniform magnetic field of strength 0.10 T, will produce an emf <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>sin</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>110</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn><mi>π</mi><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>rad/s</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-problems#fs-id1171241317836",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-13#fs-id1171241317836-solution",
