    "topic": "Motion with Constant Acceleration",
    "prompt": "During a slap shot, a hockey player accelerates the puck from a velocity of 8.00 m/s to 40.0 m/s in the same direction. If this shot takes 3.33 × 10 − 2 s , what is the distance over…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>During a slap shot, a hockey player accelerates the puck from a velocity of 8.00 m/s to 40.0 m/s in the same direction. If this shot takes <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.33</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, what is the distance over which the puck accelerates?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>During a slap shot, a hockey player accelerates the puck from a velocity of 8.00 m/s to 40.0 m/s in the same direction. If this shot takes <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.33</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, what is the distance over which the puck accelerates?</p>\n</div>",
