    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Mass and Weight",
    "prompt": "A rocket sled accelerates at a rate of 49.0 m/s 2 . Its passenger has a mass of 75.0 kg. (a) Calculate the horizontal component of the force the seat exerts against his body. Compare…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A rocket sled accelerates at a rate of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>49.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Its passenger has a mass of 75.0 kg. (a) Calculate the horizontal component of the force the seat exerts against his body. Compare this with his weight using a ratio. (b) Calculate the direction and magnitude of the total force the seat exerts against his body.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A rocket sled accelerates at a rate of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>49.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Its passenger has a mass of 75.0 kg. (a) Calculate the horizontal component of the force the seat exerts against his body. Compare this with his weight using a ratio. (b) Calculate the direction and magnitude of the total force the seat exerts against his body.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-problems#fs-id1165037883254",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1165037883254-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>h</mtext></msub></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mn>3.68</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N and</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mi>w</mi></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mn>7.35</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>h</mtext></msub></mrow><mi>w</mi></mfrac></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mn>5.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>times greater than weight</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nb. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mtext>net</mtext></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mn>3750</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mi>θ</mi></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mn>11.3</mn><mtext>°</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>from horizontal</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 43. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-problems#fs-id1165037883254\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
