    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Determining Field from Potential",
    "prompt": "In a particular region, the electric potential is given by V = − x y 2 z + 4 x y . What is the electric field in this region?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>In a particular region, the electric potential is given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the electric field in this region?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>In a particular region, the electric potential is given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the electric field in this region?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167585172136",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 56. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167585172136\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
