    "topic": "Calculating Moments of Inertia",
    "prompt": "A pendulum consists of a rod of mass 2 kg and length 1 m with a solid sphere at one end with mass 0.3 kg and radius 20 cm (see the following figure). If the pendulum is released from…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A pendulum consists of a rod of mass 2 kg and length 1 m with a solid sphere at one end with mass 0.3 kg and radius 20 cm (see the following figure). If the pendulum is released from rest at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, what is the angular velocity at the lowest point?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A pendulum consists of a rod of mass 2 kg and length 1 m with a solid sphere at one end with mass 0.3 kg and radius 20 cm (see the following figure). If the pendulum is released from rest at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, what is the angular velocity at the lowest point?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows a pendulum that consists of a rod of mass 2 kg and length 1 m with a solid sphere at one end with mass 0.3 kg and radius 20 cm. The pendulum is released from rest at an angle of 30 degrees.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/a5f778dc59d84003d9bc652a.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
