    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Force and Torque on a Current Loop",
    "prompt": "Since the equation for torque on a current-carrying loop is τ = NIAB sin θ , the units of N ⋅ m must equal units of A ⋅ m 2 T. Verify this.",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Since the equation for torque on a current-carrying loop is τ = <em>NIAB</em> sin <em>θ</em>, the units of N ⋅ m must equal units of A ⋅ m<sup>2</sup> T. Verify this.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Since the equation for torque on a current-carrying loop is τ = <em>NIAB</em> sin <em>θ</em>, the units of N ⋅ m must equal units of A ⋅ m<sup>2</sup> T. Verify this.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171360193975",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-11#fs-id1171360193975-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>A</mtext>\n<mo>·</mo>\n<msup>\n<mtext>m</mtext>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n<mo>·</mo>\n<mtext>T</mtext>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mtext>A</mtext>\n<mo>·</mo>\n<msup>\n<mtext>m</mtext>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n<mo>.</mo>\n<mfrac>\n<mtext>N</mtext>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>A</mtext>\n<mo>·</mo>\n<mtext>m</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mfrac>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mtext>N</mtext>\n<mo>·</mo>\n<mtext>m</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 43. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-problems#fs-id1171360193975\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
