    "category": "challenge-problems",
    "topic": "Newton’s laws",
    "prompt": "At a circus, a donkey pulls on a sled carrying a small clown with a force given by 2.48 i ^ + 4.33 j ^ N . A horse pulls on the same sled, aiding the hapless donkey, with a force of 6.56…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>At a circus, a donkey pulls on a sled carrying a small clown with a force given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.48</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>4.33</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. A horse pulls on the same sled, aiding the hapless donkey, with a force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.56</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>5.33</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. The mass of the sled is 575 kg. Using <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></semantics></math></span> form for the answer to each problem, find (a) the net force on the sled when the two animals act together, (b) the acceleration of the sled, and (c) the velocity after 6.50 s.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>At a circus, a donkey pulls on a sled carrying a small clown with a force given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.48</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>4.33</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. A horse pulls on the same sled, aiding the hapless donkey, with a force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.56</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>5.33</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. The mass of the sled is 575 kg. Using <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></semantics></math></span> form for the answer to each problem, find (a) the net force on the sled when the two animals act together, (b) the acceleration of the sled, and (c) the velocity after 6.50 s.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-challenge-problems#fs-id1165039466174",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 104. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-challenge-problems#fs-id1165039466174\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
