    "topic": "Coulomb's Law",
    "prompt": "The charges q 1 = 2.0 × 10 −7 C, q 2 = −4.0 × 10 −7 C, and q 3 = −1.0 × 10 −7 C are placed at the corners of the triangle shown below. What is the force on q 1 ?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The charges <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−7</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C,</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>−4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−7</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>−1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−7</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> are placed at the corners of the triangle shown below. What is the force on <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The charges <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−7</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C,</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>−4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−7</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>−1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−7</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> are placed at the corners of the triangle shown below. What is the force on <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Charges are shown at the vertices of a right triangle. The bottom of the triangle is length 4 meters, the vertical side on the left is length 3 meters, and the hypotenuse is length 5 meters. The charge at the top is q sub one and positive, the charge at the bottom left is q sub 3 and negative and the charge at the bottom right is q sub 2 and negative.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/88b782302ce53584794d53ce.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172101783420",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 62. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172101783420\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
