    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Equipotential Surfaces and Conductors",
    "prompt": "Two parallel plates 10 cm on a side are given equal and opposite charges of magnitude 5.0 × 10 −9 C . The plates are 1.5 mm apart. What is the potential difference between the plates?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Two parallel plates 10 cm on a side are given equal and opposite charges of magnitude <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−9</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> The plates are 1.5 mm apart. What is the potential difference between the plates?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Two parallel plates 10 cm on a side are given equal and opposite charges of magnitude <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−9</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> The plates are 1.5 mm apart. What is the potential difference between the plates?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167586016324",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-7#fs-id1167586016324-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>V</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>85</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>V</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 63. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167586016324\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
