    "topic": "Work-Energy Theorem",
    "prompt": "A 2.0-kg block starts with a speed of 10 m/s at the bottom of a plane inclined at 37 ° to the horizontal. The coefficient of sliding friction between the block and plane is μ k = 0.30 .…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A 2.0-kg block starts with a speed of 10 m/s at the bottom of a plane inclined at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>37</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> to the horizontal. The coefficient of sliding friction between the block and plane is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.30</mn><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) Use the work-energy principle to determine how far the block slides along the plane before momentarily coming to rest. (b) After stopping, the block slides back down the plane. What is its speed when it reaches the bottom? (<em>Hint:</em> For the round trip, only the force of friction does work on the block.)</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A 2.0-kg block starts with a speed of 10 m/s at the bottom of a plane inclined at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>37</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> to the horizontal. The coefficient of sliding friction between the block and plane is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.30</mn><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) Use the work-energy principle to determine how far the block slides along the plane before momentarily coming to rest. (b) After stopping, the block slides back down the plane. What is its speed when it reaches the bottom? (<em>Hint:</em> For the round trip, only the force of friction does work on the block.)</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165038018269",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 60. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165038018269\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
