    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Calculating Electric Fields of Charge Distributions",
    "prompt": "Charge is distributed along the entire x -axis with uniform density λ x and along the entire y -axis with uniform density λ y . Calculate the resulting electric field at (a) r → = a i ^…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Charge is distributed along the entire <em>x</em>-axis with uniform density <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and along the entire <em>y</em>-axis with uniform density <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Calculate the resulting electric field at (a) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>r</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>j</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and (b) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>r</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>k</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Charge is distributed along the entire <em>x</em>-axis with uniform density <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and along the entire <em>y</em>-axis with uniform density <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Calculate the resulting electric field at (a) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>r</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>j</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and (b) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>r</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>k</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172098410621",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1172098410621-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>E</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>r</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>j</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>k</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 89. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172098410621\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
