    "prompt": "(a) What is the capacitance of a parallel-plate capacitor with plates of area 1.50 m 2 that are separated by 0.0200 mm of neoprene rubber? (b) What charge does it hold when 9.00 V is…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>(a) What is the capacitance of a parallel-plate capacitor with plates of area <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> that are separated by 0.0200 mm of neoprene rubber? (b) What charge does it hold when 9.00 V is applied to it?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>(a) What is the capacitance of a parallel-plate capacitor with plates of area <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> that are separated by 0.0200 mm of neoprene rubber? (b) What charge does it hold when 9.00 V is applied to it?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/8-problems#fs-id1167131499185",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-8#fs-id1167131499185-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>μ</mtext><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mtext>-5</mtext></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 8, Problem 59. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/8-problems#fs-id1167131499185\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
