    "number": 67,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Superconductors",
    "prompt": "A 12-gauge gold wire has a length of 1 meter. (a) What would be the length of a silver 12-gauge wire with the same resistance? (b) What are their respective resistances at the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A 12-gauge gold wire has a length of 1 meter. (a) What would be the length of a silver 12-gauge wire with the same resistance? (b) What are their respective resistances at the temperature of boiling water?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A 12-gauge gold wire has a length of 1 meter. (a) What would be the length of a silver 12-gauge wire with the same resistance? (b) What are their respective resistances at the temperature of boiling water?</p></div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170902705567",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-9#fs-id1170902705567-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mtext>Au</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mtext>Ag</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.8em\"></mspace><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mtext>Au</mtext></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mtext>Au</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mtext>Au</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mtext>Ag</mtext></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mtext>Ag</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mtext>Ag</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.8em\"></mspace><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mtext>Ag</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.53</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nb. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mtext>Au,20 °C</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0074</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.8em\"></mspace><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mtext>Au,100 °C</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0094</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.8em\"></mspace><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mtext>Ag</mtext><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°C</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0096</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 67. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170902705567\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
