    "topic": "Molecular Model of a Dielectric",
    "prompt": "Two parallel plates have equal and opposite charges. When the space between the plates is evacuated, the electrical field is E = 3.20 × 10 5 V / m . When the space is filled with…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Two parallel plates have equal and opposite charges. When the space between the plates is evacuated, the electrical field is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.20</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>V</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. When the space is filled with dielectric, the electrical field is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>V</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (a) What is the surface charge density on each surface of the dielectric? (b) What is the dielectric constant?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Two parallel plates have equal and opposite charges. When the space between the plates is evacuated, the electrical field is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.20</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>V</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. When the space is filled with dielectric, the electrical field is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>V</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (a) What is the surface charge density on each surface of the dielectric? (b) What is the dielectric constant?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/8-problems#fs-id1167134857697",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 8, Problem 60. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/8-problems#fs-id1167134857697\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
