    "topic": "Induced Electric Fields",
    "prompt": "The magnetic field at all points within the cylindrical region whose cross-section is indicated in the accompanying figure starts at 1.0 T and decreases uniformly to zero in 20 s. What…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The magnetic field at all points within the cylindrical region whose cross-section is indicated in the accompanying figure starts at 1.0 T and decreases uniformly to zero in 20 s. What is the electric field (both magnitude and direction) as a function of <em>r</em>, the distance from the geometric center of the region?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The magnetic field at all points within the cylindrical region whose cross-section is indicated in the accompanying figure starts at 1.0 T and decreases uniformly to zero in 20 s. What is the electric field (both magnitude and direction) as a function of <em>r</em>, the distance from the geometric center of the region?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows a uniform magnetic field with a radius of 20 centimeters.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/0807f754649ffeb9646cd1ac.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
