    "topic": "Finding Velocity and Displacement from Acceleration",
    "prompt": "The velocity of a particle moving along the x- axis varies with time according to v ( t ) = A + B t −1 , where A = 2 m/s, B = 0.25 m, and 1.0 s ≤ t ≤ 8.0 s . Determine the acceleration…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The velocity of a particle moving along the <em>x-</em>axis varies with time according to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>−1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, where <em>A</em> = 2 m/s, <em>B</em> = 0.25 m, and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>8.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Determine the acceleration and position of the particle at <em>t</em> = 2.0 s and <em>t</em> = 5.0 s. Assume that <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The velocity of a particle moving along the <em>x-</em>axis varies with time according to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>−1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, where <em>A</em> = 2 m/s, <em>B</em> = 0.25 m, and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>8.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Determine the acceleration and position of the particle at <em>t</em> = 2.0 s and <em>t</em> = 5.0 s. Assume that <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168054976898",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 3, Problem 80. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168054976898\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
