    "number": 45,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Angular Momentum",
    "prompt": "A boulder of mass 20 kg and radius 20 cm rolls down a hill 15 m high from rest. What is its angular momentum when it is half way down the hill? (b) At the bottom?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A boulder of mass 20 kg and radius 20 cm rolls down a hill 15 m high from rest. What is its angular momentum when it is half way down the hill? (b) At the bottom?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A boulder of mass 20 kg and radius 20 cm rolls down a hill 15 m high from rest. What is its angular momentum when it is half way down the hill? (b) At the bottom?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-problems#fs-id1165036843517",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-11#fs-id1165036843517-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>51.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>rad</mtext></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><msup><mrow><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nb. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>72.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>rad</mtext></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>23.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><msup><mrow><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 45. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-problems#fs-id1165036843517\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
