    "category": "challenge-problems",
    "topic": "DC circuits",
    "prompt": "Consider the circuit shown below. Each battery has an emf of 1.50 V and an internal resistance of 1.00 Ω . (a) What is the current through the external resistor, which has a resistance…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Consider the circuit shown below. Each battery has an emf of 1.50 V and an internal resistance of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) What is the current through the external resistor, which has a resistance of 10.00 ohms? (b) What is the terminal voltage of each battery?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Consider the circuit shown below. Each battery has an emf of 1.50 V and an internal resistance of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) What is the current through the external resistor, which has a resistance of 10.00 ohms? (b) What is the terminal voltage of each battery?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"The circuit shows three parallel branches. The first and second branch both have two voltage sources ε with positive terminals upward and internal resistances r. The third branch has a resistor R.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/d50fddfa621b9e0af1bfe5a5.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-challenge-problems#fs-id1172102078125",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-10#fs-id1172102078125-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. 0.273 A; b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.36</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 89. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-challenge-problems#fs-id1172102078125\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
