    "number": 69,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Electric Field",
    "prompt": "What is the electric field at a point where the force on a −2.0 × 10 −6 −C charge is ( 4.0 i ^ − 6.0 j ^ ) × 10 −6 N?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>What is the electric field at a point where the force on a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>−2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−6</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>−C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> charge is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>j</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−6</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N?</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>What is the electric field at a point where the force on a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>−2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−6</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>−C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> charge is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>j</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−6</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N?</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172101727500",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1172101727500-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>E</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mo>(</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>−2.0</mn>\n<mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\">\n<mover accent=\"true\">\n<mtext>i</mtext>\n<mo>^</mo>\n</mover>\n</mstyle>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mn>3.0</mn>\n<mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\">\n<mover accent=\"true\">\n<mtext>j</mtext>\n<mo>^</mo>\n</mover>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n<mo>)</mo>\n</mrow>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>N/C</mtext>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 69. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172101727500\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
