    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Motion with Constant Acceleration",
    "prompt": "Blood is accelerated from rest to 30.0 cm/s in a distance of 1.80 cm by the left ventricle of the heart. (a) Make a sketch of the situation. (b) List the knowns in this problem. (c) How…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Blood is accelerated from rest to 30.0 cm/s in a distance of 1.80 cm by the left ventricle of the heart. (a) Make a sketch of the situation. (b) List the knowns in this problem. (c) How long does the acceleration take? To solve this part, first identify the unknown, then discuss how you chose the appropriate equation to solve for it. After choosing the equation, show your steps in solving for the unknown, checking your units. (d) Is the answer reasonable when compared with the time for a heartbeat?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Blood is accelerated from rest to 30.0 cm/s in a distance of 1.80 cm by the left ventricle of the heart. (a) Make a sketch of the situation. (b) List the knowns in this problem. (c) How long does the acceleration take? To solve this part, first identify the unknown, then discuss how you chose the appropriate equation to solve for it. After choosing the equation, show your steps in solving for the unknown, checking your units. (d) Is the answer reasonable when compared with the time for a heartbeat?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168329462605",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-3#fs-id1168329462605-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a.<span><br/></span>\n</p><span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows object with zero speed and unknown acceleration at the beginning. After unknown time, object reaches speed of 30 centimeters per second and is at distance of 1.8 centimeters from the starting point. Acceleration of the object at this point is unknown.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/1f6ec968b3e88fcc952d8ab6.jpg\"/>\n</span><p><span><br/></span>\nb. Knowns: <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30.0</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><mtext>s,</mtext></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.80</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nc. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>250</mn><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm/</mtext><mrow><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.12</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nd. yes</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 3, Problem 55. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168329462605\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
