    "number": 107,
    "category": "challenge-problems",
    "topic": "Newton’s laws",
    "prompt": "An object is acted on by three simultaneous forces: F → 1 = ( −3.00 i ^ + 2.00 j ^ ) N , F → 2 = ( 6.00 i ^ − 4.00 j ^ ) N , and F → 3 = ( 2.00 i ^ + 5.00 j ^ ) N . The object…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>An object is acted on by three simultaneous forces: <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>−3.00</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>2.00</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>6.00</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>4.00</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2.00</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>5.00</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. The object experiences acceleration of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.23</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (a) Find the acceleration vector in terms of <em>m</em>. (b) Find the mass of the object. (c) If the object begins from rest, find its speed after 5.00 s. (d) Find the components of the velocity of the object after 5.00 s.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>An object is acted on by three simultaneous forces: <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>−3.00</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>2.00</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>6.00</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>4.00</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2.00</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>5.00</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. The object experiences acceleration of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.23</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (a) Find the acceleration vector in terms of <em>m</em>. (b) Find the mass of the object. (c) If the object begins from rest, find its speed after 5.00 s. (d) Find the components of the velocity of the object after 5.00 s.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-challenge-problems#fs-id1165039484259",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1165039484259-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>5.00</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3.00</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> b. 1.38 kg; c. 21.2 m/s; d. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>18.1</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>10.9</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 107. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-challenge-problems#fs-id1165039484259\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
