    "prompt": "Consider Figure 5.28 . The driver attempts to get the car out of the mud by exerting a perpendicular force of 610.0 N, and the distance she pushes in the middle of the rope is 1.00 m…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Consider <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-6-common-forces\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Figure 5.28</a>. The driver attempts to get the car out of the mud by exerting a perpendicular force of 610.0 N, and the distance she pushes in the middle of the rope is 1.00 m while she stands 6.00 m away from the car on the left and 6.00 m away from the tree on the right. What is the tension <em>T</em> in the rope, and how do you find the answer?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Consider <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-6-common-forces\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Figure 5.28</a>. The driver attempts to get the car out of the mud by exerting a perpendicular force of 610.0 N, and the distance she pushes in the middle of the rope is 1.00 m while she stands 6.00 m away from the car on the left and 6.00 m away from the tree on the right. What is the tension <em>T</em> in the rope, and how do you find the answer?</p>\n</div>",
