    "topic": "Work-Energy Theorem",
    "prompt": "When a 3.0-kg block is pushed against a massless spring of force constant 4.5 × 10 3 N/m, the spring is compressed 8.0 cm. The block is released, and it slides 2.0 m (from the point at…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>When a 3.0-kg block is pushed against a massless spring of force constant <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N/m,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> the spring is compressed 8.0 cm. The block is released, and it slides 2.0 m (from the point at which it is released) across a horizontal surface before friction stops it. What is the coefficient of kinetic friction between the block and the surface?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>When a 3.0-kg block is pushed against a massless spring of force constant <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N/m,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> the spring is compressed 8.0 cm. The block is released, and it slides 2.0 m (from the point at which it is released) across a horizontal surface before friction stops it. What is the coefficient of kinetic friction between the block and the surface?</p></div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165036886605",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-7#fs-id1165036886605-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>0.25</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 61. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165036886605\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
