    "topic": "Angular Momentum",
    "prompt": "A mountain biker takes a jump in a race and goes airborne. The mountain bike is travelling at 10.0 m/s before it goes airborne. If the mass of the front wheel on the bike is 750 g and…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A mountain biker takes a jump in a race and goes airborne. The mountain bike is travelling at 10.0 m/s before it goes airborne. If the mass of the front wheel on the bike is 750 g and has radius 35 cm, what is the angular momentum of the spinning wheel in the air the moment the bike leaves the ground?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A mountain biker takes a jump in a race and goes airborne. The mountain bike is travelling at 10.0 m/s before it goes airborne. If the mass of the front wheel on the bike is 750 g and has radius 35 cm, what is the angular momentum of the spinning wheel in the air the moment the bike leaves the ground?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-problems#fs-id1165036901951",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-11#fs-id1165036901951-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>ω</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>28.6</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>rad</mtext>\n</mrow>\n<mtext>/</mtext>\n<mtext>s</mtext>\n</mrow>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">⇒</mo>\n<mi>L</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>2.6</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>kg</mtext>\n<mo>·</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<msup>\n<mtext>m</mtext>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n<mtext>/</mtext>\n<mtext>s</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 51. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-problems#fs-id1165036901951\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
