    "topic": "Capacitance",
    "prompt": "A capacitor is made from two flat parallel plates placed 0.40 mm apart. When a charge of 0.020 μ C is placed on the plates the potential difference between them is 250 V. (a) What is the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A capacitor is made from two flat parallel plates placed 0.40 mm apart. When a charge of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.020</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>μ</mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is placed on the plates the potential difference between them is 250 V. (a) What is the capacitance of the plates? (b) What is the area of each plate? (c) What is the charge on the plates when the potential difference between them is 500 V? (d) What maximum potential difference can be applied between the plates so that the magnitude of electrical fields between the plates does not exceed 3.0 MV/m?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A capacitor is made from two flat parallel plates placed 0.40 mm apart. When a charge of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.020</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>μ</mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is placed on the plates the potential difference between them is 250 V. (a) What is the capacitance of the plates? (b) What is the area of each plate? (c) What is the charge on the plates when the potential difference between them is 500 V? (d) What maximum potential difference can be applied between the plates so that the magnitude of electrical fields between the plates does not exceed 3.0 MV/m?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/8-additional-problems#fs-id1167131447895",
