    "prompt": "A nichrome rod that is 3.00 mm long with a cross-sectional area of 1.00 mm 2 is used for a digital thermometer. (a) What is the resistance at room temperature? (b) What is the resistance…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A nichrome rod that is 3.00 mm long with a cross-sectional area of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.00</mn><msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>mm</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is used for a digital thermometer. (a) What is the resistance at room temperature? (b) What is the resistance at body temperature?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A nichrome rod that is 3.00 mm long with a cross-sectional area of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.00</mn><msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>mm</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is used for a digital thermometer. (a) What is the resistance at room temperature? (b) What is the resistance at body temperature?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-additional-problems#fs-id1170902756728",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-9#fs-id1170902756728-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a.<span><br/></span><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.003</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; b.<span><br/></span><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>c</mtext></msub></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mn>37.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°</mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\"><mi>R</mi></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mn>0.00302</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></semantics></math></span></p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 71. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-additional-problems#fs-id1170902756728\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
