    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Electric Field",
    "prompt": "The electric field in a particular thundercloud is 2.0 × 10 5 N/C . What is the acceleration of an electron in this field?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The electric field in a particular thundercloud is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N/C</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the acceleration of an electron in this field?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The electric field in a particular thundercloud is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N/C</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the acceleration of an electron in this field?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172101730237",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1172101730237-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.204</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−14</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.517</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 71. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172101730237\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
