    "topic": "Torque",
    "prompt": "A seesaw has length 10.0 m and uniform mass 10.0 kg and is resting at an angle of 30 ° with respect to the ground (see the following figure). The pivot is located at 6.0 m. What…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A seesaw has length 10.0 m and uniform mass 10.0 kg and is resting at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with respect to the ground (see the following figure). The pivot is located at 6.0 m. What magnitude of force needs to be applied perpendicular to the seesaw at the raised end so as to allow the seesaw to barely start to rotate?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A seesaw has length 10.0 m and uniform mass 10.0 kg and is resting at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with respect to the ground (see the following figure). The pivot is located at 6.0 m. What magnitude of force needs to be applied perpendicular to the seesaw at the raised end so as to allow the seesaw to barely start to rotate?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows a seesaw. One of the ends of the seesaw rests on the ground forming 30 degree angle with it, another end is hanging in the air.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/8c7d8eefbd5ec860e540a7dd.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-problems#fs-id1167133333416",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 78. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-problems#fs-id1167133333416\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
