    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Electric Dipoles",
    "prompt": "Consider the equal and opposite charges shown below. (a) Show that at all points on the x -axis for which | x | ≫ a , E ≈ Q a / 2 π ε 0 x 3 . (b) Show that at all points on the y -axis…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Consider the equal and opposite charges shown below. (a) Show that at all points on the <em>x</em>-axis for which <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≫</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>≈</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (b) Show that at all points on the <em>y</em>-axis for which <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≫</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>≈</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><mi>π</mi><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Consider the equal and opposite charges shown below. (a) Show that at all points on the <em>x</em>-axis for which <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≫</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>≈</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (b) Show that at all points on the <em>y</em>-axis for which <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≫</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>≈</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><mi>π</mi><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Two charges are shown on the y axis of an x y coordinate system. Charge +Q is a distance a above the origin, and charge −Q is a distance a below the origin.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/e5c92d084c694e5a3aee93a7.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172096212011",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1172096212011-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≫</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">⇒</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">⇒</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>≫</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">⇒</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 105. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172096212011\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
