    "topic": "Electric Field",
    "prompt": "A small piece of cork whose mass is 2.0 g is given a charge of 5.0 × 10 −7 C . What electric field is needed to place the cork in equilibrium under the combined electric and…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A small piece of cork whose mass is 2.0 g is given a charge of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−7</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What electric field is needed to place the cork in equilibrium under the combined electric and gravitational forces?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A small piece of cork whose mass is 2.0 g is given a charge of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−7</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What electric field is needed to place the cork in equilibrium under the combined electric and gravitational forces?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172102112398",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 72. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172102112398\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
