    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Current and resistance",
    "prompt": "The temperature in Philadelphia, PA can vary between 68.00 ° F and 100.00 ° F in one summer day. By what percentage will an aluminum wire’s resistance change during the day?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The temperature in Philadelphia, PA can vary between <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>68.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°</mtext><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>100.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°</mtext><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in one summer day. By what percentage will an aluminum wire’s resistance change during the day?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The temperature in Philadelphia, PA can vary between <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>68.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°</mtext><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>100.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°</mtext><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in one summer day. By what percentage will an aluminum wire’s resistance change during the day?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-additional-problems#fs-id1170899252186",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 72. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-additional-problems#fs-id1170899252186\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
