    "topic": "Electric Dipoles",
    "prompt": "(a) What is the dipole moment of the configuration shown above? If Q = 4.0 μ C , (b) what is the torque on this dipole with an electric field of 4.0 × 10 5 N/C i ^ ? (c) What is the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>(a) What is the dipole moment of the configuration shown above? If <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, (b) what is the torque on this dipole with an electric field of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N/C</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>? (c) What is the torque on this dipole with an electric field of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>−4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N/C</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>? (d) What is the torque on this dipole with an electric field of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N/C</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>j</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>(a) What is the dipole moment of the configuration shown above? If <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, (b) what is the torque on this dipole with an electric field of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N/C</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>? (c) What is the torque on this dipole with an electric field of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>−4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N/C</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>? (d) What is the torque on this dipole with an electric field of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N/C</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>j</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172098354217",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 106. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172098354217\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
