    "topic": "Magnetic forces",
    "prompt": "Calculate the magnetic force on a hypothetical particle of charge 1.0 × 10 −19 C moving with a velocity of 6.0 × 10 4 i ^ m/s in a magnetic field of 1.2 k ^ T .",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Calculate the magnetic force on a hypothetical particle of charge <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−19</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> moving with a velocity of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in a magnetic field of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.2</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mtext>T</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Calculate the magnetic force on a hypothetical particle of charge <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−19</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> moving with a velocity of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in a magnetic field of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.2</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mtext>T</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1171361209797",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 58. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1171361209797\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
