    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Mutual Inductance",
    "prompt": "A toroidal coil has a mean radius of 16 cm and a cross-sectional area of 0.25 cm 2 ; it is wound uniformly with 1000 turns. A second toroidal coil of 750 turns is wound uniformly over…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A toroidal coil has a mean radius of 16 cm and a cross-sectional area of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; it is wound uniformly with 1000 turns. A second toroidal coil of 750 turns is wound uniformly over the first coil. Ignoring the variation of the magnetic field within a toroid, determine the mutual inductance of the two coils.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A toroidal coil has a mean radius of 16 cm and a cross-sectional area of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; it is wound uniformly with 1000 turns. A second toroidal coil of 750 turns is wound uniformly over the first coil. Ignoring the variation of the magnetic field within a toroid, determine the mutual inductance of the two coils.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-problems#fs-id1167131168748",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-14#fs-id1167131168748-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<msub>\n<mi>M</mi>\n<mrow>\n<mn>21</mn>\n</mrow>\n</msub>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>2.3</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mo>×</mo>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<msup>\n<mn>10</mn>\n<mrow>\n<mn>−5</mn>\n</mrow>\n</msup>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>H</mtext>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 14, Problem 33. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-problems#fs-id1167131168748\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
