    "prompt": "A bare helium nucleus has two positive charges and a mass of 6.64 × 10 – 27 kg . (a) Calculate its kinetic energy in joules at 2.00 % of the speed of light. (b) What is this in…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A bare helium nucleus has two positive charges and a mass of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.64</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>–</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (a) Calculate its kinetic energy in joules at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.00</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> of the speed of light. (b) What is this in electron-volts? (c) What voltage would be needed to obtain this energy?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A bare helium nucleus has two positive charges and a mass of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.64</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>–</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (a) Calculate its kinetic energy in joules at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.00</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> of the speed of light. (b) What is this in electron-volts? (c) What voltage would be needed to obtain this energy?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167586139810",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 76. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-problems#fs-id1167586139810\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
