    "prompt": "A merry-go-round has a radius of 2.0 m and a moment of inertia 300 kg · m 2 . A boy of mass 50 kg runs tangent to the rim at a speed of 4.0 m/s and jumps on. If the merry-go-round is…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A merry-go-round has a radius of 2.0 m and a moment of inertia <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>300</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> A boy of mass 50 kg runs tangent to the rim at a speed of 4.0 m/s and jumps on. If the merry-go-round is initially at rest, what is the angular velocity after the boy jumps on?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A merry-go-round has a radius of 2.0 m and a moment of inertia <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>300</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> A boy of mass 50 kg runs tangent to the rim at a speed of 4.0 m/s and jumps on. If the merry-go-round is initially at rest, what is the angular velocity after the boy jumps on?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-problems#fs-id1165037268381",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-11#fs-id1165037268381-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>i</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>400.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>f</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>500.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.80</mn><mrow><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>rad</mtext></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 61. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-problems#fs-id1165037268381\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
