    "prompt": "A 4.00 - μ F capacitor and a 6.00 - μ F capacitor are connected in parallel across a 600-V supply line. (a) Find the charge on each capacitor and voltage across each. (b) The charged…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.00</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> capacitor and a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.00</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> capacitor are connected in parallel across a 600-V supply line. (a) Find the charge on each capacitor and voltage across each. (b) The charged capacitors are disconnected from the line and from each other. They are then reconnected to each other with terminals of unlike sign together. Find the final charge on each capacitor and the voltage across each.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.00</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> capacitor and a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.00</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> capacitor are connected in parallel across a 600-V supply line. (a) Find the charge on each capacitor and voltage across each. (b) The charged capacitors are disconnected from the line and from each other. They are then reconnected to each other with terminals of unlike sign together. Find the final charge on each capacitor and the voltage across each.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/8-additional-problems#fs-id1167131146194",
