    "topic": "DC circuits",
    "prompt": "Consider the circuit below. (a) What is the initial current through resistor R 2 when the switch is closed? (b) What is the current through resistor R 2 when the capacitor is fully…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Consider the circuit below. (a) What is the initial current through resistor <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> when the switch is closed? (b) What is the current through resistor <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> when the capacitor is fully charged, long after the switch is closed? (c) What happens if the switch is opened after it has been closed for some time? (d) If the switch has been closed for a time period long enough for the capacitor to become fully charged, and then the switch is opened, how long before the current through resistor <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> reaches half of its initial value?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Consider the circuit below. (a) What is the initial current through resistor <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> when the switch is closed? (b) What is the current through resistor <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> when the capacitor is fully charged, long after the switch is closed? (c) What happens if the switch is opened after it has been closed for some time? (d) If the switch has been closed for a time period long enough for the capacitor to become fully charged, and then the switch is opened, how long before the current through resistor <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> reaches half of its initial value?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"The positive terminal of voltage source V subscript 1 of 24 V is connected to an open switch. The other end of the switch is connected to two parallel branches, one with resistor R subscript 1 of 10 kΩ and other with capacitor C of 10 μF. The two branches are connected to source V subscript 1 through resistor R subscript 2 of 30 kΩ.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/4bdd70c708a7811b3e4815ca.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-challenge-problems#fs-id1172099515898",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 94. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-challenge-problems#fs-id1172099515898\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
