    "prompt": "A man of mass 80 kg runs up a flight of stairs 20 m high in 10 s. (a) how much power is used to lift the man? (b) If the man’s body is 25% efficient, how much power does he expend?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A man of mass 80 kg runs up a flight of stairs 20 m high in 10 s. (a) how much power is used to lift the man? (b) If the man’s body is 25% efficient, how much power does he expend?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A man of mass 80 kg runs up a flight of stairs 20 m high in 10 s. (a) how much power is used to lift the man? (b) If the man’s body is 25% efficient, how much power does he expend?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165038158671",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-7#fs-id1165038158671-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. 1.57 kW; b. 6.28 kW</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 77. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165038158671\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
