    "topic": "Torque",
    "prompt": "A horizontal beam of length 3 m and mass 2.0 kg has a mass of 1.0 kg and width 0.2 m sitting at the end of the beam (see the following figure). What is the torque of the system about the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A horizontal beam of length 3 m and mass 2.0 kg has a mass of 1.0 kg and width 0.2 m sitting at the end of the beam (see the following figure). What is the torque of the system about the support at the wall?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A horizontal beam of length 3 m and mass 2.0 kg has a mass of 1.0 kg and width 0.2 m sitting at the end of the beam (see the following figure). What is the torque of the system about the support at the wall?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows a horizontal beam that is connected to the wall. Beam has a length of 3 m and mass 2.0 kg. In addition, a mass of 1.0 kg and width 0.2 m sits at the end of the beam.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/e3983edb2a05620be504e9d8.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-problems#fs-id1167132282560",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-10#fs-id1167132282560-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mstyle>\n<mo>∑</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mi>τ</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n<mn>57.82</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>N</mtext>\n<mo>·</mo>\n<mtext>m</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 81. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-problems#fs-id1167132282560\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
