    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Projectile Motion",
    "prompt": "A basketball player shoots toward a basket 6.1 m away and 3.0 m above the floor. If the ball is released 1.8 m above the floor at an angle of 60 ° above the horizontal, what must the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A basketball player shoots toward a basket 6.1 m away and 3.0 m above the floor. If the ball is released 1.8 m above the floor at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>60</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> above the horizontal, what must the initial speed be if it were to go through the basket?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A basketball player shoots toward a basket 6.1 m away and 3.0 m above the floor. If the ball is released 1.8 m above the floor at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>60</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> above the horizontal, what must the initial speed be if it were to go through the basket?</p>\n</div>",
