    "topic": "Capacitance",
    "prompt": "Three capacitors having capacitances of 8.40, 8.40, and 4.20 μ F , respectively, are connected in series across a 36.0-V potential difference. (a) What is the charge on the 4.20 - μ F…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Three capacitors having capacitances of 8.40, 8.40, and 4.20 <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>μ</mtext><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, respectively, are connected in series across a 36.0-V potential difference. (a) What is the charge on the <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.20</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mtext>μ</mtext><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> capacitor? (b) The capacitors are disconnected from the potential difference without allowing them to discharge. They are then reconnected in parallel with each other with the positively charged plates connected together. What is the voltage across each capacitor in the parallel combination?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Three capacitors having capacitances of 8.40, 8.40, and 4.20 <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>μ</mtext><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, respectively, are connected in series across a 36.0-V potential difference. (a) What is the charge on the <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.20</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mtext>μ</mtext><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> capacitor? (b) The capacitors are disconnected from the potential difference without allowing them to discharge. They are then reconnected in parallel with each other with the positively charged plates connected together. What is the voltage across each capacitor in the parallel combination?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/8-additional-problems#fs-id1167131335360",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-8#fs-id1167131335360-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>75.6</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>μ</mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; b. 10.8 V</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 8, Problem 69. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/8-additional-problems#fs-id1167131335360\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
