    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Capacitance",
    "prompt": "Three capacitors having capacitances 8.4, 8.4, and 4.2 μ F are connected in series across a 36.0-V potential difference. (a) What is the total energy stored in all three capacitors? (b)…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Three capacitors having capacitances 8.4, 8.4, and 4.2 <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>μ</mtext><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> are connected in series across a 36.0-V potential difference. (a) What is the total energy stored in all three capacitors? (b) The capacitors are disconnected from the potential difference without allowing them to discharge. They are then reconnected in parallel with each other with the positively charged plates connected together. What is the total energy now stored in the capacitors?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Three capacitors having capacitances 8.4, 8.4, and 4.2 <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>μ</mtext><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> are connected in series across a 36.0-V potential difference. (a) What is the total energy stored in all three capacitors? (b) The capacitors are disconnected from the potential difference without allowing them to discharge. They are then reconnected in parallel with each other with the positively charged plates connected together. What is the total energy now stored in the capacitors?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/8-additional-problems#fs-id1167134835308",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 8, Problem 72. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/8-additional-problems#fs-id1167134835308\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
