    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Electric charge and fields",
    "prompt": "A charge Q is fixed at the origin and a second charge q moves along the x -axis, as shown below. How much work is done on q by the electric force when q moves from x 1 to x 2 ?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A charge <em>Q</em> is fixed at the origin and a second charge <em>q</em> moves along the <em>x</em>-axis, as shown below. How much work is done on <em>q</em> by the electric force when <em>q</em> moves from <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>to</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A charge <em>Q</em> is fixed at the origin and a second charge <em>q</em> moves along the <em>x</em>-axis, as shown below. How much work is done on <em>q</em> by the electric force when <em>q</em> moves from <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>to</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"A charge Q is shown at the origin and a second charge q is shown to its right, on the x axis, moving to the right. Both are positive charges. Point x 1 is between the charges. Point x 2 is to the right of both.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/d6b435352d81bc6605f50bda.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-additional-problems#fs-id1172098373892",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 112. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-additional-problems#fs-id1172098373892\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
