    "number": 88,
    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Electric potential",
    "prompt": "A 12.0-V battery-operated bottle warmer heats 50.0 g of glass, 2.50 × 10 2 g of baby formula, and 2.00 × 10 2 g of aluminum from 20.0 °C to 90.0 °C . (a) How much charge is moved by the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A 12.0-V battery-operated bottle warmer heats 50.0 g of glass, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>g</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> of baby formula, and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>g</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> of aluminum from <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>90.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (a) How much charge is moved by the battery? (b) How many electrons per second flow if it takes 5.00 min to warm the formula? (<em>Hint:</em> Assume that the specific heat of baby formula is about the same as the specific heat of water.)</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A 12.0-V battery-operated bottle warmer heats 50.0 g of glass, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>g</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> of baby formula, and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>g</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> of aluminum from <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>90.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (a) How much charge is moved by the battery? (b) How many electrons per second flow if it takes 5.00 min to warm the formula? (<em>Hint:</em> Assume that the specific heat of baby formula is about the same as the specific heat of water.)</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-additional-problems#fs-id1167585791609",
