    "prompt": "A resistor rated at 250 k Ω is connected across two D cell batteries (each 1.50 V) in series, with a total voltage of 3.00 V. The manufacturer advertises that their resistors are within…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A resistor rated at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>250</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>k</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is connected across two D cell batteries (each 1.50 V) in series, with a total voltage of 3.00 V. The manufacturer advertises that their resistors are within 5% of the rated value. What are the possible minimum current and maximum current through the resistor?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A resistor rated at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>250</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>k</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is connected across two D cell batteries (each 1.50 V) in series, with a total voltage of 3.00 V. The manufacturer advertises that their resistors are within 5% of the rated value. What are the possible minimum current and maximum current through the resistor?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170903858880",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-9#fs-id1170903858880-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mtable>\n<mtr></mtr>\n<mtr></mtr>\n<mtr>\n<mtd columnalign=\"left\">\n<msub>\n<mi>R</mi>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>min</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</msub>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>2.375</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mo>×</mo>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<msup>\n<mn>10</mn>\n<mn>5</mn>\n</msup>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>Ω</mtext>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mo>,</mo>\n<mspace width=\"0.8em\"></mspace>\n<msub>\n<mi>I</mi>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>min</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</msub>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>12.63</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mi>μ</mi>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>A</mtext>\n</mtd>\n</mtr>\n<mtr>\n<mtd columnalign=\"left\">\n<msub>\n<mi>R</mi>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>max</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</msub>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>2.625</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mo>×</mo>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<msup>\n<mn>10</mn>\n<mn>5</mn>\n</msup>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>Ω</mtext>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mo>,</mo>\n<mspace width=\"0.8em\"></mspace>\n<msub>\n<mi>I</mi>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>max</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</msub>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>11.43</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mi>μ</mi>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>A</mtext>\n</mtd>\n</mtr>\n</mtable>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 51. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170903858880\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
