    "prompt": "Show that, as explained in the text, a force F ⊥ exerted on a flexible medium at its center and perpendicular to its length (such as on the tightrope wire in Figure 5.26 ) gives rise to…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Show that, as explained in the text, a force <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>⊥</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> exerted on a flexible medium at its center and perpendicular to its length (such as on the tightrope wire in <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-6-common-forces\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Figure 5.26</a>) gives rise to a tension of magnitude <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>⊥</mo></msub></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><mn>2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>sin</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Show that, as explained in the text, a force <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>⊥</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> exerted on a flexible medium at its center and perpendicular to its length (such as on the tightrope wire in <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-6-common-forces\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Figure 5.26</a>) gives rise to a tension of magnitude <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>⊥</mo></msub></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><mn>2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>sin</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-problems#fs-id1165038377577",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1165038377577-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows a horizontal line parallel to x axis. An arrow F pointing downwards originates from the center of the line, with its tip intersecting x-axis. Two arrows originate from this point of intersection and their tips touch the line on either side. They form the same angle with the x-axis and the line.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/3db05beec8fe4872f4dfa9fc.jpg\"/>\n</span><p><span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mtable><mtr></mtr><mtr></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>net</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>⊥</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>sin</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>⊥</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi><mtext>sin</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>θ</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mo>⊥</mo></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>sin</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 61. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-problems#fs-id1165038377577\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
