    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Power",
    "prompt": "An electron in a television tube is accelerated uniformly from rest to a speed of 8.4 × 10 7 m/s over a distance of 2.5 cm. What is the power delivered to the electron at the instant…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>An electron in a television tube is accelerated uniformly from rest to a speed of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>8.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> over a distance of 2.5 cm. What is the power delivered to the electron at the instant that its displacement is 1.0 cm?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>An electron in a television tube is accelerated uniformly from rest to a speed of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>8.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> over a distance of 2.5 cm. What is the power delivered to the electron at the instant that its displacement is 1.0 cm?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165036891514",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-7#fs-id1165036891514-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mn>6.83</mn>\n<mtext>μW</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 79. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-problems#fs-id1165036891514\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
