    "topic": "Momentum and collisions",
    "prompt": "Two hockey players approach each other head on, each traveling at the same speed v i . They collide and get tangled together, falling down and moving off at a speed v i / 5 . What is the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Two hockey players approach each other head on, each traveling at the same speed <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>i</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. They collide and get tangled together, falling down and moving off at a speed <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>i</mtext></msub></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the ratio of their masses?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Two hockey players approach each other head on, each traveling at the same speed <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>i</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. They collide and get tangled together, falling down and moving off at a speed <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>i</mtext></msub></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the ratio of their masses?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-additional-problems#fs-id1167132230395",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 93. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-additional-problems#fs-id1167132230395\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
