    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Magnetic Field Due to a Thin Straight Wire",
    "prompt": "A long, straight, horizontal wire carries a left-to-right current of 20 A. If the wire is placed in a uniform magnetic field of magnitude 4.0 × 10 −5 T that is directed vertically…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A long, straight, horizontal wire carries a left-to-right current of 20 A. If the wire is placed in a uniform magnetic field of magnitude <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mtext>−5</mtext></mrow></msup><mtext>T</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> that is directed vertically downward, what is the resultant magnitude of the magnetic field 20 cm above the wire? 20 cm below the wire?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A long, straight, horizontal wire carries a left-to-right current of 20 A. If the wire is placed in a uniform magnetic field of magnitude <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mtext>−5</mtext></mrow></msup><mtext>T</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> that is directed vertically downward, what is the resultant magnitude of the magnetic field 20 cm above the wire? 20 cm below the wire?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/12-problems#fs-id1166168204152",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-12#fs-id1166168204152-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>Both answers have the magnitude of magnetic field of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mtext>−5</mtext></mrow></msup><mtext>T</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 12, Problem 25. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/12-problems#fs-id1166168204152\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
