    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Electric charge and fields",
    "prompt": "A charge q = −2.0 μ C is released from rest when it is 2.0 m from a fixed charge Q = 6.0 μ C . What is the kinetic energy of q when it is 1.0 m from Q ?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A charge <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>−2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is released from rest when it is 2.0 m from a fixed charge <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the kinetic energy of <em>q</em> when it is 1.0 m from <em>Q</em>?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A charge <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>−2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is released from rest when it is 2.0 m from a fixed charge <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the kinetic energy of <em>q</em> when it is 1.0 m from <em>Q</em>?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-additional-problems#fs-id1172093796129",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1172093796129-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>W</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0.054</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>J</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 113. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-additional-problems#fs-id1172093796129\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
