    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Free Fall",
    "prompt": "Calculate the displacement and velocity at times of (a) 0.500 s, (b) 1.00 s, (c) 1.50 s, (d) 2.00 s, and (e) 2.50 s for a rock thrown straight down with an initial velocity of 14.0 m/s…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Calculate the displacement and velocity at times of (a) 0.500 s, (b) 1.00 s, (c) 1.50 s, (d) 2.00 s, and (e) 2.50 s for a rock thrown straight down with an initial velocity of 14.0 m/s from the Verrazano Narrows Bridge in New York City. The roadway of this bridge is 70.0 m above the water.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Calculate the displacement and velocity at times of (a) 0.500 s, (b) 1.00 s, (c) 1.50 s, (d) 2.00 s, and (e) 2.50 s for a rock thrown straight down with an initial velocity of 14.0 m/s from the Verrazano Narrows Bridge in New York City. The roadway of this bridge is 70.0 m above the water.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168328277363",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-3#fs-id1168328277363-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mtable><mtr></mtr><mtr></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>−8.23</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mn>18.9</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nb. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mtable><mtr></mtr><mtr></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>−18.9</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>−23.8</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nc. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mtable><mtr></mtr><mtr></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>−32.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mn>28.7</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nd. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mtable><mtr></mtr><mtr></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>−47.6</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mn>33.6</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\ne. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mtable><mtr></mtr><mtr></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>−65.6</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mn>38.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></semantics></math></span></p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 3, Problem 67. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168328277363\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
