    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Newton’s Second Law for Rotation",
    "prompt": "A block of mass 3 kg slides down an inclined plane at an angle of 45 ° with a massless tether attached to a pulley with mass 1 kg and radius 0.5 m at the top of the incline (see the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A block of mass 3 kg slides down an inclined plane at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>45</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with a massless tether attached to a pulley with mass 1 kg and radius 0.5 m at the top of the incline (see the following figure). The pulley can be approximated as a disk. The coefficient of kinetic friction on the plane is 0.4. What is the acceleration of the block?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A block of mass 3 kg slides down an inclined plane at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>45</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with a massless tether attached to a pulley with mass 1 kg and radius 0.5 m at the top of the incline (see the following figure). The pulley can be approximated as a disk. The coefficient of kinetic friction on the plane is 0.4. What is the acceleration of the block?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows a block that slides down an inclined plane at an angle of 45 degrees with a tether attached to a pulley.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/0d300e45da26a2734a981edb.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-problems#fs-id1167131112903",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-10#fs-id1167131112903-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>a</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>3.6</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>m</mtext>\n<mtext>/</mtext>\n<mrow>\n<msup>\n<mtext>s</mtext>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 93. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-problems#fs-id1167131112903\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
