    "topic": "Electric potential",
    "prompt": "A glass ring of radius 5.0 cm is painted with a charged paint such that the charge density around the ring varies continuously given by the following function of the polar angle θ , λ =…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A glass ring of radius 5.0 cm is painted with a charged paint such that the charge density around the ring varies continuously given by the following function of the polar angle <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>3.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−6</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C/m</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cos</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Find the potential at a point 15 cm above the center.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A glass ring of radius 5.0 cm is painted with a charged paint such that the charge density around the ring varies continuously given by the following function of the polar angle <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>3.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−6</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C/m</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cos</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Find the potential at a point 15 cm above the center.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-additional-problems#fs-id1167586269363",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 92. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-additional-problems#fs-id1167586269363\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
