    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Rotation",
    "prompt": "A cyclist is riding such that the wheels of the bicycle have a rotation rate of 3.0 rev/s. If the cyclist brakes such that the rotation rate of the wheels decrease at a rate of 0.3 rev /…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A cyclist is riding such that the wheels of the bicycle have a rotation rate of 3.0 rev/s. If the cyclist brakes such that the rotation rate of the wheels decrease at a rate of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>rev</mtext></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, how long does it take for the cyclist to come to a complete stop?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A cyclist is riding such that the wheels of the bicycle have a rotation rate of 3.0 rev/s. If the cyclist brakes such that the rotation rate of the wheels decrease at a rate of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>rev</mtext></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, how long does it take for the cyclist to come to a complete stop?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1167134872487",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-10#fs-id1167134872487-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>Δ</mtext>\n<mi>t</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>10.0</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>s</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 107. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1167134872487\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
