    "topic": "Calculating Electric Fields of Charge Distributions",
    "prompt": "The charge per unit length on the thin semicircular wire shown below is λ . What is the electric field at the point P ?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The charge per unit length on the thin semicircular wire shown below is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the electric field at the point <em>P</em>?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The charge per unit length on the thin semicircular wire shown below is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the electric field at the point <em>P</em>?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"A semicircular arc of radius r is shown. The arc has total charge q. Point P is at the center of the circle of which the arc is a part.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/301324b7c292faf825126437.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
