    "topic": "Work and energy",
    "prompt": "Consider a particle on which a force acts that depends on the position of the particle. This force is given by F → 1 = ( 2 y ) i ^ + ( 3 x ) j ^ . Find the work done by this force when…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Consider a particle on which a force acts that depends on the position of the particle. This force is given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Find the work done by this force when the particle moves from the origin to a point 5 meters to the right on the <em>x</em>-axis.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Consider a particle on which a force acts that depends on the position of the particle. This force is given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Find the work done by this force when the particle moves from the origin to a point 5 meters to the right on the <em>x</em>-axis.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-additional-problems#fs-id1165036775783",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 88. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/7-additional-problems#fs-id1165036775783\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
