    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Momentum and collisions",
    "prompt": "Two carts on a straight track collide head on. The first cart was moving at 3.6 m/s in the positive x direction and the second was moving at 2.4 m/s in the opposite direction. After the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Two carts on a straight track collide head on. The first cart was moving at 3.6 m/s in the positive <em>x</em> direction and the second was moving at 2.4 m/s in the opposite direction. After the collision, the second car continues moving in its initial direction of motion at 0.24 m/s. If the mass of the second car is 5.0 times that of the first, what is the final velocity of the first car?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Two carts on a straight track collide head on. The first cart was moving at 3.6 m/s in the positive <em>x</em> direction and the second was moving at 2.4 m/s in the opposite direction. After the collision, the second car continues moving in its initial direction of motion at 0.24 m/s. If the mass of the second car is 5.0 times that of the first, what is the final velocity of the first car?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-additional-problems#fs-id1167132411513",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-9#fs-id1167132411513-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>−</mtext>\n<mrow>\n<mo>(</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>7.2</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>m/s</mtext>\n</mrow>\n<mo>)</mo>\n</mrow>\n<mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\">\n<mover accent=\"true\">\n<mi>i</mi>\n<mo>^</mo>\n</mover>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 96. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-additional-problems#fs-id1167132411513\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
