    "type": "FRQ",
    "level": 1,
    "imported": true,
    "source": "OpenStax",
    "volume": 1,
    "chapter": 3,
    "number": 71,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Free Fall",
    "prompt": "A diver bounces straight up from a diving board, avoiding the diving board on the way down, and falls feet first into a pool. She starts with a velocity of 4.00 m/s and her takeoff point…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A diver bounces straight up from a diving board, avoiding the diving board on the way down, and falls feet first into a pool. She starts with a velocity of 4.00 m/s and her takeoff point is 1.80 m above the pool. (a) What is her highest point above the board? (b) How long a time are her feet in the air? (c) What is her velocity when her feet hit the water?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A diver bounces straight up from a diving board, avoiding the diving board on the way down, and falls feet first into a pool. She starts with a velocity of 4.00 m/s and her takeoff point is 1.80 m above the pool. (a) What is her highest point above the board? (b) How long a time are her feet in the air? (c) What is her velocity when her feet hit the water?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168327942440",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-3#fs-id1168327942440-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>s</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>9.80</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.82</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; b. to the apex <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.41</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> times 2 to the board = 0.82 s from the board to the water <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>−1.80</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>−1.8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4.9</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mn>4.9</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1.80</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, solution to quadratic equation gives 1.13 s; c. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><mtext>s</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>−1.80</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7.16</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 3, Problem 71. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-problems#fs-id1168327942440\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
