    "source": "OpenStax",
    "volume": 1,
    "chapter": 12,
    "number": 25,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Conditions for Static Equilibrium",
    "prompt": "When opening a door, you push on it perpendicularly with a force of 55.0 N at a distance of 0.850 m from the hinges. What torque are you exerting relative to the hinges?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>When opening a door, you push on it perpendicularly with a force of 55.0 N at a distance of 0.850 m from the hinges. What torque are you exerting relative to the hinges?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>When opening a door, you push on it perpendicularly with a force of 55.0 N at a distance of 0.850 m from the hinges. What torque are you exerting relative to the hinges?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-problems#fs-id1163713149954",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-12#fs-id1163713149954-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mn>46.8</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>N</mtext>\n<mo>·</mo>\n<mtext>m</mtext>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 12, Problem 25. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-problems#fs-id1163713149954\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
