    "topic": "Electromagnetic induction",
    "prompt": "A circular loop of wire of radius 10 cm is mounted on a vertical shaft and rotated at a frequency of 5 cycles per second in a region of uniform magnetic field of 2 Gauss perpendicular to…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A circular loop of wire of radius 10 cm is mounted on a vertical shaft and rotated at a frequency of 5 cycles per second in a region of uniform magnetic field of 2 Gauss perpendicular to the axis of rotation. (a) Find an expression for the time-dependent flux through the ring. (b) Determine the time-dependent current through the ring if it has a resistance of 10 <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Ω</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A circular loop of wire of radius 10 cm is mounted on a vertical shaft and rotated at a frequency of 5 cycles per second in a region of uniform magnetic field of 2 Gauss perpendicular to the axis of rotation. (a) Find an expression for the time-dependent flux through the ring. (b) Determine the time-dependent current through the ring if it has a resistance of 10 <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Ω</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows a circular loop of wire mounted on a vertical shaft and rotated in a region of uniform magnetic field perpendicular to the axis of rotation.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/d76cfe619e8cd28937a3f3c1.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-additional-problems#fs-id1171242457536",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 70. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-additional-problems#fs-id1171242457536\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
