    "topic": "Momentum and collisions",
    "prompt": "Derive the equations giving the final speeds for two objects that collide elastically, with the mass of the objects being m 1 and m 2 and the initial speeds being v 1,i and v 2,i = 0…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Derive the equations giving the final speeds for two objects that collide elastically, with the mass of the objects being <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and the initial speeds being <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mtext>1,i</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mtext>2,i</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (i.e., second object is initially stationary).</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Derive the equations giving the final speeds for two objects that collide elastically, with the mass of the objects being <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and the initial speeds being <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mtext>1,i</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mtext>2,i</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (i.e., second object is initially stationary).</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-additional-problems#fs-id1167132227134",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-9#fs-id1167132227134-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<msub>\n<mi>v</mi>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>1,f</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</msub>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<msub>\n<mi>v</mi>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>1,i</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</msub>\n<mfrac>\n<mrow>\n<msub>\n<mi>m</mi>\n<mn>1</mn>\n</msub>\n<mo>−</mo>\n<msub>\n<mi>m</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msub>\n</mrow>\n<mrow>\n<msub>\n<mi>m</mi>\n<mn>1</mn>\n</msub>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<msub>\n<mi>m</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msub>\n</mrow>\n</mfrac>\n<mo>,</mo>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<msub>\n<mi>v</mi>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>2,f</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</msub>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<msub>\n<mi>v</mi>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>1,i</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</msub>\n<mfrac>\n<mrow>\n<mn>2</mn>\n<msub>\n<mi>m</mi>\n<mn>1</mn>\n</msub>\n</mrow>\n<mrow>\n<msub>\n<mi>m</mi>\n<mn>1</mn>\n</msub>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<msub>\n<mi>m</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msub>\n</mrow>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 98. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-additional-problems#fs-id1167132227134\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
