    "prompt": "Calculate the mass of the Sun based on data for average Earth’s orbit and compare the value obtained with the Sun’s commonly listed value of 1.989 × 10 30 kg .",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Calculate the mass of the Sun based on data for average Earth’s orbit and compare the value obtained with the Sun’s commonly listed value of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.989</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Calculate the mass of the Sun based on data for average Earth’s orbit and compare the value obtained with the Sun’s commonly listed value of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.989</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-problems#fs-id1168329105797",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-13#fs-id1168329105797-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.98</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; The values are the same within 0.05%.</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 47. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-problems#fs-id1168329105797\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
