    "topic": "Self-Inductance and Inductors",
    "prompt": "Suppose that a rectangular toroid has 2000 windings and a self-inductance of 0.040 H. If h = 0.10 m , what is the ratio of its outer radius to its inner radius?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Suppose that a rectangular toroid has 2000 windings and a self-inductance of 0.040 H. If <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, what is the ratio of its outer radius to its inner radius?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Suppose that a rectangular toroid has 2000 windings and a self-inductance of 0.040 H. If <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, what is the ratio of its outer radius to its inner radius?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows the cross section of a toroid. The inner radius of the ring is R1 and the outer radius is R2. The height of the rectangular cross section is h. A small section of thickness dr is located at the center of the rectangular cross section. This is at a distance r from the center of the ring. The area within the rectangular cross section with thickness dr and height h is highlighted and labeled da. Field lines and current i flowing through the toroid are shown.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/1ae54f8d1a2187714bee8a31.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-problems#fs-id1167133579828",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 14, Problem 44. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-problems#fs-id1167133579828\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
