    "prompt": "Three charges are positioned at the corners of a parallelogram as shown below. (a) If Q = 8.0 μ C , what is the electric field at the unoccupied corner? (b) What is the force on a 5.0 -…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Three charges are positioned at the corners of a parallelogram as shown below. (a) If <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> what is the electric field at the unoccupied corner? (b) What is the force on a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> charge placed at this corner?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Three charges are positioned at the corners of a parallelogram as shown below. (a) If <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> what is the electric field at the unoccupied corner? (b) What is the force on a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> charge placed at this corner?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Three charges are positioned at the corners of a parallelogram. The top and bottom of the parallelogram are horizontal and are 3.0 meters long. The sides are at a thirty degree angle to the x axis. The vertical height of the parallelogram is 1.0 meter. The charges are a positive Q in the lower left corner, positive 2 Q in the lower right corner, and negative 3 Q in the upper left corner.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/4002fe316a71cf3c0112dd32.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-additional-problems#fs-id1172098529180",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 118. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-additional-problems#fs-id1172098529180\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
