    "topic": "Electromagnetic induction",
    "prompt": "The magnetic field between the poles of a horseshoe electromagnet is uniform and has a cylindrical symmetry about an axis from the middle of the South Pole to the middle of the North…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The magnetic field between the poles of a horseshoe electromagnet is uniform and has a cylindrical symmetry about an axis from the middle of the South Pole to the middle of the North Pole. The magnitude of the magnetic field changes as a rate of <em>dB</em>/<em>dt</em> due to the changing current through the electromagnet. Determine the electric field at a distance r from the center.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The magnetic field between the poles of a horseshoe electromagnet is uniform and has a cylindrical symmetry about an axis from the middle of the South Pole to the middle of the North Pole. The magnitude of the magnetic field changes as a rate of <em>dB</em>/<em>dt</em> due to the changing current through the electromagnet. Determine the electric field at a distance r from the center.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-additional-problems#fs-id1171242550092",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-13#fs-id1171242550092-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mo>(</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mrow>\n<mi>d</mi>\n<mi>B</mi>\n</mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>d</mi>\n<mi>t</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n<mo>)</mo>\n</mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mi>A</mi>\n<mrow>\n<mn>2</mn>\n<mi>π</mi>\n<mi>r</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 71. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/13-additional-problems#fs-id1171242550092\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
