    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Projectile Motion",
    "prompt": "The Lunar Roving Vehicle used in NASA’s late Apollo missions reached an unofficial lunar land speed of 5.0 m/s by astronaut Eugene Cernan. If the rover was moving at this speed on a flat…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The Lunar Roving Vehicle used in NASA’s late <em>Apollo</em> missions reached an unofficial lunar land speed of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> by astronaut Eugene Cernan. If the rover was moving at this speed on a flat lunar surface and hit a small bump that projected it off the surface at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mtext>°</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> how long would it be “airborne” on the Moon?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The Lunar Roving Vehicle used in NASA’s late <em>Apollo</em> missions reached an unofficial lunar land speed of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> by astronaut Eugene Cernan. If the rover was moving at this speed on a flat lunar surface and hit a small bump that projected it off the surface at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mtext>°</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> how long would it be “airborne” on the Moon?</p></div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165167697338",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 4, Problem 54. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165167697338\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
