    "topic": "Calculating Electric Fields of Charge Distributions",
    "prompt": "A rod bent into the arc of a circle subtends an angle 2 θ at the center P of the circle (see below). If the rod is charged uniformly with a total charge Q , what is the electric field at P ?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A rod bent into the arc of a circle subtends an angle <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> at the center <em>P</em> of the circle (see below). If the rod is charged uniformly with a total charge <em>Q</em>, what is the electric field at <em>P</em>?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A rod bent into the arc of a circle subtends an angle <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> at the center <em>P</em> of the circle (see below). If the rod is charged uniformly with a total charge <em>Q</em>, what is the electric field at <em>P</em>?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"An arc that is part of a circle of radius R and with center P is shown. The arc extends from an angle theta to the left of vertical to an angle theta to the right of vertical.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/b3cafbd1e82c7676fabb3950.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172100559867",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 90. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172100559867\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
