    "topic": "Forces and motion",
    "prompt": "A boater and motor boat are at rest on a lake. Together, they have mass 200.0 kg. If the thrust of the motor is a constant force of 40.0 N in the direction of motion, and if the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A boater and motor boat are at rest on a lake. Together, they have mass 200.0 kg. If the thrust of the motor is a constant force of 40.0 N in the direction of motion, and if the resistive force of the water is numerically equivalent to 2 times the speed <em>v</em> of the boat, set up and solve the differential equation to find: (a) the velocity of the boat at time <em>t</em>; (b) the limiting velocity (the velocity after a long time has passed).</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A boater and motor boat are at rest on a lake. Together, they have mass 200.0 kg. If the thrust of the motor is a constant force of 40.0 N in the direction of motion, and if the resistive force of the water is numerically equivalent to 2 times the speed <em>v</em> of the boat, set up and solve the differential equation to find: (a) the velocity of the boat at time <em>t</em>; (b) the limiting velocity (the velocity after a long time has passed).</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-challenge-problems#fs-id1165035685642",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-6#fs-id1165035685642-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20.0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>−0.01</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>;</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mtext>limiting</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 135. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-challenge-problems#fs-id1165035685642\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
