    "topic": "Electric charge and fields",
    "prompt": "A positive charge q is released from rest at the origin of a rectangular coordinate system and moves under the influence of the electric field E → = E 0 ( 1 + x / a ) i ^ . What is the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A positive charge <em>q</em> is released from rest at the origin of a rectangular coordinate system and moves under the influence of the electric field <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>E</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mtext>/</mtext><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the kinetic energy of <em>q</em> when it passes through <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A positive charge <em>q</em> is released from rest at the origin of a rectangular coordinate system and moves under the influence of the electric field <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>E</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mtext>/</mtext><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the kinetic energy of <em>q</em> when it passes through <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-additional-problems#fs-id1172100650088",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1172100650088-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mtext>/</mtext><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>15</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>J</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 119. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-additional-problems#fs-id1172100650088\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
