    "topic": "Rotation",
    "prompt": "A system of point particles is rotating about a fixed axis at 4 rev/s. The particles are fixed with respect to each other. The masses and distances to the axis of the point particles are…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A system of point particles is rotating about a fixed axis at 4 rev/s. The particles are fixed with respect to each other. The masses and distances to the axis of the point particles are <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (a) What is the moment of inertia of the system? (b) What is the rotational kinetic energy of the system?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A system of point particles is rotating about a fixed axis at 4 rev/s. The particles are fixed with respect to each other. The masses and distances to the axis of the point particles are <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (a) What is the moment of inertia of the system? (b) What is the rotational kinetic energy of the system?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1167134990874",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 112. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1167134990874\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
