    "topic": "Kepler's Laws of Planetary Motion",
    "prompt": "The perihelion of Halley’s comet is 0.586 AU and the aphelion is 17.8 AU. Given that its speed at perihelion is 55 km/s, what is the speed at aphelion ( 1 AU = 1.496 × 10 11 m )? ( Hint:…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The perihelion of Halley’s comet is 0.586 AU and the aphelion is 17.8 AU. Given that its speed at perihelion is 55 km/s, what is the speed at aphelion (<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>AU</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1.496</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>)? (<em>Hint:</em> You may use either conservation of energy or angular momentum, but the latter is much easier.)</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The perihelion of Halley’s comet is 0.586 AU and the aphelion is 17.8 AU. Given that its speed at perihelion is 55 km/s, what is the speed at aphelion (<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>AU</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1.496</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>)? (<em>Hint:</em> You may use either conservation of energy or angular momentum, but the latter is much easier.)</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-problems#fs-id1168329196621",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 50. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-problems#fs-id1168329196621\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
