    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Energy in a Magnetic Field",
    "prompt": "At the instant a current of 0.20 A is flowing through a coil of wire, the energy stored in its magnetic field is 6.0 × 10 −3 J . What is the self-inductance of the coil?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>At the instant a current of 0.20 A is flowing through a coil of wire, the energy stored in its magnetic field is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>J</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the self-inductance of the coil?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>At the instant a current of 0.20 A is flowing through a coil of wire, the energy stored in its magnetic field is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>J</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the self-inductance of the coil?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-problems#fs-id1167131117623",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 14, Problem 46. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-problems#fs-id1167131117623\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
