    "topic": "Electric potential",
    "prompt": "Calculate the angular velocity ω of an electron orbiting a proton in the hydrogen atom, given the radius of the orbit is 0.530 × 10 −10 m . You may assume that the proton is stationary…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Calculate the angular velocity <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> of an electron orbiting a proton in the hydrogen atom, given the radius of the orbit is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.530</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−10</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. You may assume that the proton is stationary and the centripetal force is supplied by Coulomb attraction.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Calculate the angular velocity <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> of an electron orbiting a proton in the hydrogen atom, given the radius of the orbit is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.530</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−10</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. You may assume that the proton is stationary and the centripetal force is supplied by Coulomb attraction.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-additional-problems#fs-id1167586272245",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 7, Problem 104. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/7-additional-problems#fs-id1167586272245\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
