    "topic": "Calculating Electric Fields of Charge Distributions",
    "prompt": "A spherical water droplet of radius 25 μ m carries an excess 250 electrons. What vertical electric field is needed to balance the gravitational force on the droplet at the surface of the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A spherical water droplet of radius <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>25</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> carries an excess 250 electrons. What vertical electric field is needed to balance the gravitational force on the droplet at the surface of the earth?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A spherical water droplet of radius <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>25</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> carries an excess 250 electrons. What vertical electric field is needed to balance the gravitational force on the droplet at the surface of the earth?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172098590845",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1172098590845-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−11</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.6</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>N</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 93. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172098590845\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
