    "number": 74,
    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Electromagnetic induction",
    "prompt": "The armature and field coils of a series-wound motor have a total resistance of 3.0 Ω . When connected to a 120-V source and running at normal speed, the motor draws 4.0 A. (a) How large…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The armature and field coils of a series-wound motor have a total resistance of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. When connected to a 120-V source and running at normal speed, the motor draws 4.0 A. (a) How large is the back emf? (b) What current will the motor draw just after it is turned on? Can you suggest a way to avoid this large initial current?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The armature and field coils of a series-wound motor have a total resistance of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. When connected to a 120-V source and running at normal speed, the motor draws 4.0 A. (a) How large is the back emf? (b) What current will the motor draw just after it is turned on? Can you suggest a way to avoid this large initial current?</p>\n</div>",
