    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Conservation of Angular Momentum",
    "prompt": "The centrifuge at NASA Ames Research Center has a radius of 8.8 m and can produce forces on its payload of 20 g s or 20 times the force of gravity on Earth. (a) What is the angular…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The centrifuge at NASA Ames Research Center has a radius of 8.8 m and can produce forces on its payload of 20 <em>g</em>s or 20 times the force of gravity on Earth. (a) What is the angular momentum of a 20-kg payload that experiences 10 <em>g</em>s in the centrifuge? (b) If the driver motor was turned off in (a) and the payload lost 10 kg, what would be its new spin rate, taking into account there are no frictional forces present?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The centrifuge at NASA Ames Research Center has a radius of 8.8 m and can produce forces on its payload of 20 <em>g</em>s or 20 times the force of gravity on Earth. (a) What is the angular momentum of a 20-kg payload that experiences 10 <em>g</em>s in the centrifuge? (b) If the driver motor was turned off in (a) and the payload lost 10 kg, what would be its new spin rate, taking into account there are no frictional forces present?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-problems#fs-id1165037975810",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 70. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-problems#fs-id1165037975810\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
