    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Electrical Energy and Power",
    "prompt": "A 0.50-W, 220 - Ω resistor carries the maximum current possible without damaging the resistor. If the current were reduced to half the value, what would be the power consumed?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A 0.50-W, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>220</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> resistor carries the maximum current possible without damaging the resistor. If the current were reduced to half the value, what would be the power consumed?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A 0.50-W, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>220</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> resistor carries the maximum current possible without damaging the resistor. If the current were reduced to half the value, what would be the power consumed?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170902304194",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 62. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170902304194\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
