    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Magnetic Field of a Current Loop",
    "prompt": "Two flat, circular coils, each with a radius R and wound with N turns, are mounted along the same axis so that they are parallel a distance d apart. What is the magnetic field at the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Two flat, circular coils, each with a radius <em>R</em> and wound with <em>N</em> turns, are mounted along the same axis so that they are parallel a distance <em>d</em> apart. What is the magnetic field at the midpoint of the common axis if a current <em>I</em> flows in the same direction through each coil?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Two flat, circular coils, each with a radius <em>R</em> and wound with <em>N</em> turns, are mounted along the same axis so that they are parallel a distance <em>d</em> apart. What is the magnetic field at the midpoint of the common axis if a current <em>I</em> flows in the same direction through each coil?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/12-problems#fs-id1166167277513",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-12#fs-id1166167277513-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mi>I</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mtext>/</mtext><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>\n</p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 12, Problem 39. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/12-problems#fs-id1166167277513\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
