    "topic": "Electric charge and fields",
    "prompt": "The circular arc shown below carries a charge per unit length λ = λ 0 cos θ , where θ is measured from the x -axis. What is the electric field at the origin?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The circular arc shown below carries a charge per unit length <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cos</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> is measured from the <em>x</em>-axis. What is the electric field at the origin?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The circular arc shown below carries a charge per unit length <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cos</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> is measured from the <em>x</em>-axis. What is the electric field at the origin?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"An arc that is part of a circle of radius r and with center at the origin of an x y coordinate system is shown. The arc extends from an angle theta sub zero above the x axis to an angle theta sub zero below the x axis.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/b1aff8c3cecf002808bec9b7.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-additional-problems#fs-id1172098268523",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 122. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-additional-problems#fs-id1172098268523\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
