    "prompt": "Consider a power plant is located 60 km away from a residential area uses 0-gauge ( A = 42.40 mm 2 ) wire of copper to transmit power at a current of I = 100.00 A . How much more power…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Consider a power plant is located 60 km away from a residential area uses 0-gauge <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>42.40</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>mm</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> wire of copper to transmit power at a current of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. How much more power is dissipated in the copper wires than it would be in superconducting wires?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Consider a power plant is located 60 km away from a residential area uses 0-gauge <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>42.40</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>mm</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> wire of copper to transmit power at a current of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. How much more power is dissipated in the copper wires than it would be in superconducting wires?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170903033483",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-9#fs-id1170903033483-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mtable>\n<mtr></mtr>\n<mtr></mtr>\n<mtr></mtr>\n<mtr></mtr>\n<mtr>\n<mtd columnalign=\"left\">\n<msub>\n<mi>R</mi>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>copper</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</msub>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>23.77</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>Ω</mtext>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n</mtd>\n</mtr>\n<mtr>\n<mtd columnalign=\"left\">\n<mi>P</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>2.377</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mo>×</mo>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<msup>\n<mn>10</mn>\n<mn>5</mn>\n</msup>\n<mtext>W</mtext>\n</mtd>\n</mtr>\n</mtable>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 63. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170903033483\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
