    "prompt": "A current I flows around the rectangular loop shown in the accompanying figure. Evaluate ∮ B → · d l → for the paths A , B , C , and D .",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A current <em>I</em> flows around the rectangular loop shown in the accompanying figure. Evaluate <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle><mrow><mo>∮</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mstyle><mo>·</mo><mi>d</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> for the paths <em>A</em>, <em>B</em>, <em>C</em>, and <em>D</em>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A current <em>I</em> flows around the rectangular loop shown in the accompanying figure. Evaluate <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle><mrow><mo>∮</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mstyle><mo>·</mo><mi>d</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> for the paths <em>A</em>, <em>B</em>, <em>C</em>, and <em>D</em>.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows rectangular loop carrying current I. Paths A and C intersect with the short sides of the loop. Path B intersects with the two long sides of the loop. Path D intersects both with the short and the long sides of the loop.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/54723548051d12d4f295f632.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/12-problems#fs-id1166166206191",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-12#fs-id1166166206191-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi><mo>;</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> b. 0; c. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi><mo>;</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> d. 0</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 12, Problem 41. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/12-problems#fs-id1166166206191\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
