    "prompt": "A 10-H inductor carries a current of 20 A. How much ice at 0 ° C could be melted by the energy stored in the magnetic field of the inductor? ( Hint : Use the value L f = 334 J/g for ice.)",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A 10-H inductor carries a current of 20 A. How much ice at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mtext>°</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> could be melted by the energy stored in the magnetic field of the inductor? (<em>Hint</em>: Use the value <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>f</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>334</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>J/g</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> for ice.)</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A 10-H inductor carries a current of 20 A. How much ice at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mtext>°</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> could be melted by the energy stored in the magnetic field of the inductor? (<em>Hint</em>: Use the value <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>f</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>334</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>J/g</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> for ice.)</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-problems#fs-id1167131259494",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-14#fs-id1167131259494-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>6.0 g</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 14, Problem 49. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-problems#fs-id1167131259494\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
