    "topic": "Magnetic forces",
    "prompt": "Two particles have the same linear momentum, but particle A has four times the charge of particle B. If both particles move in a plane perpendicular to a uniform magnetic field, what is…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Two particles have the same linear momentum, but particle A has four times the charge of particle B. If both particles move in a plane perpendicular to a uniform magnetic field, what is the ratio <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mtext>/</mtext><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> of the radii of their circular orbits?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Two particles have the same linear momentum, but particle A has four times the charge of particle B. If both particles move in a plane perpendicular to a uniform magnetic field, what is the ratio <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mtext>/</mtext><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> of the radii of their circular orbits?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1171361477681",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-11#fs-id1171361477681-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>1/4</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 75. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1171361477681\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
