    "topic": "Self-Inductance and Inductors",
    "prompt": "The current shown in part (a) below is increasing, whereas that shown in part (b) is decreasing. In each case, determine which end of the inductor is at the higher potential.",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The current shown in part (a) below is increasing, whereas that shown in part (b) is decreasing. In each case, determine which end of the inductor is at the higher potential.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The current shown in part (a) below is increasing, whereas that shown in part (b) is decreasing. In each case, determine which end of the inductor is at the higher potential.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure a shows current flowing through a coil from left to right. Figure b shows current flowing through a coil from right to left.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/cf6222c1a2bb1e03070653a7.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
