    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Conservation of Energy",
    "prompt": "Assume that the force of a bow on an arrow behaves like the spring force. In aiming the arrow, an archer pulls the bow back 50 cm and holds it in position with a force of 150 N . If the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Assume that the force of a bow on an arrow behaves like the spring force. In aiming the arrow, an archer pulls the bow back 50 cm and holds it in position with a force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>150</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. If the mass of the arrow is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>g</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and the “spring” is massless, what is the speed of the arrow immediately after it leaves the bow?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Assume that the force of a bow on an arrow behaves like the spring force. In aiming the arrow, an archer pulls the bow back 50 cm and holds it in position with a force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>150</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. If the mass of the arrow is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>g</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and the “spring” is massless, what is the speed of the arrow immediately after it leaves the bow?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/8-problems#fs-id1165037260938",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-8#fs-id1165037260938-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mn>39</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>m</mtext>\n<mtext>/</mtext>\n<mtext>s</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 8, Problem 37. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/8-problems#fs-id1165037260938\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
