    "volume": 1,
    "chapter": 9,
    "number": 106,
    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Momentum and collisions",
    "prompt": "Two identical billiard balls collide. The first one is initially traveling at ( 2.2 m/s ) i ^ − ( 0.4 m/s ) j ^ and the second one at − ( 1.4 m/s ) i ^ + ( 2.4 m/s ) j ^ . Suppose they…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Two identical billiard balls collide. The first one is initially traveling at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>0.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and the second one at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Suppose they collide when the center of ball 1 is at the origin and the center of ball 2 is at the point <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <em>R</em> is the radius of the balls. What is the final velocity of each ball?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Two identical billiard balls collide. The first one is initially traveling at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>0.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and the second one at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Suppose they collide when the center of ball 1 is at the origin and the center of ball 2 is at the point <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <em>R</em> is the radius of the balls. What is the final velocity of each ball?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-additional-problems#fs-id1167133403316",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-9#fs-id1167133403316-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>ball 1: <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>0.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, ball 2: <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 106. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/9-additional-problems#fs-id1167133403316\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
