    "previewHTML": "<p>Two infinite rods, each carrying a uniform charge density <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> are parallel to one another and perpendicular to the plane of the page. (See below.) What is the electrical field at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>?</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>At</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Two infinite rods, each carrying a uniform charge density <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> are parallel to one another and perpendicular to the plane of the page. (See below.) What is the electrical field at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>?</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>At</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>?</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"An end view of the arrangement in the problem is shown. Two rods are parallel to one another and perpendicular to the plane of the page. They are separated by a horizontal distance of a. Pint P 1 is a distance of a over 2 above the midpoint between the rods, and so also a distance of a over 2 horizontally from each rod. Point P 2 is a distance of a to the right of the rightmost rod.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/6cb09ee6e0072963a9f9befa.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172098372410",
