    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Calculating Electric Fields of Charge Distributions",
    "prompt": "Positive charge is distributed with a uniform density λ along the positive x -axis from r to ∞ , along the positive y -axis from r to ∞ , and along a 90 ° arc of a circle of radius r ,…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Positive charge is distributed with a uniform density <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> along the positive <em>x</em>-axis from <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>to</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>∞</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> along the positive <em>y</em>-axis from <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>to</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>∞</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and along a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>90</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> arc of a circle of radius <em>r</em>, as shown below. What is the electric field at <em>O</em>?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Positive charge is distributed with a uniform density <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> along the positive <em>x</em>-axis from <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>to</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>∞</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> along the positive <em>y</em>-axis from <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>to</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>∞</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and along a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>90</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> arc of a circle of radius <em>r</em>, as shown below. What is the electric field at <em>O</em>?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"A uniform distribution of positive charges is shown on an x y coordinate system. The charges are distributed along a 90 degree arc of a circle of radius r in the first quadrant, centered on the origin. The distribution continues along the positive x and y axes from r to infinity.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/05fbb17eeb29ce386a8dcb78.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172098625840",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1172098625840-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>circular arc <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cos</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>E</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>sin</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>j</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>E</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>j</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\n<em>y</em>-axis: <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>E</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\n<em>x</em>-axis: <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>E</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>j</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,<span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>E</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>i</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mtext>j</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 97. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/5-problems#fs-id1172098625840\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
