    "level": 0,
    "imported": true,
    "source": "OpenStax",
    "volume": 2,
    "chapter": 9,
    "number": 65,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Superconductors",
    "prompt": "Digital medical thermometers determine temperature by measuring the resistance of a semiconductor device called a thermistor (which has α = −0.06 / ° C ) when it is at the same…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Digital medical thermometers determine temperature by measuring the resistance of a semiconductor device called a thermistor (which has <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>−0.06</mn><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>°</mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>) when it is at the same temperature as the patient. What is a patient’s temperature if the thermistor’s resistance at that temperature is 82.0% of its value at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>37</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°</mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (normal body temperature)?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Digital medical thermometers determine temperature by measuring the resistance of a semiconductor device called a thermistor (which has <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>−0.06</mn><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>°</mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>) when it is at the same temperature as the patient. What is a patient’s temperature if the thermistor’s resistance at that temperature is 82.0% of its value at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>37</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>°</mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (normal body temperature)?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170903141104",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-9#fs-id1170903141104-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mtable>\n<mtr>\n<mtd columnalign=\"left\">\n<mi>R</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<msub>\n<mi>R</mi>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</msub>\n<mrow>\n<mo>(</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>1</mn>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mi>α</mi>\n<mrow>\n<mo>(</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mi>T</mi>\n<mo>−</mo>\n<msub>\n<mi>T</mi>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</msub>\n</mrow>\n<mo>)</mo>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n<mo>)</mo>\n</mrow>\n</mtd>\n</mtr>\n<mtr>\n<mtd columnalign=\"left\">\n<mn>0.82</mn>\n<msub>\n<mi>R</mi>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</msub>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<msub>\n<mi>R</mi>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</msub>\n<mrow>\n<mo>(</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>1</mn>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mi>α</mi>\n<mrow>\n<mo>(</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mi>T</mi>\n<mo>−</mo>\n<msub>\n<mi>T</mi>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</msub>\n</mrow>\n<mo>)</mo>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n<mo>)</mo>\n</mrow>\n<mo>,</mo>\n<mspace width=\"0.8em\"></mspace>\n<mn>0.82</mn>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>1</mn>\n<mo>−</mo>\n<mn>0.06</mn>\n<mrow>\n<mo>(</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mi>T</mi>\n<mo>−</mo>\n<mn>37</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>°</mtext>\n<mtext>C</mtext>\n</mrow>\n<mo>)</mo>\n</mrow>\n<mo>,</mo>\n<mspace width=\"0.8em\"></mspace>\n<mi>T</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>40</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>°</mtext>\n<mtext>C</mtext>\n</mtd>\n</mtr>\n</mtable>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 9, Problem 65. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/9-problems#fs-id1170903141104\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
