    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Examples of Static Equilibrium",
    "prompt": "In order to get his car out of the mud, a man ties one end of a rope to the front bumper and the other end to a tree 15 m away, as shown below. He then pulls on the center of the rope…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>In order to get his car out of the mud, a man ties one end of a rope to the front bumper and the other end to a tree 15 m away, as shown below. He then pulls on the center of the rope with a force of 400 N, which causes its center to be displaced 0.30 m, as shown. What is the force of the rope on the car?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>In order to get his car out of the mud, a man ties one end of a rope to the front bumper and the other end to a tree 15 m away, as shown below. He then pulls on the center of the rope with a force of 400 N, which causes its center to be displaced 0.30 m, as shown. What is the force of the rope on the car?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure is a schematic drawing that shows a rope tied to the front bumper and the other end to a tree 15 m away. A force of 400 N is applied to the center of the rope and causes it to get displaced 0.30 m.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/cf33e7748dc702925175f0b7.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-problems#fs-id1163709714861",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 12, Problem 34. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-problems#fs-id1163709714861\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
