    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Angular momentum",
    "prompt": "A 4.0-kg particle moves in a circle of radius 2.0 m. The angular momentum of the particle varies in time according to l = 5.0 t 2 . (a) What is the torque on the particle about the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A 4.0-kg particle moves in a circle of radius 2.0 m. The angular momentum of the particle varies in time according to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) What is the torque on the particle about the center of the circle at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>? (b) What is the angular velocity of the particle at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A 4.0-kg particle moves in a circle of radius 2.0 m. The angular momentum of the particle varies in time according to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) What is the torque on the particle about the center of the circle at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>? (b) What is the angular velocity of the particle at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1165037914410",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-11#fs-id1165037914410-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>34.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext><mo>·</mo><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nb. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">⇒</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.6</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>rad</mtext></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 83. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1165037914410\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
