    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "RL Circuits",
    "prompt": "In Figure 14.12 , ε = 12 V , L = 20 mH , and R = 5.0 Ω . Determine (a) the time constant of the circuit, (b) the initial current through the resistor, (c) the final current through the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>In <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-4-rl-circuits\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Figure 14.12</a>, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>mH</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Determine (a) the time constant of the circuit, (b) the initial current through the resistor, (c) the final current through the resistor, (d) the current through the resistor when <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and (e) the voltages across the inductor and the resistor when <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>In <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-4-rl-circuits\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Figure 14.12</a>, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>mH</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Determine (a) the time constant of the circuit, (b) the initial current through the resistor, (c) the final current through the resistor, (d) the current through the resistor when <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and (e) the voltages across the inductor and the resistor when <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-problems#fs-id1167131375381",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 14, Problem 52. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-problems#fs-id1167131375381\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
