    "prompt": "What are the largest and smallest resistances you can obtain by connecting a 36.0 - Ω , a 50.0 - Ω , and a 700 - Ω resistor together?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>What are the largest and smallest resistances you can obtain by connecting a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>36.0</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>50.0</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>700</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> resistor together?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>What are the largest and smallest resistances you can obtain by connecting a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>36.0</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>50.0</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>700</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> resistor together?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-problems#fs-id1172100960090",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-10#fs-id1172100960090-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>largest, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>786</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, smallest, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20.32</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
