    "source": "OpenStax",
    "volume": 1,
    "chapter": 12,
    "number": 36,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Examples of Static Equilibrium",
    "prompt": "When the structure shown below is supported at point P , it is in equilibrium. Find the magnitude of force F and the force applied at P . The weight of the structure is negligible.",
    "previewHTML": "<p>When the structure shown below is supported at point <em>P</em>, it is in equilibrium. Find the magnitude of force <em>F</em> and the force applied at <em>P</em>. The weight of the structure is negligible.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>When the structure shown below is supported at point <em>P</em>, it is in equilibrium. Find the magnitude of force <em>F</em> and the force applied at <em>P</em>. The weight of the structure is negligible.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows the distribution of forces applied to point P. Force of 2000 N, two meters to the left of the point P, moves it downwards. Force F, two meters to the left and two meters above of the point P, moves it to the right. Force of 1000 N, two meters to the right and three meters below of the point P, moves it to the left.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/3f363d2fefaddad9290a46fc.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-problems#fs-id1163709657344",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 12, Problem 36. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-problems#fs-id1163709657344\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
