    "prompt": "The current in the RL circuit shown below reaches half its maximum value in 1.75 ms after the switch S 1 is thrown. Determine (a) the time constant of the circuit and (b) the resistance…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The current in the <em>RL</em> circuit shown below reaches half its maximum value in 1.75 ms after the switch <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>S</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is thrown. Determine (a) the time constant of the circuit and (b) the resistance of the circuit if <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>250</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>mH</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The current in the <em>RL</em> circuit shown below reaches half its maximum value in 1.75 ms after the switch <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>S</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is thrown. Determine (a) the time constant of the circuit and (b) the resistance of the circuit if <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>250</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>mH</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows a circuit with R and L in series with a battery, epsilon and a switch S1 which is open.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/286cf80c12694128cb278706.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-problems#fs-id1167131608371",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-14#fs-id1167131608371-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. 2.52 ms; b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>99.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 14, Problem 57. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-problems#fs-id1167131608371\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
