    "prompt": "The accompanying figure shows a cross-section of a long, hollow, cylindrical conductor of inner radius r 1 = 3.0 cm and outer radius r 2 = 5.0 cm . A 50-A current distributed uniformly…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The accompanying figure shows a cross-section of a long, hollow, cylindrical conductor of inner radius <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>3.0 cm</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and outer radius <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>5.0 cm</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> A 50-A current distributed uniformly over the cross-section flows into the page. Calculate the magnetic field at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>2.0 cm</mtext><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>6.0 cm</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The accompanying figure shows a cross-section of a long, hollow, cylindrical conductor of inner radius <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>3.0 cm</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and outer radius <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>5.0 cm</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> A 50-A current distributed uniformly over the cross-section flows into the page. Calculate the magnetic field at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>2.0 cm</mtext><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>6.0 cm</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows a cross-section of a long, hollow, cylindrical conductor with an inner radius of three centimeters and an outer radius of five centimeters.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/8da8c85fb2f63cd53167cf35.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/12-problems#fs-id1166167134535",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 12, Problem 46. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/12-problems#fs-id1166167134535\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
