    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Kinematics",
    "prompt": "A particle moves along the x -axis according to the equation x ( t ) = 2.0 − 4.0 t 2 m. What are the velocity and acceleration at t = 2.0 s and t = 5.0 s?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A particle moves along the <em>x</em>-axis according to the equation <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>4.0</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> m. What are the velocity and acceleration at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> s and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> s?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A particle moves along the <em>x</em>-axis according to the equation <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>4.0</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> m. What are the velocity and acceleration at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> s and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> s?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-additional-problems#fs-id1168055120900",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 3, Problem 86. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-additional-problems#fs-id1168055120900\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
