    "topic": "Newton’s laws",
    "prompt": "A sailboat has a mass of 1.50 × 10 3 kg and is acted on by a force of 2.00 × 10 3 N toward the east, while the wind acts behind the sails with a force of 3.00 × 10 3 N in a direction 45…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A sailboat has a mass of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> kg and is acted on by a force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> N toward the east, while the wind acts behind the sails with a force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> N in a direction <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>45</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> north of east. Find the magnitude and direction of the resulting acceleration.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A sailboat has a mass of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> kg and is acted on by a force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> N toward the east, while the wind acts behind the sails with a force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> N in a direction <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>45</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> north of east. Find the magnitude and direction of the resulting acceleration.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-additional-problems#fs-id1165039293018",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 78. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-additional-problems#fs-id1165039293018\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
