    "topic": "Examples of Static Equilibrium",
    "prompt": "The uniform boom shown below weighs 3000 N. It is supported by the horizontal guy wire and by the hinged support at point A . What are the forces on the boom due to the wire and due to…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The uniform boom shown below weighs 3000 N. It is supported by the horizontal guy wire and by the hinged support at point <em>A</em>. What are the forces on the boom due to the wire and due to the support at <em>A</em>? Does the force at <em>A</em> act along the boom?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The uniform boom shown below weighs 3000 N. It is supported by the horizontal guy wire and by the hinged support at point <em>A</em>. What are the forces on the boom due to the wire and due to the support at <em>A</em>? Does the force at <em>A</em> act along the boom?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure is a schematic drawing of a 2000 N weight that is supported by the horizontal guy wire and by the hinged support at point A. Hinged support forms a 45 degree angle with the ground.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/b8b707a2738e8aad9516cd3b.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-problems#fs-id1163709698344",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 12, Problem 40. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-problems#fs-id1163709698344\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
