    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Resistors in Series and Parallel",
    "prompt": "Referring to the example combining series and parallel circuits and Figure 10.16 , calculate I 3 in the following two different ways: (a) from the known values of I and I 2 ; (b) using…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Referring to the example combining series and parallel circuits and <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-2-resistors-in-series-and-parallel\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Figure 10.16</a>, calculate <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in the following two different ways: (a) from the known values of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; (b) using Ohm’s law for <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. In both parts, explicitly show how you follow the steps in the <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-2-resistors-in-series-and-parallel\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Series and Parallel Resistors</a>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Referring to the example combining series and parallel circuits and <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-2-resistors-in-series-and-parallel\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Figure 10.16</a>, calculate <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> in the following two different ways: (a) from the known values of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; (b) using Ohm’s law for <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. In both parts, explicitly show how you follow the steps in the <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-2-resistors-in-series-and-parallel\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Series and Parallel Resistors</a>.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-problems#fs-id1172100547970",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-10#fs-id1172100547970-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. 0.74 A; b. 0.742 A</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 31. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-problems#fs-id1172100547970\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
