    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Magnetic forces",
    "prompt": "A 1.0-m-long segment of wire lies along the x -axis and carries a current of 2.0 A in the positive x -direction. Around the wire is the magnetic field of ( 3.0 i ^ + 4.0 k ^ ) × 10 −3 T…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A 1.0-m-long segment of wire lies along the <em>x</em>-axis and carries a current of 2.0 A in the positive <em>x</em>-direction. Around the wire is the magnetic field of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>3.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>+</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mn>4.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>T</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Find the magnetic force on this segment.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A 1.0-m-long segment of wire lies along the <em>x</em>-axis and carries a current of 2.0 A in the positive <em>x</em>-direction. Around the wire is the magnetic field of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>3.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>+</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mn>4.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−3</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>T</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Find the magnetic force on this segment.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1171361663412",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 80. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1171361663412\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
