    "type": "FRQ",
    "level": 1,
    "imported": true,
    "source": "OpenStax",
    "volume": 2,
    "chapter": 14,
    "number": 59,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "RL Circuits",
    "prompt": "For the circuit shown below, ε = 50 V , R 1 = 10 Ω, , R 2 = R 3 = 19.4 Ω, , and L = 2.0 mH . Find the values of I 1 and I 2 (a) immediately after switch S is closed, (b) a long time…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>For the circuit shown below, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>19.4 Ω,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>mH</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Find the values of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) immediately after switch S is closed, (b) a long time after S is closed, (c) immediately after S is reopened, and (d) a long time after S is reopened.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>For the circuit shown below, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>19.4 Ω,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>mH</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Find the values of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) immediately after switch S is closed, (b) a long time after S is closed, (c) immediately after S is reopened, and (d) a long time after S is reopened.</p><span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows a circuit with R1 and R2 connected in series with a battery, epsilon and a closed switch S. R2 is connected in parallel with L and R3. The currents through R1 and R2 are I1 and I2 respectively.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/06d913b1a44189385ae8f773.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-problems#fs-id1167131567574",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-14#fs-id1167131567574-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.7</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.54</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.27</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; c. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.27</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; d. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 14, Problem 59. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-problems#fs-id1167131567574\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
