    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Centripetal Force",
    "prompt": "Railroad tracks follow a circular curve of radius 500.0 m and are banked at an angle of 5.0 ° . For trains of what speed are these tracks designed?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Railroad tracks follow a circular curve of radius 500.0 m and are banked at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. For trains of what speed are these tracks designed?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Railroad tracks follow a circular curve of radius 500.0 m and are banked at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. For trains of what speed are these tracks designed?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-problems#fs-id1165035610496",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-6#fs-id1165035610496-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>20.7 m/s</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 75. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-problems#fs-id1165035610496\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
