    "prompt": "Referring to Figure 10.16 , (a) Calculate P 3 and note how it compares with P 3 found in the first two example problems in this module. (b) Find the total power supplied by the source…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Referring to <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-2-resistors-in-series-and-parallel\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Figure 10.16</a>, (a) Calculate <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and note how it compares with <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> found in the first two example problems in this module. (b) Find the total power supplied by the source and compare it with the sum of the powers dissipated by the resistors.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Referring to <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-2-resistors-in-series-and-parallel\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Figure 10.16</a>, (a) Calculate <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and note how it compares with <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> found in the first two example problems in this module. (b) Find the total power supplied by the source and compare it with the sum of the powers dissipated by the resistors.</p>\n</div>",
