    "topic": "Potential Energy Diagrams and Stability",
    "prompt": "A single force F ( x ) = −4.0 x (in newtons) acts on a 1.0-kg body. When x = 3.5 m, the speed of the body is 4.0 m/s. What is its speed at x = 2.0 m?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A single force <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>−4.0</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (in newtons) acts on a 1.0-kg body. When <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> the speed of the body is 4.0 m/s. What is its speed at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m?</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A single force <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>−4.0</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (in newtons) acts on a 1.0-kg body. When <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> the speed of the body is 4.0 m/s. What is its speed at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m?</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/8-problems#fs-id1165038046554",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 8, Problem 46. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/8-problems#fs-id1165038046554\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
