    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Examples of Static Equilibrium",
    "prompt": "A uniform horizontal strut weighs 400.0 N. One end of the strut is attached to a hinged support at the wall, and the other end of the strut is attached to a sign that weighs 200.0 N. The…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A uniform horizontal strut weighs 400.0 N. One end of the strut is attached to a hinged support at the wall, and the other end of the strut is attached to a sign that weighs 200.0 N. The strut is also supported by a cable attached between the end of the strut and the wall. Assuming that the entire weight of the sign is attached at the very end of the strut, find the tension in the cable and the force at the hinge of the strut.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A uniform horizontal strut weighs 400.0 N. One end of the strut is attached to a hinged support at the wall, and the other end of the strut is attached to a sign that weighs 200.0 N. The strut is also supported by a cable attached between the end of the strut and the wall. Assuming that the entire weight of the sign is attached at the very end of the strut, find the tension in the cable and the force at the hinge of the strut.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure is a schematic drawing of a sign which hangs from the end of a uniform strut. The strut forms a 30 degree angle with the cable tied to the wall above the left end of the strut.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/e4cd842301eeead93df1b9d3.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-problems#fs-id1163713166376",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 12, Problem 38. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-problems#fs-id1163713166376\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
