    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Angular momentum",
    "prompt": "A boy stands at the center of a platform that is rotating without friction at 1.0 rev/s. The boy holds weights as far from his body as possible. At this position the total moment of…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A boy stands at the center of a platform that is rotating without friction at 1.0 rev/s. The boy holds weights as far from his body as possible. At this position the total moment of inertia of the boy, platform, and weights is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> The boy draws the weights in close to his body, thereby decreasing the total moment of inertia to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) What is the final angular velocity of the platform? (b) By how much does the rotational kinetic energy increase?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A boy stands at the center of a platform that is rotating without friction at 1.0 rev/s. The boy holds weights as far from his body as possible. At this position the total moment of inertia of the boy, platform, and weights is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> The boy draws the weights in close to his body, thereby decreasing the total moment of inertia to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) What is the final angular velocity of the platform? (b) By how much does the rotational kinetic energy increase?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1165037903736",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 90. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1165037903736\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
