    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Examples of Static Equilibrium",
    "prompt": "A 12.0-m boom, AB , of a crane lifting a 3000-kg load is shown below. The center of mass of the boom is at its geometric center, and the mass of the boom is 1000 kg. For the position…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A 12.0-m boom, <em>AB</em>, of a crane lifting a 3000-kg load is shown below. The center of mass of the boom is at its geometric center, and the mass of the boom is 1000 kg. For the position shown, calculate tension <em>T</em> in the cable and the force at the axle <em>A</em>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A 12.0-m boom, <em>AB</em>, of a crane lifting a 3000-kg load is shown below. The center of mass of the boom is at its geometric center, and the mass of the boom is 1000 kg. For the position shown, calculate tension <em>T</em> in the cable and the force at the axle <em>A</em>.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure is a schematic drawing of a crane lifting a 3000-kg load. Arm of a crane forms a 30 degree angle with the line parallel to the ground. Cable supporting load forms a 10 degree angle with the arm.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/9011065115dfa0580412f2b4.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-problems#fs-id1163709668129",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 12, Problem 42. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-problems#fs-id1163709668129\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
