    "type": "FRQ",
    "level": 1,
    "imported": true,
    "source": "OpenStax",
    "volume": 2,
    "chapter": 14,
    "number": 76,
    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Inductance",
    "prompt": "Suppose that a cylindrical solenoid is wrapped around a core of iron whose magnetic susceptibility is x . Using Equation 14.9 , show that the self-inductance of the solenoid is given by…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Suppose that a cylindrical solenoid is wrapped around a core of iron whose magnetic susceptibility is <strong><em>x</em></strong>. Using <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-2-self-inductance-and-inductors\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Equation 14.9</a>, show that the self-inductance of the solenoid is given by</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Suppose that a cylindrical solenoid is wrapped around a core of iron whose magnetic susceptibility is <strong><em>x</em></strong>. Using <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-2-self-inductance-and-inductors\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Equation 14.9</a>, show that the self-inductance of the solenoid is given by</p>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>L</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mfrac>\n<mrow>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mn>1</mn>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n<msub>\n<mi>μ</mi>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</msub>\n<msup>\n<mi>N</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n<mi>A</mi>\n</mrow>\n<mi>l</mi>\n</mfrac>\n<mo>,</mo>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n<p>where <em>l</em> is its length, <em>A</em> its cross-sectional area, and <em>N</em> its total number of turns.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-additional-problems#fs-id1167129970346",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 14, Problem 76. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-additional-problems#fs-id1167129970346\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
