    "topic": "Kinematics",
    "prompt": "An electron is moving in a straight line with a velocity of 4.0 × 10 5 m/s. It enters a region 5.0 cm long where it undergoes an acceleration of 6.0 × 10 12 m/s 2 along the same straight…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>An electron is moving in a straight line with a velocity of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> m/s. It enters a region 5.0 cm long where it undergoes an acceleration of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> along the same straight line. (a) What is the electron’s velocity when it emerges from this region? b) How long does the electron take to cross the region?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>An electron is moving in a straight line with a velocity of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> m/s. It enters a region 5.0 cm long where it undergoes an acceleration of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> along the same straight line. (a) What is the electron’s velocity when it emerges from this region? b) How long does the electron take to cross the region?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-additional-problems#fs-id1168055478200",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-3#fs-id1168055478200-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a.<span><br/></span><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8.7</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7.8</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 3, Problem 89. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-additional-problems#fs-id1168055478200\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
