    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Examples of Static Equilibrium",
    "prompt": "A uniform trapdoor shown below is 1.0 m by 1.5 m and weighs 300 N. It is supported by a single hinge (H), and by a light rope tied between the middle of the door and the floor. The door…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A uniform trapdoor shown below is 1.0 m by 1.5 m and weighs 300 N. It is supported by a single hinge (H), and by a light rope tied between the middle of the door and the floor. The door is held at the position shown, where its slab makes a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> angle with the horizontal floor and the rope makes a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> angle with the floor. Find the tension in the rope and the force at the hinge.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A uniform trapdoor shown below is 1.0 m by 1.5 m and weighs 300 N. It is supported by a single hinge (H), and by a light rope tied between the middle of the door and the floor. The door is held at the position shown, where its slab makes a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> angle with the horizontal floor and the rope makes a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> angle with the floor. Find the tension in the rope and the force at the hinge.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure is a schematic drawing of a trapdoor that is 1.0 m by 1.5 m. Door is supported by a single hinge labeled H, and by a light rope tied between the middle of the door and the floor. The door makes a 30 degree angle with the floor and the rope makes a 20 degree angle with the floor.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/a9b1d3ca26e824150515bbed.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-problems#fs-id1163713161847",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-12#fs-id1163713161847-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>1500 N; 1620 N at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 12, Problem 43. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-problems#fs-id1163713161847\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
