    "topic": "Resistors in Series and Parallel",
    "prompt": "Show that if two resistors R 1 and R 2 are combined and one is much greater than the other ( R 1 ≫ R 2 ) , (a) their series resistance is very nearly equal to the greater resistance R 1…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Show that if two resistors <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> are combined and one is much greater than the other <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≫</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, (a) their series resistance is very nearly equal to the greater resistance<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and (b) their parallel resistance is very nearly equal to the smaller resistance <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Show that if two resistors <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> are combined and one is much greater than the other <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≫</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, (a) their series resistance is very nearly equal to the greater resistance<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and (b) their parallel resistance is very nearly equal to the smaller resistance <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p></div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-problems#fs-id1172098315793",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 34. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-problems#fs-id1172098315793\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
