    "topic": "Magnetic forces",
    "prompt": "The current loop shown in the accompanying figure lies in the plane of the page, as does the magnetic field. Determine the net force and the net torque on the loop if I = 10 A and B = 1.5 T.",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The current loop shown in the accompanying figure lies in the plane of the page, as does the magnetic field. Determine the net force and the net torque on the loop if <em>I</em> = 10 A and <em>B</em> = 1.5 T.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The current loop shown in the accompanying figure lies in the plane of the page, as does the magnetic field. Determine the net force and the net torque on the loop if <em>I</em> = 10 A and <em>B</em> = 1.5 T.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"The current loop forms a parallelogram: the top and bottom are horizontal and 10 cm long, the sides are tilted at an angle of 60 degrees up from the +x direction and are 8.0 cm long. A current of 10 A flows counterclockwise. The magnetic field is up.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/3cfc12aa903a31d9b61c7066.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1171361424258",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-11#fs-id1171361424258-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>0 N and 0.012 Nm</p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 83. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1171361424258\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
