    "topic": "Inductance",
    "prompt": "A solenoid with 4 x 10 7 turns/m has an iron core placed in it whose magnetic susceptibility is 4.0 × 10 3 . (a) If a current of 2.0 A flows through the solenoid, what is the magnetic…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A solenoid with <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>x</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow></semantics></math></span> turns/m has an iron core placed in it whose magnetic susceptibility is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (a) If a current of 2.0 A flows through the solenoid, what is the magnetic field in the iron core? (b) What is the effective surface current formed by the aligned atomic current loops in the iron core? (c) What is the self-inductance of the filled solenoid?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A solenoid with <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>x</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow></semantics></math></span> turns/m has an iron core placed in it whose magnetic susceptibility is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (a) If a current of 2.0 A flows through the solenoid, what is the magnetic field in the iron core? (b) What is the effective surface current formed by the aligned atomic current loops in the iron core? (c) What is the self-inductance of the filled solenoid?</p></div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-additional-problems#fs-id1167131615186",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-14#fs-id1167131615186-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. 100 T; b. 2 A; c. 0.50 H</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 14, Problem 77. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-additional-problems#fs-id1167131615186\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
