    "prompt": "The terminal velocity of a person falling in air depends upon the weight and the area of the person facing the fluid. Find the terminal velocity (in meters per second and kilometers per…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The terminal velocity of a person falling in air depends upon the weight and the area of the person facing the fluid. Find the terminal velocity (in meters per second and kilometers per hour) of an 80.0-kg skydiver falling in a headfirst position with a surface area of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.140</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The terminal velocity of a person falling in air depends upon the weight and the area of the person facing the fluid. Find the terminal velocity (in meters per second and kilometers per hour) of an 80.0-kg skydiver falling in a headfirst position with a surface area of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.140</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p></div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-problems#fs-id1165039251723",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-6#fs-id1165039251723-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>115 m/s or 414 km/h</p>\n</div>",
