    "topic": "Angular momentum",
    "prompt": "A top has moment of inertia 3.2 × 10 −4 kg · m 2 and radius 4.0 cm from the center of mass to the pivot point. If it spins at 20.0 rev/s and is precessing, how many revolutions does it…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A top has moment of inertia <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>×</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−4</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and radius 4.0 cm from the center of mass to the pivot point. If it spins at 20.0 rev/s and is precessing, how many revolutions does it precess in 10.0 s?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A top has moment of inertia <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>×</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−4</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext><mo>·</mo><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and radius 4.0 cm from the center of mass to the pivot point. If it spins at 20.0 rev/s and is precessing, how many revolutions does it precess in 10.0 s?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1165037150252",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 94. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1165037150252\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
