    "imported": true,
    "source": "OpenStax",
    "volume": 2,
    "chapter": 6,
    "number": 29,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Electric Flux",
    "prompt": "An infinite charged wire with charge per unit length λ lies along the central axis of a cylindrical surface of radius r and length l . What is the flux through the surface due to the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>An infinite charged wire with charge per unit length <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> lies along the central axis of a cylindrical surface of radius <em>r</em> and length <em>l</em>. What is the flux through the surface due to the electric field of the charged wire?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>An infinite charged wire with charge per unit length <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> lies along the central axis of a cylindrical surface of radius <em>r</em> and length <em>l</em>. What is the flux through the surface due to the electric field of the charged wire?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172101003685",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-6#fs-id1172101003685-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\">\n<mover accent=\"true\">\n<mtext>E</mtext>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo>\n</mover>\n</mstyle>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n<mi>z</mi>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mfrac>\n<mn>1</mn>\n<mrow>\n<mn>4</mn>\n<mi>π</mi>\n<msub>\n<mi>ε</mi>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</msub>\n</mrow>\n</mfrac>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mfrac>\n<mrow>\n<mn>2</mn>\n<mi>λ</mi>\n</mrow>\n<mi>z</mi>\n</mfrac>\n<mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\">\n<mover accent=\"true\">\n<mtext>k</mtext>\n<mo>^</mo>\n</mover>\n</mstyle>\n<mo>,</mo>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mstyle>\n<mrow>\n<mo>∫</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\">\n<mover accent=\"true\">\n<mtext>E</mtext>\n<mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo>\n</mover>\n</mstyle>\n<mo>·</mo>\n<mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\">\n<mover accent=\"true\">\n<mtext>n</mtext>\n<mo>^</mo>\n</mover>\n</mstyle>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</mstyle>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mi>d</mi>\n<mi>A</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mfrac>\n<mi>λ</mi>\n<mrow>\n<msub>\n<mi>ε</mi>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</msub>\n</mrow>\n</mfrac>\n<mi>l</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 29. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172101003685\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
