    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Resistors in Series and Parallel",
    "prompt": "Consider the circuit shown below. The terminal voltage of the battery is V = 18.00 V . (a) Find the equivalent resistance of the circuit. (b) Find the current through each resistor. (c)…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Consider the circuit shown below. The terminal voltage of the battery is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>18.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) Find the equivalent resistance of the circuit. (b) Find the current through each resistor. (c) Find the potential drop across each resistor. (d) Find the power dissipated by each resistor. (e) Find the power supplied by the battery.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Consider the circuit shown below. The terminal voltage of the battery is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>18.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) Find the equivalent resistance of the circuit. (b) Find the current through each resistor. (c) Find the potential drop across each resistor. (d) Find the power dissipated by each resistor. (e) Find the power supplied by the battery.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"The figure shows negative terminal of a voltage source of 18 V connected to three resistors in series, R subscript 1 of 4 Ω, R subscript 2 of 1 Ω and R subscript 3 of 4 Ω.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/8959eb75a31b58701a1d4feb.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-problems#fs-id1172100856012",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-10#fs-id1172100856012-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>9.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; b.<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nc. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; d. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>16.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>W</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>W</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>16.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>W</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; e. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>36.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>W</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 35. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-problems#fs-id1172100856012\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
