    "topic": "Inductance",
    "prompt": "The switch S of the circuit shown below is closed at t = 0 . Determine (a) the initial current through the battery and (b) the steady-state current through the battery.",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The switch S of the circuit shown below is closed at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Determine (a) the initial current through the battery and (b) the steady-state current through the battery.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The switch S of the circuit shown below is closed at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Determine (a) the initial current through the battery and (b) the steady-state current through the battery.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"A 12 volt battery is connected in series with a 5 ohm resistor, a 1 Henry inductor, a 3 ohm resistor and an open switch S. Parallel to the 3 ohm resistor is a 2 Henry inductor.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/feae8ee9b1655558055ad602.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-additional-problems#fs-id1167131399352",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-14#fs-id1167131399352-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. 0 A; b. 2.4 A</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 14, Problem 79. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-additional-problems#fs-id1167131399352\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
