    "topic": "Static equilibrium",
    "prompt": "A pencil rests against a corner, as shown below. The sharpened end of the pencil touches a smooth vertical surface and the eraser end touches a rough horizontal floor. The coefficient of…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A pencil rests against a corner, as shown below. The sharpened end of the pencil touches a smooth vertical surface and the eraser end touches a rough horizontal floor. The coefficient of static friction between the eraser and the floor is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.80</mn><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> The center of mass of the pencil is located 9.0 cm from the tip of the eraser and 11.0 cm from the tip of the pencil lead. Find the minimum angle <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> for which the pencil does not slip.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A pencil rests against a corner, as shown below. The sharpened end of the pencil touches a smooth vertical surface and the eraser end touches a rough horizontal floor. The coefficient of static friction between the eraser and the floor is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.80</mn><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> The center of mass of the pencil is located 9.0 cm from the tip of the eraser and 11.0 cm from the tip of the pencil lead. Find the minimum angle <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> for which the pencil does not slip.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows a pencil that rests against a corner. The sharpened end of the pencil touches a smooth vertical surface and the eraser end touches a rough horizontal floor. Angle between pencil and ground is Theta. Center of mass is 9 cm from the eraser and 11 cm from the sharpened end.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/0a79a5e672ea4eca9cc9d413.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-additional-problems#fs-id1163713258704",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 12, Problem 70. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/12-additional-problems#fs-id1163713258704\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
