    "previewHTML": "<p>(a) What is the orbital radius of an Earth satellite having a period of 1.00 h? (b) What is unreasonable about this result?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>(a) What is the orbital radius of an Earth satellite having a period of 1.00 h? (b) What is unreasonable about this result?</p></div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-problems#fs-id1168325665712",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-13#fs-id1168325665712-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.08</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>km</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; b. This less than the radius of Earth.</p>\n</div>",
