    "topic": "Applying Gauss’s Law",
    "prompt": "When a charge is placed on a metal sphere, it ends up in equilibrium at the outer surface. Use this information to determine the electric field of + 3.0 μ C charge put on a 5.0-cm…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>When a charge is placed on a metal sphere, it ends up in equilibrium at the outer surface. Use this information to determine the electric field of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> charge put on a 5.0-cm aluminum spherical ball at the following two points in space: (a) a point 1.0 cm from the center of the ball (an inside point) and (b) a point 10 cm from the center of the ball (an outside point).</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>When a charge is placed on a metal sphere, it ends up in equilibrium at the outer surface. Use this information to determine the electric field of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> charge put on a 5.0-cm aluminum spherical ball at the following two points in space: (a) a point 1.0 cm from the center of the ball (an inside point) and (b) a point 10 cm from the center of the ball (an outside point).</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172101998967",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-6#fs-id1172101998967-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. 0; b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.70</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>N</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 47. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172101998967\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
