    "prompt": "A cyclist traveling southeast along a road at 15 km/h feels a wind blowing from the southwest at 25 km/h. To a stationary observer, what are the speed and direction of the wind?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A cyclist traveling southeast along a road at 15 km/h feels a wind blowing from the southwest at 25 km/h. To a stationary observer, what are the speed and direction of the wind?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A cyclist traveling southeast along a road at 15 km/h feels a wind blowing from the southwest at 25 km/h. To a stationary observer, what are the speed and direction of the wind?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165039333594",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-4#fs-id1165039333594-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>25</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>km</mtext></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><mtext>h</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>km</mtext></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><mtext>h</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>29.15</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>km</mtext></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>h</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><br/></span>\nThe angle between <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>31</mn><mtext>°</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> so the direction of the wind is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>14</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> north of east.<span><br/></span>\n</p><span>\n<img alt=\"Vectors V sub A C, V sub C G and V sub A G form a triangle. V sub A C and V sub C G are at right angles. V sub A G is the vector sum of v sub A C and V sub C G.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"textbook-assets/75456ed7833ab5fbba767db2.jpg\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 4, Problem 77. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165039333594\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
