    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Sources of Energy",
    "prompt": "A 5.00 × 10 5 -kg subway train is brought to a stop from a speed of 0.500 m/s in 0.400 m by a large spring bumper at the end of its track. What is the spring constant k of the spring?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>-kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> subway train is brought to a stop from a speed of 0.500 m/s in 0.400 m by a large spring bumper at the end of its track. What is the spring constant <em>k</em> of the spring?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>-kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> subway train is brought to a stop from a speed of 0.500 m/s in 0.400 m by a large spring bumper at the end of its track. What is the spring constant <em>k</em> of the spring?</p>\n</div>",
