    "number": 63,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Sources of Energy",
    "prompt": "A pogo stick has a spring with a spring constant of 2.5 × 10 4 N/m, which can be compressed 12.0 cm. To what maximum height from the uncompressed spring can a child jump on the stick…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A pogo stick has a spring with a spring constant of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N/m,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> which can be compressed 12.0 cm. To what maximum height from the uncompressed spring can a child jump on the stick using only the energy in the spring, if the child and stick have a total mass of 40 kg?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A pogo stick has a spring with a spring constant of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N/m,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> which can be compressed 12.0 cm. To what maximum height from the uncompressed spring can a child jump on the stick using only the energy in the spring, if the child and stick have a total mass of 40 kg?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/8-problems#fs-id1165036846980",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-8#fs-id1165036846980-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>33.9 cm</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 8, Problem 63. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/8-problems#fs-id1165036846980\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
