    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "RC Circuits",
    "prompt": "The timing device in an automobile’s intermittent wiper system is based on an RC time constant and utilizes a 0.500 - μ F capacitor and a variable resistor. Over what range must R be…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The timing device in an automobile’s intermittent wiper system is based on an <em>RC</em> time constant and utilizes a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.500</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> capacitor and a variable resistor. Over what range must <em>R</em> be made to vary to achieve time constants from 2.00 to 15.0 s?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The timing device in an automobile’s intermittent wiper system is based on an <em>RC</em> time constant and utilizes a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.500</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mi>μ</mi><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> capacitor and a variable resistor. Over what range must <em>R</em> be made to vary to achieve time constants from 2.00 to 15.0 s?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-problems#fs-id1172101798159",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-10#fs-id1172101798159-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mn>4.00</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>to</mtext>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mn>30.0</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>M</mtext>\n<mtext>Ω</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 49. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-problems#fs-id1172101798159\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
