    "topic": "Applying Gauss’s Law",
    "prompt": "A long silver rod of radius 3 cm has a charge of − 5 μ C/cm on its surface. (a) Find the electric field at a point 5 cm from the center of the rod (an outside point). (b) Find the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A long silver rod of radius 3 cm has a charge of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C/cm</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> on its surface. (a) Find the electric field at a point 5 cm from the center of the rod (an outside point). (b) Find the electric field at a point 2 cm from the center of the rod (an inside point).</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A long silver rod of radius 3 cm has a charge of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C/cm</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> on its surface. (a) Find the electric field at a point 5 cm from the center of the rod (an outside point). (b) Find the electric field at a point 2 cm from the center of the rod (an inside point).</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172101898549",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 50. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172101898549\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
