    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Newton’s laws",
    "prompt": "As shown below, two identical springs, each with the spring constant 20 N/m, support a 15.0-N weight. (a) What is the tension in spring A? (b) What is the amount of stretch of spring A…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>As shown below, two identical springs, each with the spring constant 20 N/m, support a 15.0-N weight. (a) What is the tension in spring A? (b) What is the amount of stretch of spring A from the rest position?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>As shown below, two identical springs, each with the spring constant 20 N/m, support a 15.0-N weight. (a) What is the tension in spring A? (b) What is the amount of stretch of spring A from the rest position?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Figure shows two identical springs hanging side by side. Their lower ends are brought together and support a weight. Each spring makes an angle of 30 degrees with the vertical.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/b74646ba89f21b529659c754ed47b1c25584d7a4\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-additional-problems#fs-id1165039309174",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-5#fs-id1165039309174-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. 8.66 N; b. 0.433 m</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 5, Problem 87. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/5-additional-problems#fs-id1165039309174\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
