    "topic": "Drag Force and Terminal Speed",
    "prompt": "Suppose that the resistive force of the air on a skydiver can be approximated by f = − b v 2 . If the terminal velocity of a 50.0-kg skydiver is 60.0 m/s, what is the value of b ?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Suppose that the resistive force of the air on a skydiver can be approximated by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> If the terminal velocity of a 50.0-kg skydiver is 60.0 m/s, what is the value of <em>b</em>?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Suppose that the resistive force of the air on a skydiver can be approximated by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>−</mtext><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> If the terminal velocity of a 50.0-kg skydiver is 60.0 m/s, what is the value of <em>b</em>?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-problems#fs-id1165033377748",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 88. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-problems#fs-id1165033377748\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
