    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Gravitation and orbits",
    "prompt": "A satellite of mass 1000 kg is in circular orbit about Earth. The radius of the orbit of the satellite is equal to two times the radius of Earth. (a) How far away is the satellite? (b)…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A satellite of mass 1000 kg is in circular orbit about Earth. The radius of the orbit of the satellite is equal to two times the radius of Earth. (a) How far away is the satellite? (b) Find the kinetic, potential, and total energies of the satellite.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A satellite of mass 1000 kg is in circular orbit about Earth. The radius of the orbit of the satellite is equal to two times the radius of Earth. (a) How far away is the satellite? (b) Find the kinetic, potential, and total energies of the satellite.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-additional-problems#fs-id1168325860673",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-13#fs-id1168325860673-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.3</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.56</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>J</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mn>3.12</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>J</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>−1.56</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>J</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 71. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-additional-problems#fs-id1168325860673\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
