    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Explaining Gauss’s Law",
    "prompt": "The electric flux through a spherical surface is 4.0 × 10 4 N · m 2 /C . What is the net charge enclosed by the surface?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The electric flux through a spherical surface is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext><mo>·</mo><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext>/C</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the net charge enclosed by the surface?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The electric flux through a spherical surface is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>N</mtext><mo>·</mo><msup><mtext>m</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext>/C</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the net charge enclosed by the surface?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172101032982",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-6#fs-id1172101032982-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>q</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>3.54</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mo>×</mo>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<msup>\n<mrow>\n<mn>10</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mn>−7</mn>\n</mrow>\n</msup>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mtext>C</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 37. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172101032982\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
