    "topic": "Magnetic forces",
    "prompt": "Consider an electron rotating in a circular orbit of radius r. Show that the magnitudes of the magnetic dipole moment μ and the angular momentum L of the electron are related by: μ L = e…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Consider an electron rotating in a circular orbit of radius r. Show that the magnitudes of the magnetic dipole moment μ and the angular momentum <em>L</em> of the electron are related by:</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Consider an electron rotating in a circular orbit of radius r. Show that the magnitudes of the magnetic dipole moment μ and the angular momentum <em>L</em> of the electron are related by:</p>\n<div>\n<math display=\"block\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mi>μ</mi>\n<mi>L</mi>\n</mfrac>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mfrac>\n<mi>e</mi>\n<mrow>\n<mn>2</mn>\n<mi>m</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mfrac>\n<mo>.</mo>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</semantics>\n</math>\n</div>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1171361374215",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-11#fs-id1171361374215-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>(Proof)</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 91. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1171361374215\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
