    "source": "OpenStax",
    "volume": 1,
    "chapter": 3,
    "number": 103,
    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Kinematics",
    "prompt": "A soft tennis ball is dropped onto a hard floor from a height of 1.50 m and rebounds to a height of 1.10 m. (a) Calculate its velocity just before it strikes the floor. (b) Calculate its…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A soft tennis ball is dropped onto a hard floor from a height of 1.50 m and rebounds to a height of 1.10 m. (a) Calculate its velocity just before it strikes the floor. (b) Calculate its velocity just after it leaves the floor on its way back up. (c) Calculate its acceleration during contact with the floor if that contact lasts 3.50 ms <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (d) How much did the ball compress during its collision with the floor, assuming the floor is absolutely rigid?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A soft tennis ball is dropped onto a hard floor from a height of 1.50 m and rebounds to a height of 1.10 m. (a) Calculate its velocity just before it strikes the floor. (b) Calculate its velocity just after it leaves the floor on its way back up. (c) Calculate its acceleration during contact with the floor if that contact lasts 3.50 ms <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (d) How much did the ball compress during its collision with the floor, assuming the floor is absolutely rigid?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-additional-problems#fs-id1168055388728",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-3#fs-id1168055388728-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.42</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nb. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4.64</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nc. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2874.28</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nd. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5.11</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 3, Problem 103. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-additional-problems#fs-id1168055388728\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
