    "prompt": "In the reality television show “Amazing Race” , a contestant is firing 3.0-kg watermelons from a slingshot to hit targets down the field. The slingshot is pulled back 2.0 m and the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>In the reality television show <a href=\"https://openstax.org/l/21amazraceclip\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">“Amazing Race”</a>, a contestant is firing 3.0-kg watermelons from a slingshot to hit targets down the field. The slingshot is pulled back 2.0 m and the watermelon is considered to be at ground level. The launch point is 0.75 m from the ground and the targets are 10 m horizontally away. Calculate the spring constant of the slingshot.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>In the reality television show <a href=\"https://openstax.org/l/21amazraceclip\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">“Amazing Race”</a>, a contestant is firing 3.0-kg watermelons from a slingshot to hit targets down the field. The slingshot is pulled back 2.0 m and the watermelon is considered to be at ground level. The launch point is 0.75 m from the ground and the targets are 10 m horizontally away. Calculate the spring constant of the slingshot.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/8-problems#fs-id1165037976761",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-8#fs-id1165037976761-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>490 N/m</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 8, Problem 53. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/8-problems#fs-id1165037976761\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
