    "topic": "Applying Gauss’s Law",
    "prompt": "Charge is distributed throughout a spherical shell of inner radius r 1 and outer radius r 2 with a volume density given by ρ = ρ 0 r 1 / r , where ρ 0 is a constant. Determine the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Charge is distributed throughout a spherical shell of inner radius <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and outer radius <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with a volume density given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is a constant. Determine the electric field due to this charge as a function of <em>r</em>, the distance from the center of the shell.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Charge is distributed throughout a spherical shell of inner radius <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and outer radius <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with a volume density given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is a constant. Determine the electric field due to this charge as a function of <em>r</em>, the distance from the center of the shell.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172099922015",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 56. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172099922015\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
