    "topic": "Kinematics",
    "prompt": "Compare the time in the air of a basketball player who jumps 1.0 m vertically off the floor with that of a player who jumps 0.3 m vertically.",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Compare the time in the air of a basketball player who jumps 1.0 m vertically off the floor with that of a player who jumps 0.3 m vertically.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Compare the time in the air of a basketball player who jumps 1.0 m vertically off the floor with that of a player who jumps 0.3 m vertically.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-additional-problems#fs-id1168055124296",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-3#fs-id1168055124296-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>Consider the players fall from rest at the height 1.0 m and 0.3 m.<span><br/></span>\n0.9 s<span><br/></span>\n0.5 s</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 3, Problem 105. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/3-additional-problems#fs-id1168055124296\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
