    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Gravitation Near Earth's Surface",
    "prompt": "On a planet whose radius is 1.2 × 10 7 m , the acceleration due to gravity is 18 m/s 2 . What is the mass of the planet?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>On a planet whose radius is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, the acceleration due to gravity is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the mass of the planet?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>On a planet whose radius is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, the acceleration due to gravity is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the mass of the planet?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-problems#fs-id1168328270951",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 24. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-problems#fs-id1168328270951\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
