    "topic": "Household Wiring and Electrical Safety",
    "prompt": "While taking a bath, a person touches the metal case of a radio. The path through the person to the drainpipe and ground has a resistance of 4000 Ω . What is the smallest voltage on the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>While taking a bath, a person touches the metal case of a radio. The path through the person to the drainpipe and ground has a resistance of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4000</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the smallest voltage on the case of the radio that could cause ventricular fibrillation?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>While taking a bath, a person touches the metal case of a radio. The path through the person to the drainpipe and ground has a resistance of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4000</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. What is the smallest voltage on the case of the radio that could cause ventricular fibrillation?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-problems#fs-id1172099486343",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-10#fs-id1172099486343-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>400 V</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 61. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-problems#fs-id1172099486343\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
