    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Applying Gauss’s Law",
    "prompt": "Consider a uranium nucleus to be sphere of radius R = 7.4 × 10 −15 m with a charge of 92 e distributed uniformly throughout its volume. (a) What is the electric force exerted on an…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Consider a uranium nucleus to be sphere of radius <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−15</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with a charge of 92<em>e</em> distributed uniformly throughout its volume. (a) What is the electric force exerted on an electron when it is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−15</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> from the center of the nucleus? (b) What is the acceleration of the electron at this point?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Consider a uranium nucleus to be sphere of radius <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−15</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with a charge of 92<em>e</em> distributed uniformly throughout its volume. (a) What is the electric force exerted on an electron when it is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−15</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> from the center of the nucleus? (b) What is the acceleration of the electron at this point?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172099650658",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 58. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172099650658\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
