    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Applying Gauss’s Law",
    "prompt": "Suppose that the charge density of the spherical charge distribution shown in Figure 6.23 is ρ ( r ) = ρ 0 r / R for r ≤ R and zero for r > R . Obtain expressions for the electric field…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Suppose that the charge density of the spherical charge distribution shown in <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-3-applying-gausss-law\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Figure 6.23</a> is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>r</mi></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> for <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and zero for <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Obtain expressions for the electric field both inside and outside the distribution.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Suppose that the charge density of the spherical charge distribution shown in <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-3-applying-gausss-law\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Figure 6.23</a> is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>r</mi></mrow><mtext>/</mtext><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> for <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and zero for <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Obtain expressions for the electric field both inside and outside the distribution.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172102106817",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 42. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172102106817\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
