    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Gravitation Near Earth's Surface",
    "prompt": "The mean diameter of the planet Mercury is 4.88 × 10 6 m , and the acceleration due to gravity at its surface is 3.78 m/s 2 . Estimate the mass of this planet.",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The mean diameter of the planet Mercury is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.88</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and the acceleration due to gravity at its surface is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.78</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Estimate the mass of this planet.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The mean diameter of the planet Mercury is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4.88</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and the acceleration due to gravity at its surface is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.78</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. Estimate the mass of this planet.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-problems#fs-id1168327916830",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 26. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-problems#fs-id1168327916830\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
