    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Applying Gauss’s Law",
    "prompt": "A large sheet of charge has a uniform charge density of 10 μ C/m 2 . What is the electric field due to this charge at a point just above the surface of the sheet?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A large sheet of charge has a uniform charge density of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><msup><mrow><mtext>C/m</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the electric field due to this charge at a point just above the surface of the sheet?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A large sheet of charge has a uniform charge density of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><msup><mrow><mtext>C/m</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> What is the electric field due to this charge at a point just above the surface of the sheet?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172099514803",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 48. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172099514803\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
