    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Displacement and Velocity Vectors",
    "prompt": "The position of a particle is r → ( t ) = 4.0 t 2 i ^ − 3.0 j ^ + 2.0 t 3 k ^ m . (a) What is the velocity of the particle at 0 s and at 1.0 s? (b) What is the average velocity between 0…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The position of a particle is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>3.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>2.0</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mtext>m</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) What is the velocity of the particle at 0 s and at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> s? (b) What is the average velocity between 0 s and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> s?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The position of a particle is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>3.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>2.0</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mtext>m</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) What is the velocity of the particle at 0 s and at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> s? (b) What is the average velocity between 0 s and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> s?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165038198131",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-4#fs-id1165038198131-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>8.0</mn><mi>t</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>6.0</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.7em\"></mspace><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.7em\"></mspace><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>8.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,\n\n<span><br/></span>b. \n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mrow><mtext>avg</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mtext>​</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 4, Problem 23. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165038198131\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
