    "topic": "Magnetic forces",
    "prompt": "Unreasonable results An inventor wants to generate 120-V power by moving a 1.00-m-long wire perpendicular to Earth’s 5.00 × 10 −5 T field. (a) Find the speed with which the wire must…",
    "previewHTML": "<p><strong>Unreasonable results</strong> An inventor wants to generate 120-V power by moving a 1.00-m-long wire perpendicular to Earth’s <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−5</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>T</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> field. (a) Find the speed with which the wire must move. (b) What is unreasonable about this result? (c) Which assumption is responsible?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p><strong>Unreasonable results</strong> An inventor wants to generate 120-V power by moving a 1.00-m-long wire perpendicular to Earth’s <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−5</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>T</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> field. (a) Find the speed with which the wire must move. (b) What is unreasonable about this result? (c) Which assumption is responsible?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1171361540249",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 11, Problem 100. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/11-additional-problems#fs-id1171361540249\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
