    "topic": "Conductors in Electrostatic Equilibrium",
    "prompt": "An aluminum spherical ball of radius 4 cm is charged with 5 μ C of charge. A copper spherical shell of inner radius 6 cm and outer radius 8 cm surrounds it. A total charge of −8 μ C is…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>An aluminum spherical ball of radius 4 cm is charged with <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> of charge. A copper spherical shell of inner radius 6 cm and outer radius 8 cm surrounds it. A total charge of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>−8</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is put on the copper shell. (a) Find the electric field at all points in space, including points inside the aluminum and copper shell when copper shell and aluminum sphere are concentric. (b) Find the electric field at all points in space, including points inside the aluminum and copper shell when the centers of copper shell and aluminum sphere are 1 cm apart.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>An aluminum spherical ball of radius 4 cm is charged with <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> of charge. A copper spherical shell of inner radius 6 cm and outer radius 8 cm surrounds it. A total charge of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>−8</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is put on the copper shell. (a) Find the electric field at all points in space, including points inside the aluminum and copper shell when copper shell and aluminum sphere are concentric. (b) Find the electric field at all points in space, including points inside the aluminum and copper shell when the centers of copper shell and aluminum sphere are 1 cm apart.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172098376747",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 64. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172098376747\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
