    "topic": "DC circuits",
    "prompt": "A circuit contains a D cell battery, a switch, a 20 - Ω resistor, and four 20-mF capacitors connected in series. (a) What is the equivalent capacitance of the circuit? (b) What is the RC…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A circuit contains a D cell battery, a switch, a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> resistor, and four 20-mF capacitors connected in series. (a) What is the equivalent capacitance of the circuit? (b) What is the <em>RC</em> time constant? (c) How long before the current decreases to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>50</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> of the initial value once the switch is closed?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A circuit contains a D cell battery, a switch, a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> resistor, and four 20-mF capacitors connected in series. (a) What is the equivalent capacitance of the circuit? (b) What is the <em>RC</em> time constant? (c) How long before the current decreases to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>50</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> of the initial value once the switch is closed?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1172099544191",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-10#fs-id1172099544191-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mtext>eq</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>mF</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; c. 0.069 s</p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 67. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1172099544191\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
