    "prompt": "The position of a particle is r → ( t ) = ( 3.0 t 2 i ^ + 5.0 j ^ − 6.0 t k ^ ) m . (a) Determine its velocity and acceleration as functions of time. (b) What are its velocity and…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The position of a particle is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3.0</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mi>t</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) Determine its velocity and acceleration as functions of time. (b) What are its velocity and acceleration at time <em>t</em> = 0?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The position of a particle is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3.0</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mi>t</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) Determine its velocity and acceleration as functions of time. (b) What are its velocity and acceleration at time <em>t</em> = 0?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165038328945",
