    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Applying Gauss’s Law",
    "prompt": "Charge is distributed throughout a spherical volume of radius R with a density ρ = α r 2 , where α is a constant. Determine the electric field due to the charge at points both inside and…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Charge is distributed throughout a spherical volume of radius <em>R</em> with a density <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> is a constant. Determine the electric field due to the charge at points both inside and outside the sphere.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Charge is distributed throughout a spherical volume of radius <em>R</em> with a density <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> is a constant. Determine the electric field due to the charge at points both inside and outside the sphere.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172099587946",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-6#fs-id1172099587946-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mtext>enc</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">⇒</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mtext>enc</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>E</mi><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">⇒</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 57. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172099587946\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
