    "prompt": "A circuit contains a D-cell battery, a switch, a 20 - Ω resistor, and three 20-mF capacitors. The capacitors are connected in parallel, and the parallel connection of capacitors are…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A circuit contains a D-cell battery, a switch, a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> resistor, and three 20-mF capacitors. The capacitors are connected in parallel, and the parallel connection of capacitors are connected in series with the switch, the resistor and the battery. (a) What is the equivalent capacitance of the circuit? (b) What is the <em>RC</em> time constant? (c) How long before the current decreases to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>50</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> of the initial value once the switch is closed?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A circuit contains a D-cell battery, a switch, a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mtext>-</mtext><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> resistor, and three 20-mF capacitors. The capacitors are connected in parallel, and the parallel connection of capacitors are connected in series with the switch, the resistor and the battery. (a) What is the equivalent capacitance of the circuit? (b) What is the <em>RC</em> time constant? (c) How long before the current decreases to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>50</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> of the initial value once the switch is closed?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1172102021422",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 68. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1172102021422\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
