    "prompt": "A boat leaves the dock at t = 0 and heads out into a lake with an acceleration of 2.0 m/ s 2 i ^ . A strong wind is pushing the boat, giving it an additional velocity of 2.0 m/s i ^ +…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A boat leaves the dock at <em>t</em> = 0 and heads out into a lake with an acceleration of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m/</mtext><mrow><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> A strong wind is pushing the boat, giving it an additional velocity of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) What is the velocity of the boat at <em>t</em> = 10 s? (b) What is the position of the boat at <em>t</em> = 10s? Draw a sketch of the boat’s trajectory and position at <em>t</em> = 10 s, showing the <em>x-</em> and <em>y</em>-axes.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A boat leaves the dock at <em>t</em> = 0 and heads out into a lake with an acceleration of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m/</mtext><mrow><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> A strong wind is pushing the boat, giving it an additional velocity of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) What is the velocity of the boat at <em>t</em> = 10 s? (b) What is the position of the boat at <em>t</em> = 10s? Draw a sketch of the boat’s trajectory and position at <em>t</em> = 10 s, showing the <em>x-</em> and <em>y</em>-axes.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165038298654",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 4, Problem 28. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165038298654\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
