    "number": 59,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Applying Gauss’s Law",
    "prompt": "The volume charge density of a spherical charge distribution is given by ρ ( r ) = ρ 0 e − α r , where ρ 0 and α are constants. What is the electric field produced by this charge…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The volume charge density of a spherical charge distribution is given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mi>α</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> are constants. What is the electric field produced by this charge distribution?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The volume charge density of a spherical charge distribution is given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mi>α</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> are constants. What is the electric field produced by this charge distribution?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172102043394",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-6#fs-id1172102043394-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>integrate by parts: <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mtext>enc</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mi>α</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">⇒</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mtext>−</mtext><mi>α</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 59. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172102043394\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
