    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Conductors in Electrostatic Equilibrium",
    "prompt": "At the surface of any conductor in electrostatic equilibrium, E = σ / ε 0 . Show that this equation is consistent with the fact that E = k q / r 2 at the surface of a spherical conductor.",
    "previewHTML": "<p>At the surface of any conductor in electrostatic equilibrium, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>σ</mi><mtext>/</mtext><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Show that this equation is consistent with the fact that <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi><mtext>/</mtext><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> at the surface of a spherical conductor.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>At the surface of any conductor in electrostatic equilibrium, <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>σ</mi><mtext>/</mtext><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Show that this equation is consistent with the fact that <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi><mtext>/</mtext><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> at the surface of a spherical conductor.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172100946378",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 66. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172100946378\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
