    "topic": "Potential energy",
    "prompt": "A body of mass m and negligible size starts from rest and slides down the surface of a frictionless solid sphere of radius R . (See below.) Prove that the body leaves the sphere when θ =…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A body of mass <em>m</em> and negligible size starts from rest and slides down the surface of a frictionless solid sphere of radius <em>R</em>. (See below.) Prove that the body leaves the sphere when <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mtext>cos</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>−1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext>/</mtext><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A body of mass <em>m</em> and negligible size starts from rest and slides down the surface of a frictionless solid sphere of radius <em>R</em>. (See below.) Prove that the body leaves the sphere when <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mtext>cos</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>−1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext>/</mtext><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"A sphere of radius R is shown. A block is shown at two locations on the surface of the sphere and moving clockwise. It is shown at the top, and at an angle of theta measured clockwise from the vertical.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/32c477883cca0118d036f996abf2e55b40928e03\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
