    "topic": "Conductors in Electrostatic Equilibrium",
    "prompt": "A positive point charge is placed at the angle bisector of two uncharged plane conductors that make an angle of 45 ° . See below. Draw the electric field lines.",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A positive point charge is placed at the angle bisector of two uncharged plane conductors that make an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>45</mn><mtext>°</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> See below. Draw the electric field lines.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A positive point charge is placed at the angle bisector of two uncharged plane conductors that make an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>45</mn><mtext>°</mtext><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> See below. Draw the electric field lines.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"An acute angle is shown. Its bisector is a dotted line. A positive charge q is shown on the dotted line.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/7c7e5d23b7eb7195e59733c332c596286baffb3f\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
