    "topic": "Conductors in Electrostatic Equilibrium",
    "prompt": "Two parallel conducting plates, each of cross-sectional area 400 cm 2 , are 2.0 cm apart and uncharged. If 1.0 × 10 12 electrons are transferred from one plate to the other, what are (a)…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Two parallel conducting plates, each of cross-sectional area <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>400</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, are 2.0 cm apart and uncharged. If <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> electrons are transferred from one plate to the other, what are (a) the charge density on each plate? (b) The electric field between the plates?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Two parallel conducting plates, each of cross-sectional area <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>400</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, are 2.0 cm apart and uncharged. If <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> electrons are transferred from one plate to the other, what are (a) the charge density on each plate? (b) The electric field between the plates?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172100562401",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 68. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-problems#fs-id1172100562401\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
