    "prompt": "Consider a circuit that consists of a real battery with an emf ε and an internal resistance of r connected to a variable resistor R . (a) In order for the terminal voltage of the battery…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Consider a circuit that consists of a real battery with an emf <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> and an internal resistance of <em>r</em> connected to a variable resistor <em>R</em>. (a) In order for the terminal voltage of the battery to be equal to the emf of the battery, what should the resistance of the variable resistor be adjusted to? (b) In order to get the maximum current from the battery, what should the resistance of the variable resistor be adjusted to? (c) In order for the maximum power output of the battery to be reached, what should the resistance of the variable resistor be set to?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Consider a circuit that consists of a real battery with an emf <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> and an internal resistance of <em>r</em> connected to a variable resistor <em>R</em>. (a) In order for the terminal voltage of the battery to be equal to the emf of the battery, what should the resistance of the variable resistor be adjusted to? (b) In order to get the maximum current from the battery, what should the resistance of the variable resistor be adjusted to? (c) In order for the maximum power output of the battery to be reached, what should the resistance of the variable resistor be set to?</p></div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1172101779662",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 74. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1172101779662\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
