    "topic": "Potential energy",
    "prompt": "Shown below is a small ball of mass m attached to a string of length a . A small peg is located a distance h below the point where the string is supported. If the ball is released when…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Shown below is a small ball of mass <em>m</em> attached to a string of length <em>a</em>. A small peg is located a distance <em>h</em> below the point where the string is supported. If the ball is released when the string is horizontal, show that <em>h</em> must be greater than 3<em>a</em>/5 if the ball is to swing completely around the peg.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Shown below is a small ball of mass <em>m</em> attached to a string of length <em>a</em>. A small peg is located a distance <em>h</em> below the point where the string is supported. If the ball is released when the string is horizontal, show that <em>h</em> must be greater than 3<em>a</em>/5 if the ball is to swing completely around the peg.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"A small ball is shown attached to a string of length a. A small peg is located a distance h below the point where the string is supported. The ball is released when the string is horizontal  and swings in a circular arc.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/cfa0737f30f801d3a4bb54c731a1749e845949ae\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/8-additional-problems#fs-id1165036880529",
