    "topic": "DC circuits",
    "prompt": "Consider a circuit consisting of a battery with an emf ε and an internal resistance r connected in series with a resistor R and a capacitor C . Show that the total energy supplied by the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Consider a circuit consisting of a battery with an emf <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> and an internal resistance <em>r</em> connected in series with a resistor <em>R</em> and a capacitor <em>C</em>. Show that the total energy supplied by the battery while charging the capacitor is equal to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Consider a circuit consisting of a battery with an emf <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span> and an internal resistance <em>r</em> connected in series with a resistor <em>R</em> and a capacitor <em>C</em>. Show that the total energy supplied by the battery while charging the capacitor is equal to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1172099414258",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 76. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1172099414258\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
