    "number": 77,
    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "DC circuits",
    "prompt": "Consider the circuit shown below. The terminal voltages of the batteries are shown. (a) Find the equivalent resistance of the circuit and the current out of the battery. (b) Find the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Consider the circuit shown below. The terminal voltages of the batteries are shown. (a) Find the equivalent resistance of the circuit and the current out of the battery. (b) Find the current through each resistor. (c) Find the potential drop across each resistor. (d) Find the power dissipated by each resistor. (e) Find the total power supplied by the batteries.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Consider the circuit shown below. The terminal voltages of the batteries are shown. (a) Find the equivalent resistance of the circuit and the current out of the battery. (b) Find the current through each resistor. (c) Find the potential drop across each resistor. (d) Find the power dissipated by each resistor. (e) Find the total power supplied by the batteries.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"The figure shows two series voltage sources of 12 V each with upward negative terminals connected to four resistors. The sources are connected in series to resistor R subscript 1 of 14 Ω connected in series to two parallel resistors, R subscript 2 of 9 Ω and R subscript 3 of 18 Ω connected in series to resistor R subscript 4 of 4 Ω.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/720ab18e785d1ac289662eaed3e96496c8336f77\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1172102066961",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-10#fs-id1172102066961-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mtext>eq</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>24.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>Ω</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.67</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.33</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nc. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>14.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>V</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nd.\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>14.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>W</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4.04</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>W</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.96</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>W</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>W</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; e. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24.00</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>W</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 77. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1172102066961\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
