    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-12#fs-id1166167074737-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>B</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>1.4</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mo>×</mo>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<msup>\n<mrow>\n<mn>10</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mn>−4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</msup>\n<mtext>T</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 12, Problem 65. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/12-additional-problems#fs-id1166167074737\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
