    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Projectile Motion",
    "prompt": "A projectile is launched at an angle of 30 ° and lands 20 s later at the same height as it was launched. (a) What is the initial speed of the projectile? (b) What is the maximum…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A projectile is launched at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and lands 20 s later at the same height as it was launched. (a) What is the initial speed of the projectile? (b) What is the maximum altitude? (c) What is the range? (d) Calculate the displacement from the point of launch to the position on its trajectory at 15 s.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A projectile is launched at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and lands 20 s later at the same height as it was launched. (a) What is the initial speed of the projectile? (b) What is the maximum altitude? (c) What is the range? (d) Calculate the displacement from the point of launch to the position on its trajectory at 15 s.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165167946074",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-4#fs-id1165167946074-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mtext>s,</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>98.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>s</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>196.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, <span><br/></span>b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>490.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><br/></span>c. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>169.7</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><mtext>s,</mtext></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3394.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>\n<span><br/></span>d. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mtable><mtr></mtr><mtr></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>169.7</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>15.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2550</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr>\n<mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>98.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>15.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>–</mo><mn>4.9</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>15.0</mn><mtext>s</mtext><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>368</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr>\n<mtr><mtd columnalign=\"left\"><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>s</mi><mtext>r</mtext></mover></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>2550</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>368</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></semantics></math></span></p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 4, Problem 39. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165167946074\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
