    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Projectile Motion",
    "prompt": "A rock is thrown off a cliff at an angle of 53 ° with respect to the horizontal. The cliff is 100 m high. The initial speed of the rock is 30 m/s. (a) How high above the edge of the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A rock is thrown off a cliff at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>53</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with respect to the horizontal. The cliff is 100 m high. The initial speed of the rock is 30 m/s. (a) How high above the edge of the cliff does the rock rise? (b) How far has it moved horizontally when it is at maximum altitude? (c) How long after the release does it hit the ground? (d) What is the range of the rock? (e) What are the horizontal and vertical positions of the rock relative to the edge of the cliff at <em>t</em> = 2.0 s, <em>t</em> = 4.0 s, and <em>t</em> = 6.0 s?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A rock is thrown off a cliff at an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>53</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with respect to the horizontal. The cliff is 100 m high. The initial speed of the rock is 30 m/s. (a) How high above the edge of the cliff does the rock rise? (b) How far has it moved horizontally when it is at maximum altitude? (c) How long after the release does it hit the ground? (d) What is the range of the rock? (e) What are the horizontal and vertical positions of the rock relative to the edge of the cliff at <em>t</em> = 2.0 s, <em>t</em> = 4.0 s, and <em>t</em> = 6.0 s?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165168033133",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-4#fs-id1165168033133-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">⇒</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>29.3</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,<span><br/></span>\nb. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m/s</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>43.2</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,<span><br/></span>c. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>−100</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mo>−</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4.9</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">⇒</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7.58</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,<span><br/></span>d. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>136.44</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>,<span><br/></span>e. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>28.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>17.6</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>72</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span><span><br/></span>\n<span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>−32.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>108</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 4, Problem 45. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165168033133\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
