    "topic": "Gauss’s law",
    "prompt": "Suppose that the electric field of an isolated point charge were proportional to 1 / r 2 + σ rather than 1 / r 2 . Determine the flux that passes through the surface of a sphere of…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Suppose that the electric field of an isolated point charge were proportional to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> rather than <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Determine the flux that passes through the surface of a sphere of radius <em>R</em> centered at the charge. Would Gauss’s law remain valid?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Suppose that the electric field of an isolated point charge were proportional to <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> rather than <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Determine the flux that passes through the surface of a sphere of radius <em>R</em> centered at the charge. Would Gauss’s law remain valid?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1172098310066",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 76. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1172098310066\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
