    "prompt": "Apply the junction rule at point a shown below.",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Apply the junction rule at point <em>a</em> shown below.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Apply the junction rule at point <em>a</em> shown below.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"The figure shows a circuit with three horizontal branches and two vertical branches. The first horizontal branch has voltage source ε subscript 1 of 24 V and internal resistance 0.1 Ω with right positive terminal. The second horizontal branch has voltage source ε subscript 2 of 48 V and internal resistance 0.5 Ω with right positive terminal and resistor R subscript 2 of 40 Ω with right current I subscript 2. The third horizontal branch has voltage source ε subscript 3 of 6 V and internal resistance 0.05 Ω with left positive terminal. The first and second branches are connected on the left through resistor R subscript 1 of 5 Ω with upward current I subscript 1 and on the right through R subscript 5 of 20 Ω. The second and third branch are connected on the left through resistor R subscript 3 of 78 Ω with upward current I subscript 3 and on the right through voltage source ε subscript 4 of 36 V and internal resistance 0.2 Ω with upward positive terminal.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/82e32d30bbeb9511ab87b78527ee5ee9127cf452\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1172099707203",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 82. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1172099707203\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
