    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Potential energy",
    "prompt": "A 200-g steel ball is tied to a 2.00-m “massless” string and hung from the ceiling to make a pendulum, and then, the ball is brought to a position making a 30 ° angle with the vertical…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A 200-g steel ball is tied to a 2.00-m “massless” string and hung from the ceiling to make a pendulum, and then, the ball is brought to a position making a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> angle with the vertical direction and released from rest. Ignoring the effects of the air resistance, find the speed of the ball when the string (a) is vertically down, (b) makes an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with the vertical and (c) makes an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with the vertical.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A 200-g steel ball is tied to a 2.00-m “massless” string and hung from the ceiling to make a pendulum, and then, the ball is brought to a position making a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> angle with the vertical direction and released from rest. Ignoring the effects of the air resistance, find the speed of the ball when the string (a) is vertically down, (b) makes an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with the vertical and (c) makes an angle of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> with the vertical.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/8-additional-problems#fs-id1165037029550",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 8, Problem 84. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/8-additional-problems#fs-id1165037029550\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
