    "topic": "Gauss’s law",
    "prompt": "A 10 cm × 10 cm piece of aluminum foil of 0.1 mm thickness has a charge of 20 μ C that spreads on both wide side surfaces evenly. You may ignore the charges on the thin sides of the…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mn>10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> piece of aluminum foil of 0.1 mm thickness has a charge of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> that spreads on both wide side surfaces evenly. You may ignore the charges on the thin sides of the edges. (a) Find the charge density on each side of the foil. (b) Find the electric field due to each side of the sheet and the net electric field due to all of the charge at a point outside of the foil, 1 cm from the center. Assume approximate planar symmetry.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mn>10</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> piece of aluminum foil of 0.1 mm thickness has a charge of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mi>μ</mi><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> that spreads on both wide side surfaces evenly. You may ignore the charges on the thin sides of the edges. (a) Find the charge density on each side of the foil. (b) Find the electric field due to each side of the sheet and the net electric field due to all of the charge at a point outside of the foil, 1 cm from the center. Assume approximate planar symmetry.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1172100746229",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 80. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1172100746229\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
