    "number": 85,
    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "DC circuits",
    "prompt": "Consider the circuit shown below. (a) Find the current through each resistor. (b) Check the calculations by analyzing the power in the circuit.",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Consider the circuit shown below. (a) Find the current through each resistor. (b) Check the calculations by analyzing the power in the circuit.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Consider the circuit shown below. (a) Find the current through each resistor. (b) Check the calculations by analyzing the power in the circuit.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"The positive terminal of voltage source of 20 V and internal resistance 5 Ω is connected to two parallel branches. The first branch has resistors R subscript 1 of 15 Ω and R subscript 3 of 10 Ω. The second branch has resistors R subscript 2 of 10 Ω and R subscript 4 of 15 Ω. The two branches are connected in the middle using resistor R subscript 5 of 5 Ω.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/e8b837d3c52554a3afd1f13fcf72eff49d59324c\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1172101971117",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/chapter-10#fs-id1172101971117-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.17</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.67</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.67</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.17</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>A</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>;<span><br/></span>\nb. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mtext>output</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>23.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>W</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mtext>input</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>23.4</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>W</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 10, Problem 85. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-additional-problems#fs-id1172101971117\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
