    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Relative Motion in One and Two Dimensions",
    "prompt": "A small plane flies at 200 km/h in still air. If the wind blows directly out of the west at 50 km/h, (a) in what direction must the pilot head her plane to move directly north across…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A small plane flies at 200 km/h in still air. If the wind blows directly out of the west at 50 km/h, (a) in what direction must the pilot head her plane to move directly north across land and (b) how long does it take her to reach a point 300 km directly north of her starting point?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A small plane flies at 200 km/h in still air. If the wind blows directly out of the west at 50 km/h, (a) in what direction must the pilot head her plane to move directly north across land and (b) how long does it take her to reach a point 300 km directly north of her starting point?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165039267560",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 4, Problem 76. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165039267560\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
