    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Relative Motion in One and Two Dimensions",
    "prompt": "A river is moving east at 4.0 m/s. A boat starts from the dock heading 30 ° north of west at 7.0 m/s. If the river is 1800 m wide, (a) what is the velocity of the boat with respect to…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A river is moving east at 4.0 m/s. A boat starts from the dock heading <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> north of west at 7.0 m/s. If the river is 1800 m wide, (a) what is the velocity of the boat with respect to Earth and (b) how long does it take the boat to cross the river?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A river is moving east at 4.0 m/s. A boat starts from the dock heading <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> north of west at 7.0 m/s. If the river is 1800 m wide, (a) what is the velocity of the boat with respect to Earth and (b) how long does it take the boat to cross the river?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165039244987",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 4, Problem 78. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-problems#fs-id1165039244987\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
