    "prompt": "A Formula One race car is traveling at 89.0 m/s along a straight track enters a turn on the race track with radius of curvature of 200.0 m. What centripetal acceleration must the car…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A Formula One race car is traveling at 89.0 m/s along a straight track enters a turn on the race track with radius of curvature of 200.0 m. What centripetal acceleration must the car have to stay on the track?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A Formula One race car is traveling at 89.0 m/s along a straight track enters a turn on the race track with radius of curvature of 200.0 m. What centripetal acceleration must the car have to stay on the track?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-additional-problems#fs-id1165039273301",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-4#fs-id1165039273301-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<msub>\n<mi>a</mi>\n<mtext>C</mtext>\n</msub>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>39.6</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>m</mtext>\n<mtext>/</mtext>\n<mrow>\n<msup>\n<mtext>s</mtext>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
