    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Sources of magnetic fields",
    "prompt": "Between the two ends of a horseshoe magnet the field is uniform as shown in the diagram. As you move out to outside edges, the field bends. Show by Ampère’s law that the field must bend…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Between the two ends of a horseshoe magnet the field is uniform as shown in the diagram. As you move out to outside edges, the field bends. Show by Ampère’s law that the field must bend and thereby the field weakens due to these bends.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Between the two ends of a horseshoe magnet the field is uniform as shown in the diagram. As you move out to outside edges, the field bends. Show by Ampère’s law that the field must bend and thereby the field weakens due to these bends.</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"This figure shows a horse shoe magnet with the magnetic lines going from the North end to the South end.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/effd807be98dfec7ad6fae1bbe5bc033e0e7ffec\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/12-additional-problems#fs-id1166164823338",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 12, Problem 82. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/12-additional-problems#fs-id1166164823338\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
