    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Gauss’s law",
    "prompt": "A point charge of q = 5.0 × 10 −8 C is placed at the center of an uncharged spherical conducting shell of inner radius 6.0 cm and outer radius 9.0 cm. Find the electric field at (a) r =…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A point charge of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−8</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is placed at the center of an uncharged spherical conducting shell of inner radius 6.0 cm and outer radius 9.0 cm. Find the electric field at (a) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, (b) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and (c) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (d) What are the charges induced on the inner and outer surfaces of the shell?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A point charge of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>−8</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>C</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is placed at the center of an uncharged spherical conducting shell of inner radius 6.0 cm and outer radius 9.0 cm. Find the electric field at (a) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, (b) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and (c) <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>. (d) What are the charges induced on the inner and outer surfaces of the shell?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1172098757407",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 2</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 90. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1172098757407\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
