    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Drag Force and Terminal Speed",
    "prompt": "To maintain a constant speed, the force provided by a car’s engine must equal the drag force plus the force of friction of the road (the rolling resistance). (a) What are the drag forces…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>To maintain a constant speed, the force provided by a car’s engine must equal the drag force plus the force of friction of the road (the rolling resistance). (a) What are the drag forces at 70 km/h and 100 km/h for a Toyota Camry? (Drag area is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.70</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>) (b) What is the drag force at 70 km/h and 100 km/h for a Hummer H2? (Drag area is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.44</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Assume all values are accurate to three significant digits.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>To maintain a constant speed, the force provided by a car’s engine must equal the drag force plus the force of friction of the road (the rolling resistance). (a) What are the drag forces at 70 km/h and 100 km/h for a Toyota Camry? (Drag area is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.70</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>) (b) What is the drag force at 70 km/h and 100 km/h for a Hummer H2? (Drag area is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.44</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Assume all values are accurate to three significant digits.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-problems#fs-id1165039111535",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 82. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-problems#fs-id1165039111535\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
