    "number": 90,
    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Motion in two dimensions",
    "prompt": "The position of a particle is given by r → ( t ) = ( 50 m / s ) t i ^ − ( 4.9 m / s 2 ) t 2 j ^ . (a) What are the particle’s velocity and acceleration as functions of time? (b) What are…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>The position of a particle is given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>s</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>t</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>4.9</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) What are the particle’s velocity and acceleration as functions of time? (b) What are the initial conditions to produce the motion?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>The position of a particle is given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mtext>s</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>t</mi><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>4.9</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mrow><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>/</mtext><mrow><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> (a) What are the particle’s velocity and acceleration as functions of time? (b) What are the initial conditions to produce the motion?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-additional-problems#fs-id1165039248632",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 4, Problem 90. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-additional-problems#fs-id1165039248632\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
