    "topic": "Forces and motion",
    "prompt": "(a) What is the final velocity of a car originally traveling at 50.0 km/h that accelerates opposite to the motion at a rate of 0.400 m/s 2 for 50.0 s? Assume a coefficient of friction of…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>(a) What is the final velocity of a car originally traveling at 50.0 km/h that accelerates opposite to the motion at a rate of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.400</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> for 50.0 s? Assume a coefficient of friction of 1.0. (b) What is unreasonable about the result? (c) Which premise is unreasonable, or which premises are inconsistent?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>(a) What is the final velocity of a car originally traveling at 50.0 km/h that accelerates opposite to the motion at a rate of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.400</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> for 50.0 s? Assume a coefficient of friction of 1.0. (b) What is unreasonable about the result? (c) Which premise is unreasonable, or which premises are inconsistent?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1165039345130",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 90. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1165039345130\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
