    "number": 93,
    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Forces and motion",
    "prompt": "As shown below, if M = 5.50 kg, what is the tension in string 1?",
    "previewHTML": "<p>As shown below, if <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> what is the tension in string 1?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>As shown below, if <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.50</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg,</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> what is the tension in string 1?</p>\n<span>\n<img alt=\"Mass M is suspended from strings 1 and 2. String 1 connects to a wall at a point below and to the left of the mass. String 1 makes an angle of 40 degrees below the horizontal. String 2 connects to a ceiling at a point above and to the right of the mass. String 2 makes an angle of 40 degrees to the right of vertical.\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/86a15128bbd2a06be7a45fe7e705ed0472536502\"/>\n</span>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1165036006942",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-6#fs-id1165036006942-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>199 N</p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 93. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1165036006942\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
