    "topic": "Motion in two dimensions",
    "prompt": "A mountain biker encounters a jump on a race course that sends him into the air at 60 ° to the horizontal. If he lands at a horizontal distance of 45.0 m and 20 m below his launch point,…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A mountain biker encounters a jump on a race course that sends him into the air at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>60</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> to the horizontal. If he lands at a horizontal distance of 45.0 m and 20 m below his launch point, what is his initial speed?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A mountain biker encounters a jump on a race course that sends him into the air at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>60</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> to the horizontal. If he lands at a horizontal distance of 45.0 m and 20 m below his launch point, what is his initial speed?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/4-additional-problems#fs-id1165039312654",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-4#fs-id1165039312654-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>\n<span><math display=\"inline\">\n<semantics>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<msub>\n<mi>v</mi>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</msub>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>20.1</mn>\n<mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace>\n<mrow>\n<mtext>m</mtext>\n<mtext>/</mtext>\n<mtext>s</mtext>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n\n</semantics>\n</math></span>\n</p>\n</div>",
