    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Forces and motion",
    "prompt": "A half-full recycling bin has mass 3.0 kg and is pushed up a 40.0 ° incline with constant speed under the action of a 26-N force acting up and parallel to the incline. The incline has…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A half-full recycling bin has mass 3.0 kg and is pushed up a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>40.0</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> incline with constant speed under the action of a 26-N force acting up and parallel to the incline. The incline has friction. What magnitude force must act up and parallel to the incline for the bin to move down the incline at constant velocity?</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A half-full recycling bin has mass 3.0 kg and is pushed up a <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>40.0</mn><mtext>°</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> incline with constant speed under the action of a 26-N force acting up and parallel to the incline. The incline has friction. What magnitude force must act up and parallel to the incline for the bin to move down the incline at constant velocity?</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1165039109864",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-6#fs-id1165039109864-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>12 N</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 97. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1165039109864\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
