    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Forces and motion",
    "prompt": "An object with mass m moves along the x -axis. Its position at any time is given by x ( t ) = p t 3 + q t 2 where p and q are constants. Find the net force on this object for any time t .",
    "previewHTML": "<p>An object with mass <em>m</em> moves along the <em>x</em>-axis. Its position at any time is given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <em>p</em> and <em>q</em> are constants. Find the net force on this object for any time <em>t</em>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>An object with mass <em>m</em> moves along the <em>x</em>-axis. Its position at any time is given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <em>p</em> and <em>q</em> are constants. Find the net force on this object for any time <em>t</em>.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1165039027173",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-6#fs-id1165039027173-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p><em>m</em>(6<em>pt</em> + 2<em>q</em>)</p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 101. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1165039027173\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
