    "prompt": "A helicopter with mass 2.35 × 10 4 kg has a position given by r → ( t ) = ( 0.020 t 3 ) i ^ + ( 2.2 t ) j ^ − ( 0.060 t 2 ) k ^ . Find the net force on the helicopter at t = 3.0 s .",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A helicopter with mass <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.35</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> has a position given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.020</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2.2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.060</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Find the net force on the helicopter at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A helicopter with mass <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2.35</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> has a position given by <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.020</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2.2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.060</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>.</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> Find the net force on the helicopter at <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>s</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1165039335542",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 102. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1165039335542\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
