    "topic": "Forces and motion",
    "prompt": "Located at the origin, an electric car of mass m is at rest and in equilibrium. A time dependent force of F → ( t ) is applied at time t = 0 , and its components are F x ( t ) = p + n t…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>Located at the origin, an electric car of mass <em>m</em> is at rest and in equilibrium. A time dependent force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is applied at time <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and its components are <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <em>p</em>, <em>q</em>, and <em>n</em> are constants. Find the position <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and velocity <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> as functions of time <em>t</em>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>Located at the origin, an electric car of mass <em>m</em> is at rest and in equilibrium. A time dependent force of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> is applied at time <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>, and its components are <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> where <em>p</em>, <em>q</em>, and <em>n</em> are constants. Find the position <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and velocity <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> as functions of time <em>t</em>.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1165039453675",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-6#fs-id1165039453675-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p><span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo></mover></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle mathvariant=\"bold\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mstyle></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p></div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 6, Problem 103. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/6-additional-problems#fs-id1165039453675\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
