    "type": "FRQ",
    "level": 1,
    "imported": true,
    "source": "OpenStax",
    "volume": 1,
    "chapter": 13,
    "number": 16,
    "category": "problems",
    "topic": "Newton's Law of Universal Gravitation",
    "prompt": "A mountain 10.0 km from a person exerts a gravitational force on the person equal to 2.00% of their weight. (a) Calculate the mass of the mountain. (b) Compare the mountain’s mass with…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>A mountain 10.0 km from a person exerts a gravitational force on the person equal to 2.00% of their weight. (a) Calculate the mass of the mountain. (b) Compare the mountain’s mass with that of Earth. (c) What is unreasonable about these results? (d) Which premises are unreasonable or inconsistent? (Note that accurate gravitational measurements can easily detect the effect of nearby mountains and variations in local geology.)</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>A mountain 10.0 km from a person exerts a gravitational force on the person equal to 2.00% of their weight. (a) Calculate the mass of the mountain. (b) Compare the mountain’s mass with that of Earth. (c) What is unreasonable about these results? (d) Which premises are unreasonable or inconsistent? (Note that accurate gravitational measurements can easily detect the effect of nearby mountains and variations in local geology.)</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-problems#fs-id1168328170296",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 16. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-problems#fs-id1168328170296\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
