    "prompt": "(a) Calculate Earth’s mass given the acceleration due to gravity at the North Pole is measured to be 9.832 m/s 2 and the radius of the Earth at the pole is 6356 km. (b) Compare this with…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>(a) Calculate Earth’s mass given the acceleration due to gravity at the North Pole is measured to be <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>9.832</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and the radius of the Earth at the pole is 6356 km. (b) Compare this with the NASA’s Earth Fact Sheet value of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.9726</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>24</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>(a) Calculate Earth’s mass given the acceleration due to gravity at the North Pole is measured to be <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>9.832</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and the radius of the Earth at the pole is 6356 km. (b) Compare this with the NASA’s Earth Fact Sheet value of <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5.9726</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>24</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-problems#fs-id1168328323599",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 20. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-problems#fs-id1168328323599\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
