    "prompt": "(a) What is the acceleration due to gravity on the surface of the Moon? (b) On the surface of Mars? The mass of Mars is 6.418 × 10 23 kg and its radius is 3.38 × 10 6 m .",
    "previewHTML": "<p>(a) What is the acceleration due to gravity on the surface of the Moon? (b) On the surface of Mars? The mass of Mars is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.418</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>23</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and its radius is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.38</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>(a) What is the acceleration due to gravity on the surface of the Moon? (b) On the surface of Mars? The mass of Mars is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6.418</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>23</mn></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>kg</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> and its radius is <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.38</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mo>×</mo><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><mtext>m</mtext></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-problems#fs-id1168328167976",
    "solutionUrl": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/chapter-13#fs-id1168328167976-solution",
    "solutionHTML": "<div>\n<p>a. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1.62</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span>; b. <span><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3.75</mn><mspace width=\"0.2em\"></mspace><msup><mrow><mtext>m/s</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span></p>\n</div>",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 21. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-problems#fs-id1168328167976\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
