    "category": "additional-problems",
    "topic": "Gravitation and orbits",
    "prompt": "What is the orbital velocity of our solar system about the center of the Milky Way? Assume that the mass within a sphere of radius equal to our distance away from the center is about a 1…",
    "previewHTML": "<p>What is the orbital velocity of our solar system about the center of the Milky Way? Assume that the mass within a sphere of radius equal to our distance away from the center is about a 1 × 10<sup>11</sup> solar masses. Our distance from the center is 27,000 light years.</p>",
    "statementHTML": "<div>\n<p>What is the orbital velocity of our solar system about the center of the Milky Way? Assume that the mass within a sphere of radius equal to our distance away from the center is about a 1 × 10<sup>11</sup> solar masses. Our distance from the center is 27,000 light years.</p>\n</div>",
    "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-additional-problems#fs-id1168327962924",
    "attributionHTML": "OpenStax, <em>University Physics Volume 1</em>, Chapter 13, Problem 74. Authors: William Moebs, Samuel J. Ling, and Jeff Sanny. <a href=\"https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/13-additional-problems#fs-id1168327962924\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Access for free at OpenStax</a>. Content © Rice University, licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Formatting adapted for this noncommercial local study app."
